{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg6Ed814RuwJEsZFtyXZL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Qs8ikxQBSDQ6jVp5vApDH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\nRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\nNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\nADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\nconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n\n**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\ncalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\nactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\ncredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\na single-provider app.\n\n**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\nroute through, not a new auth layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n\n**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\nverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\nruns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\nso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\nCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\nif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\nto revisit.\n\n**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\nother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n\n**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\nencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\nLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\nlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\nconstant-time comparison outright.\n\n**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\nelsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n\n**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n\n**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\nand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\nMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\nRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n\n**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\nacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n\n**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\nbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\npattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\nZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\nstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\nschema, not two.\n\n**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\nUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n\n**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n\n**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\nhashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\nintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\nchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\nexisting Playwright setup.\n\n**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\ninfra to stand up.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\nspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\nof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3655,"cache_read_input_tokens":33073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3655},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c779e9d-4856-495d-b076-78ae7a06f05c","uuid":"388f1080-9c1a-4b2f-95e8-80262604f00f","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:32:09.510Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6Ed7eiwoAsxsd77GtG3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Qs8ikxQBSDQ6jVp5vApDH","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c779e9d-4856-495d-b076-78ae7a06f05c","uuid":"3010c8ba-a839-4aef-a3b8-baaaec939e1a","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:32:09.587Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\nRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\nNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\nADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\nconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n\n**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\ncalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\nactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\ncredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\na single-provider app.\n\n**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\nroute through, not a new auth layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n\n**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\nverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\nruns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\nso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\nCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\nif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\nto revisit.\n\n**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\nother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n\n**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\nencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\nLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\nlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\nconstant-time comparison outright.\n\n**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\nelsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n\n**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n\n**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\nand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\nMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\nRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n\n**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\nacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n\n**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\nbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\npattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\nZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\nstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\nschema, not two.\n\n**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\nUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n\n**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n\n**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\nhashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\nintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\nchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\nexisting Playwright setup.\n\n**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\ninfra to stand up.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\nspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\nof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":175,"newStart":1,"newLines":132,"lines":[" # Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log"," ","-Ticket: abcd-1 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete","+Ticket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete"," ","-Intake's detected stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`) is treated as a","-strong prior. All decisions below confirm or refine it against the FR/NFR","-list; none diverge from intake's detection because the PRD pins versions and","-libraries explicitly (greenfield, `--tech-stack react`, Next.js 14 fixed).","+This PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App","+Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,","+React Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).","+NFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these","+ADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus","+confirming that everything else is reused unchanged."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-1: Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TypeScript strict","+## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy"," ","-**Context:** FR-1 through FR-3, NFR-7, NFR-8 require a scaffolded app with a","-fast, scriptable dev loop (`npm install && db:migrate && db:seed && dev` in","-under 5 minutes) and clean lint/typecheck/test gates on a fresh clone.","+**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF)."," ","-**Decision:** Use Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict mode,","-ESLint (`next/core-web-vitals` + `@typescript-eslint/recommended`), Prettier,","-and a `@/*` → `src/*` path alias. No deviation from intake's detection —","-the PRD fixes these versions explicitly, there is no \"does it fit\" question","-to re-litigate.","+**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider","+calling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on","+activity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is","+credentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for","+a single-provider app."," ","-**Consequences:** App Router gives server components and route groups","-(`(app)`, `(public)`) for free, which the app-shell/public-layout split","-(FR-30, FR-36) needs anyway. Strict TS + ESLint gates are required for","-NFR-8's clean-clone CI bar.","+**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js","+(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/","+`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must","+route through, not a new auth layer."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-2: PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Docker Compose for local dev","+## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety"," ","-**Context:** FR-4 (docker-compose Postgres 16), FR-7 (Prisma schema,","-singleton `SchoolSettings`), FR-8 (cached Prisma client surviving hot","-reload), FR-9 (idempotent seed), NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up).","+**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3."," ","-**Decision:** PostgreSQL 16 in Docker Compose with a named volume;","-Prisma as the sole ORM/migration tool (`db:migrate`, `db:deploy`, `db:seed`,","-`db:reset` npm scripts map directly to Prisma CLI commands).","+**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and","+verification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still","+runs a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,","+so unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).","+Cost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —","+if real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob","+to revisit."," ","-**Consequences:** `src/server/db.ts` must cache the client on","-`globalThis` in development to avoid exhausting Postgres connections across","-hot reloads — a standard Next.js + Prisma pattern, not a new abstraction.","-Seed idempotency (FR-9) means seed logic must upsert, not create.","+**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no","+other hashing library is introduced alongside it."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-3: Zod for env validation and all request/response parsing","+## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing"," ","-**Context:** FR-6 (startup env validation with readable errors), FR-14/FR-15","-(pagination + body/query parsing in `http.ts`), FR-13 (`ZodError` →","-`VALIDATION_ERROR` mapping), NFR-6 (test coverage of `env.ts` validation).","+**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1."," ","-**Decision:** Zod is the single validation library, used both for","-`src/lib/env.ts` (process.env schema) and for all API request parsing via","-`parseBody`/`parseQuery`. No duplicate validation layer (e.g., no Joi,","-no hand-rolled checks).","+**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-","+encoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.","+Lookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto","+library is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and","+constant-time comparison outright."," ","-**Consequences:** One error-shape convention (`ZodError`) flows through the","-whole API surface, which keeps `withHandler`'s error-mapping switch (FR-13)","-to a handful of cases instead of per-route error handling.","+**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link","+(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged","+elsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-4: Centralized API helpers in `src/server/http.ts`","+## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store"," ","-**Context:** FR-10 through FR-16 define `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`,","-`withHandler`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`/`parseQuery` as one cohesive","-module; FR-16 (health check) and every future PRD's route handlers depend on","-this contract.","+**Context:** FR-6, FR-17."," ","-**Decision:** One shared `src/server/http.ts` module is the only sanctioned","-way routes build responses or parse input — no per-route reimplementation of","-pagination clamping or error mapping.","+**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)","+and forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory","+Map-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No","+Redis or other external store is introduced for this PRD."," ","-**Consequences:** Every route handler is a thin wrapper around","-`withHandler(fn)`; Prisma error codes (P2002, P2025) are mapped once, here,","-not scattered across route files. This is the reuse boundary later PRDs'","-route handlers must respect.","+**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state","+across horizontally-scaled instances.","+`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`"," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-5: Material UI v9 as the exclusive UI/styling library","+## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB"," ","-**Context:** NFR-1 mandates MUI as the only UI library and bans a long list","-of alternatives (Tailwind, Radix, Chakra, shadcn/ui, Ant Design, etc.) via","-ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (FR-19). FR-17/FR-18 pin exact MUI v9","-packages + the `react-is@18.3.1` override for React 18 compatibility.","-NFR-2 (LCP < 2.5s), NFR-3 (WCAG 2.1 AA), NFR-4 (360–1920px responsive) all","-constrain how that UI layer is built.","+**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7."," ","-**Decision:** MUI v9 (`@mui/material`, `@mui/material-nextjs`,","-`@mui/icons-material`, `@mui/x-data-grid`, `@mui/x-date-pickers`,","-`@mui/x-charts`) + Emotion for styling, `AppRouterCacheProvider` for SSR","-style injection, `cssVariables` theme mode for the light/dark toggle. No","-second styling system (no Tailwind, no CSS Modules) — intake's","-`cssPreprocessor: css` fallback reflects \"no CSS-in-JS enum option\", not an","-actual second system.","+**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the","+`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing","+`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing","+`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer."," ","-**Consequences:** All thirteen shared components (FR-20–FR-29) are MUI","-compositions, not custom-built primitives — this is a library-reuse","-decision the whole design-system layer inherits. The ESLint ban (FR-19) is","-the enforcement mechanism, not a style guideline; it fails the build.","+**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers","+(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton","+(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-6: React Hook Form for all form state","+## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI"," ","-**Context:** FR-25 requires `FormField` helpers binding React Hook Form's","-`Controller` to MUI inputs (TextField, Select, Autocomplete, Checkbox,","-Switch, RadioGroup, DatePicker/DateTimePicker).","+**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5."," ","-**Decision:** React Hook Form is the sole form-state library; Zod schemas","-(ADR-3) double as RHF resolvers via `@hookform/resolvers`, keeping one","-validation source instead of separate client/server schemas.","+**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,","+`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are","+built from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver","+pattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one","+Zod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live","+strength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one","+schema, not two."," ","-**Consequences:** No uncontrolled/ad-hoc form state in any shared component;","-every form field goes through `Controller`.","+**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced","+UI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-7: Vitest + Testing Library + Playwright + axe-core for testing","+## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack"," ","-**Context:** NFR-6 lists unit/component coverage (withHandler, parsePagination,","-formatInSchoolTz, env.ts, DataTable/ConfirmDialog/useToast, the ESLint rule)","-and Playwright e2e scenarios; NFR-3 requires `@axe-core/playwright` on `/`","-and `/dashboard` with zero serious/critical violations; NFR-8 requires both","-`test` and `test:e2e` npm scripts to pass on a fresh clone.","+**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8."," ","-**Decision:** Vitest + Testing Library for unit/component tests,","-Playwright (`tests/e2e`) + `@axe-core/playwright` for e2e and accessibility","-gating. No Jest (avoids a second test runner config) — Vitest already","-covers the Vite/Next toolchain needs with less config.","+**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token","+hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and","+integration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,","+change-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the","+existing Playwright setup."," ","-**Consequences:** Accessibility is a CI gate (zero serious/critical axe","-violations), not a manual checklist — ties directly to NFR-3's WCAG bar.","+**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection","+(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test","+infra to stand up."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-8: Structured logging via a single `src/lib/logger.ts`","-","-**Context:** FR-40 requires `logger.info|warn|error(message, meta?)`","-emitting JSON lines in production and readable lines in development.","-","-**Decision:** One logger module, no external logging library (e.g., no","-pino/winston) — the required shape (JSON-in-prod, readable-in-dev, three","-levels, optional meta) is small enough that a dependency would be","-over-engineering for what `console.*` + a format branch already covers.","-","-**Consequences:** `withHandler` (ADR-4) routes uncaught errors through this","-logger before returning `INTERNAL` to the client (FR-13), keeping stack","-traces server-side only.","-","----","-","-## ADR-9: Security headers and CSP in `next.config.js`, not middleware","-","-**Context:** NFR-5 requires `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`,","-`X-Frame-Options`, and a restrictive CSP.","-","-**Decision:** Set headers via Next.js's built-in `headers()` config","-function in `next.config.js` rather than a custom middleware — it's the","-native platform mechanism for static security headers and needs no request-","-time logic.","-","-**Consequences:** CSP must explicitly allow `'unsafe-inline'` for styles","-(Emotion/MUI inject inline `<style>` tags at runtime) while keeping","-script-src restricted to `'self'`.","-","----","-"," ## Status"," ","-All nine decisions trace to at least one FR/NFR id above. No open","-questions block `arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.","+Seven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to","+specific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse","+of abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block","+`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-1 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nIntake's detected stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`) is treated as a\nstrong prior. All decisions below confirm or refine it against the FR/NFR\nlist; none diverge from intake's detection because the PRD pins versions and\nlibraries explicitly (greenfield, `--tech-stack react`, Next.js 14 fixed).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TypeScript strict\n\n**Context:** FR-1 through FR-3, NFR-7, NFR-8 require a scaffolded app with a\nfast, scriptable dev loop (`npm install && db:migrate && db:seed && dev` in\nunder 5 minutes) and clean lint/typecheck/test gates on a fresh clone.\n\n**Decision:** Use Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict mode,\nESLint (`next/core-web-vitals` + `@typescript-eslint/recommended`), Prettier,\nand a `@/*` → `src/*` path alias. No deviation from intake's detection —\nthe PRD fixes these versions explicitly, there is no \"does it fit\" question\nto re-litigate.\n\n**Consequences:** App Router gives server components and route groups\n(`(app)`, `(public)`) for free, which the app-shell/public-layout split\n(FR-30, FR-36) needs anyway. Strict TS + ESLint gates are required for\nNFR-8's clean-clone CI bar.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Docker Compose for local dev\n\n**Context:** FR-4 (docker-compose Postgres 16), FR-7 (Prisma schema,\nsingleton `SchoolSettings`), FR-8 (cached Prisma client surviving hot\nreload), FR-9 (idempotent seed), NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up).\n\n**Decision:** PostgreSQL 16 in Docker Compose with a named volume;\nPrisma as the sole ORM/migration tool (`db:migrate`, `db:deploy`, `db:seed`,\n`db:reset` npm scripts map directly to Prisma CLI commands).\n\n**Consequences:** `src/server/db.ts` must cache the client on\n`globalThis` in development to avoid exhausting Postgres connections across\nhot reloads — a standard Next.js + Prisma pattern, not a new abstraction.\nSeed idempotency (FR-9) means seed logic must upsert, not create.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Zod for env validation and all request/response parsing\n\n**Context:** FR-6 (startup env validation with readable errors), FR-14/FR-15\n(pagination + body/query parsing in `http.ts`), FR-13 (`ZodError` →\n`VALIDATION_ERROR` mapping), NFR-6 (test coverage of `env.ts` validation).\n\n**Decision:** Zod is the single validation library, used both for\n`src/lib/env.ts` (process.env schema) and for all API request parsing via\n`parseBody`/`parseQuery`. No duplicate validation layer (e.g., no Joi,\nno hand-rolled checks).\n\n**Consequences:** One error-shape convention (`ZodError`) flows through the\nwhole API surface, which keeps `withHandler`'s error-mapping switch (FR-13)\nto a handful of cases instead of per-route error handling.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Centralized API helpers in `src/server/http.ts`\n\n**Context:** FR-10 through FR-16 define `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`,\n`withHandler`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`/`parseQuery` as one cohesive\nmodule; FR-16 (health check) and every future PRD's route handlers depend on\nthis contract.\n\n**Decision:** One shared `src/server/http.ts` module is the only sanctioned\nway routes build responses or parse input — no per-route reimplementation of\npagination clamping or error mapping.\n\n**Consequences:** Every route handler is a thin wrapper around\n`withHandler(fn)`; Prisma error codes (P2002, P2025) are mapped once, here,\nnot scattered across route files. This is the reuse boundary later PRDs'\nroute handlers must respect.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Material UI v9 as the exclusive UI/styling library\n\n**Context:** NFR-1 mandates MUI as the only UI library and bans a long list\nof alternatives (Tailwind, Radix, Chakra, shadcn/ui, Ant Design, etc.) via\nESLint `no-restricted-imports` (FR-19). FR-17/FR-18 pin exact MUI v9\npackages + the `react-is@18.3.1` override for React 18 compatibility.\nNFR-2 (LCP < 2.5s), NFR-3 (WCAG 2.1 AA), NFR-4 (360–1920px responsive) all\nconstrain how that UI layer is built.\n\n**Decision:** MUI v9 (`@mui/material`, `@mui/material-nextjs`,\n`@mui/icons-material`, `@mui/x-data-grid`, `@mui/x-date-pickers`,\n`@mui/x-charts`) + Emotion for styling, `AppRouterCacheProvider` for SSR\nstyle injection, `cssVariables` theme mode for the light/dark toggle. No\nsecond styling system (no Tailwind, no CSS Modules) — intake's\n`cssPreprocessor: css` fallback reflects \"no CSS-in-JS enum option\", not an\nactual second system.\n\n**Consequences:** All thirteen shared components (FR-20–FR-29) are MUI\ncompositions, not custom-built primitives — this is a library-reuse\ndecision the whole design-system layer inherits. The ESLint ban (FR-19) is\nthe enforcement mechanism, not a style guideline; it fails the build.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: React Hook Form for all form state\n\n**Context:** FR-25 requires `FormField` helpers binding React Hook Form's\n`Controller` to MUI inputs (TextField, Select, Autocomplete, Checkbox,\nSwitch, RadioGroup, DatePicker/DateTimePicker).\n\n**Decision:** React Hook Form is the sole form-state library; Zod schemas\n(ADR-3) double as RHF resolvers via `@hookform/resolvers`, keeping one\nvalidation source instead of separate client/server schemas.\n\n**Consequences:** No uncontrolled/ad-hoc form state in any shared component;\nevery form field goes through `Controller`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Vitest + Testing Library + Playwright + axe-core for testing\n\n**Context:** NFR-6 lists unit/component coverage (withHandler, parsePagination,\nformatInSchoolTz, env.ts, DataTable/ConfirmDialog/useToast, the ESLint rule)\nand Playwright e2e scenarios; NFR-3 requires `@axe-core/playwright` on `/`\nand `/dashboard` with zero serious/critical violations; NFR-8 requires both\n`test` and `test:e2e` npm scripts to pass on a fresh clone.\n\n**Decision:** Vitest + Testing Library for unit/component tests,\nPlaywright (`tests/e2e`) + `@axe-core/playwright` for e2e and accessibility\ngating. No Jest (avoids a second test runner config) — Vitest already\ncovers the Vite/Next toolchain needs with less config.\n\n**Consequences:** Accessibility is a CI gate (zero serious/critical axe\nviolations), not a manual checklist — ties directly to NFR-3's WCAG bar.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Structured logging via a single `src/lib/logger.ts`\n\n**Context:** FR-40 requires `logger.info|warn|error(message, meta?)`\nemitting JSON lines in production and readable lines in development.\n\n**Decision:** One logger module, no external logging library (e.g., no\npino/winston) — the required shape (JSON-in-prod, readable-in-dev, three\nlevels, optional meta) is small enough that a dependency would be\nover-engineering for what `console.*` + a format branch already covers.\n\n**Consequences:** `withHandler` (ADR-4) routes uncaught errors through this\nlogger before returning `INTERNAL` to the client (FR-13), keeping stack\ntraces server-side only.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Security headers and CSP in `next.config.js`, not middleware\n\n**Context:** NFR-5 requires `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`,\n`X-Frame-Options`, and a restrictive CSP.\n\n**Decision:** Set headers via Next.js's built-in `headers()` config\nfunction in `next.config.js` rather than a custom middleware — it's the\nnative platform mechanism for static security headers and needs no request-\ntime logic.\n\n**Consequences:** CSP must explicitly allow `'unsafe-inline'` for styles\n(Emotion/MUI inject inline `<style>` tags at runtime) while keeping\nscript-src restricted to `'self'`.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nAll nine decisions trace to at least one FR/NFR id above. No open\nquestions block `arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n","userModified":false}}
