{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBL7ib4kiB1PCfb7zC4y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DtpGciWGePGxkmDHAWx2u1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n\nBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\nfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\nand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\nevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\nreal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\nreports no blockers.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n\n- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n  passing with no scope creep.\n- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n\n## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n\n- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n  browser before anything hits the network.\n\n## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n\n- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n  table.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n  request lifetime).\n\n## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n\n- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n\n## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n\n- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n  wrapper design-system package.\n- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n\n## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n\n- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n  queries unaffected.\n\n## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n\n- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n\n## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n\n- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n  user service.\n- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n  re-implements.\n\n## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n\n- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n  not generated at request time.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n  edit, not a code change.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":35298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1350},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988faf09-d4cc-4ec3-a738-cbf6e1942ce7","uuid":"3b0e0fcd-57c4-43f8-aff7-e4f258dae4a7","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:07:25.648Z","request_id":"req_011CgBL7iMRxTMp46Jn7qbnW"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DtpGciWGePGxkmDHAWx2u1","type":"tool_result","content":"The file artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"988faf09-d4cc-4ec3-a738-cbf6e1942ce7","uuid":"b7c56a74-3227-4638-90ba-c9c6515570c3","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:07:25.742Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n\nBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\nfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\nand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\nevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\nreal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\nreports no blockers.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n\n- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n  passing with no scope creep.\n- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n\n## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n\n- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n  browser before anything hits the network.\n\n## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n\n- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n  table.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n  request lifetime).\n\n## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n\n- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n\n## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n\n- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n  wrapper design-system package.\n- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n\n## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n\n- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n  queries unaffected.\n\n## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n\n- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n\n## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n\n- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n  user service.\n- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n  re-implements.\n\n## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n\n- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n  not generated at request time.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n  edit, not a code change.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":132,"newStart":1,"newLines":121,"lines":[" # Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log"," ","-Ticket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete","+Ticket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete"," ","-This PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App","-Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,","-React Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).","-NFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these","-ADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus","-confirming that everything else is reused unchanged.","+Brownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per","+`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already","+fixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)","+and MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,","+React Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework","+evaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of","+real choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`","+reports no blockers."," ","----","+## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework"," ","-## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy","+- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing","+  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating","+  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep","+  passing with no scope creep.","+- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,","+  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.","+- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match","+  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a","+  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library."," ","-**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).","+## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON"," ","-**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider","-calling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on","-activity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is","-credentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for","-a single-provider app.","+- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview","+  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to","+  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.","+- **Decision:** No server-side