*Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of","+  per-export escaping logic that could drift."," ","-**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and","-verification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still","-runs a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,","-so unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).","-Cost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —","-if real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob","-to revisit.","+## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule"," ","-**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no","-other hashing library is introduced alongside it.","+- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from","+  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP","+  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,","+  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.","+- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if","+  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI","+  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import","+  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no","+  wrapper design-system package.","+- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps."," ","----","+## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index"," ","-## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing","+- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,","+  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from","+  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.","+- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing","+  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,","+  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).","+- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02","+  queries unaffected."," ","-**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.","+## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation"," ","-**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-","-encoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.","-Lookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto","-library is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and","-constant-time comparison outright.","+- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation","+  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the","+  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).","+- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),","+  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the","+  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side","+  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.","+- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies","+  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly."," ","-**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link","-(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged","-elsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.","+## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing"," ","----","+- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working","+  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST","+  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`","+  fields PRD-01 already defined.","+- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips","+  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading","+  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the","+  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing","+  user service.","+- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);","+  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an","+  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD","+  re-implements."," ","-## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store","+## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated"," ","-**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.","-","-**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)","-and forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory","-Map-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No","-Redis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.","-","-**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state","-across horizontally-scaled instances.","-`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`","-","----","-","-## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB","-","-**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.","-","-**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the","-`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing","-`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing","-`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.","-","-**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers","-(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton","-(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.","-","----","-","-## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI","-","-**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.","-","-**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,","-`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are","-built from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver","-pattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one","-Zod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live","-strength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one","-schema, not two.","-","-**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced","-UI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.","-","----","-","-## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack","-","-**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.","-","-**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token","-hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and","-integration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,","-change-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the","-existing Playwright setup.","-","-**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection","-(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test","-infra to stand up.","-","----","-","-## Status","-","-Seven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to","-specific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse","-of abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block","-`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.","+- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /","+  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.","+- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),","+  not generated at request time.","+- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file","+  edit, not a code change."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\nRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\nNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\nADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\nconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n\n**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\ncalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\nactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\ncredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\na single-provider app.\n\n**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\nroute through, not a new auth layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n\n**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\nverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\nruns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\nso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\nCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\nif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\nto revisit.\n\n**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\nother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n\n**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\nencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\nLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\nlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\nconstant-time comparison outright.\n\n**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\nelsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n\n**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n\n**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\nand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\nMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\nRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n\n**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\nacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n\n**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\nbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\npattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\nZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\nstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\nschema, not two.\n\n**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\nUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n\n**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n\n**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\nhashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\nintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\nchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\nexisting Playwright setup.\n\n**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\ninfra to stand up.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\nspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\nof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n","userModified":false}}
