xt:** FR-10/NFR-4 require concurrency-safe batch claiming (no email\n  sent twice by two dispatchers) without a message broker — Prisma's query\n  builder has no `SKIP LOCKED` support, and NFR-10 rules out adding\n  infrastructure (Redis/BullMQ/SQS) for a feature capped at polling-scale\n  volume.\n- **Decision:** `dispatchEmails()` uses one `prisma.$transaction` containing\n  a `$queryRaw` `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim a batch of\n  PENDING rows (flip to SENDING), then sends each via Nodemailer outside the\n  lock, then updates status (SENT, or retry backoff per FR-11, or FAILED\n  after attempt 5). A second periodic query recovers rows stuck in SENDING\n  for >10 minutes back to PENDING (NFR-4).\n- **Consequences:** No new infra; the only raw SQL in the codebase is this\n  one claim query, isolated behind `dispatchEmails()` — every other read/\n  write stays on the Prisma client API.\n\n## ADR-5: Two thin drivers over one dispatch function — HTTP route + loop script, no scheduler\n\n- **Context:** FR-12 needs both an externally-cron-triggered HTTP endpoint\n  (`POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`, bearer-guarded by `CRON_SECRET`,\n  NFR-8) and a `npm run worker:email` script that loops every 15s for local/\n  simple deployments.\n- **Decision:** Both are thin callers of the same `dispatchEmails()` (ADR-4).\n  The loop script is a plain `setInterval`-driven Node script\n  (`scripts/worker-email.ts` run via `tsx`, matching the existing\n  `db:seed` pattern) — no cron library, no job-scheduler dependency.\n- **Consequences:** One dispatch implementation, two callers; adding a real\n  scheduler later (if deployment target changes) only touches the driver,\n  not `dispatchEmails()`.\n\n## ADR-6: Bell + preferences UI stays polling, built from existing MUI/MUI X — no new UI deps\n\n- **Context:** FR-14 (unread-count bell poll every 30s, paused on\n  `visibilitychange`), FR-15 (Popover + List), FR-16 (/notifications list +\n  filters), FR-18 (preferences table with per-row Switches) are all additive\n  screens; NFR-1 mandates MUI-only, and NFR-10 explicitly rules out\n  websockets.\n- **Decision:** Plain `fetch` + `setInterval`/`document.visibilityState` for\n  polling (no SWR/React Query/socket library added). All visible elements\n  come from already-installed `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`\n  (Badge, IconButton, Popover, List, Table, Switch, Tabs) — same ESLint\n  `no-restricted-imports` MUI-only gate as prior PRDs enforces this.\n- **Consequences:** Zero new frontend dependencies; one shared polling hook\n  (e.g. `useUnreadCount`) can back both the bell and, if ever needed, the\n  list page — no premature abstraction beyond that single reuse point.\n\n## ADR-7: Notification type registry is a plain TS const + literal union, not a DB table\n\n- **Context:** FR-2/FR-3 need a typed registry (key → label/description/\n  category/defaults/roles) where `notify()` rejects unknown type keys **at\n  compile time**.\n- **Decision:** `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a `const` object in\n  `src/server/notifications/types.ts`; its key union\n  (`keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`) is the type parameter `notify()`\n  accepts. No database-backed type table, no runtime registry lookup for\n  validity — compile-time exhaustiveness is free and stronger than a runtime\n  check.\n- **Consequences:** Adding a notification type is a code change + PR review\n  (desired: it drives UI copy and default routing), not a migration or admin\n  screen.\n\n## ADR-8: purgeOldNotifications scheduling stays in-memory, no job table\n\n- **Context:** FR-17 needs a daily purge of notifications >180 days old;\n  explicitly \"acceptable to re-run after a restart.\"\n- **Decision:** Track last-run time in a module-level variable inside the\n  dispatch route handler (checked on each `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\n  call, which already fires every 15s–few minutes via the cron/worker); no\n  `CronJob`/`LastRun` table, no separate scheduler.\n- **Consequences:** Matches the stated tolerance for restart-driven re-runs;\n  avoids a persistence concept this PRD doesn't otherwise need.\n\n## ADR-9: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by the existing ESLint rule (carried over)\n\n- **Context:** NFR-1 requires every visible element to come from\n  `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X, with banned libraries blocked\n  by `no-restricted-imports`; email templates are the sole, explicit\n  exception (ADR-3).\n- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is for all app UI; the\n  exception glob only needs to cover `src/server/email/templates/**` so\n  `@react-email/components` imports aren't flagged there.\n- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..03; the one new\n  dependency surface (react-email) is scoped and fenced by lint, not by\n  convention alone.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":121,"newStart":1,"newLines":141,"lines":[" # Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log"," ","-Ticket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete","+Ticket: abcd-04 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete"," ","-Brownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per","-`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already","-fixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)","-and MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,","-React Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework","-evaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of","-real choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`","-reports no blockers.","+Brownfield PRD-04 (Notifications & Email) on top of PRD-00..03. Per","+`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the base stack is fixed:","+Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion) and","+MUI X, Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL, Zod, React Hook Form, Vitest/Testing","+Library/Playwright. `handoff-to-architect.json` reports 97% confidence and no","+blockers. This PRD's only real stack question is the email layer (FR-7..13);","+everything else slots into the existing app. NFR-10 explicitly caps scope","+(no SMS/push/websockets/digests), which rules out several heavier options","+below."," "," ## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework"," ","-- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing","-  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating","-  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep","-  passing with no scope creep.","+- **Context:** FR-1..FR-24 are additive feature work inside an existing","+  brownfield app; NFR-10 forbids scope expansion (no SMS/push, no realtime","+  websockets, no digest emails)."," - **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,","   Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.","-- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match","-  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a","-  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.","+- **Consequences:** Zero migration cost; new code must match existing `src/`","+  conventions (response envelopes, `requireUser`/`requireRole` from PRD-00/01)."," ","-## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON","+## ADR-2: Nodemailer as the one SMTP client, promoted to a direct dependency"," ","-- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview","-  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to","-  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.","-- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route","-  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and","-  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.","-- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to","-  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the","-  browser before anything hits the network.","+- **Context:** FR-10/FR-13 need an SMTP sender with env-driven config","+  (`SMTP_HOST`/`PORT`/`USER`/`PASS`/`SECURE`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT=smtp|console`).","+  `nodemailer` is already present in `package-lock.json` only as a transitive","+  dependency of `next-auth`'s email provider plumbing — it is not a direct","+  dependency and must not be assumed available at a pinned version.","+- **Decision:** Add `nodemailer` (+ `@types/nodemailer`) as a direct","+  dependency. One transport module (`src/server/email/transport.ts`) builds","+  either a real SMTP transport or a `console` transport (logs subject,","+  recipient, text body) based on `EMAIL_TRANSPORT`, defaulting to `console`","+  in development per FR-13.","+- **Consequences:** No ambiguity about which nodemailer version ships; no","+  second mail library introduced for the console/dev path."," ","-## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue","+## ADR-3: @react-email/components + @react-email/render for templates"," ","-- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or","-  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).","-- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the","-  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job","-  table.","-- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;","-  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows","-  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single","-  request lifetime).","+- **Context:** FR-7/FR-8 require branded templates (shared base layout,","+  invite/password-reset/generic) rendered to **both** HTML and plain text,","+  built with `@react-email/components` per NFR-1 (email templates are the","+  one UI surface explicitly exempted from the MUI-only rule, since MUI isn't","+  email-client-safe markup).","+- **Decision:** Add `@react-email/components` and `@react-email/render` as","+  direct dependencies. Each template is a React component under","+  `src/server/email/templates/`, sharing one `BaseLayout` component (logo,","+  content slot, footer with address + disclosure + preferences link). Render","+  call sites use `render(<Template .../>)` for HTML and","+  `render(<Template .../>, { plainText: true })` for the text part — no","+  separate hand-written text templates, so the two parts can't drift.","+- **Consequences:** One rendering path backs both EmailOutbox columns","+  (`html`, `text`); template changes automatically stay HTML/text consistent."," ","-## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library","+## ADR-4: EmailOutbox dispatch via raw `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, no queue library"," ","-- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,","-  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export","-  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also","-  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.","-- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared","-  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer","-  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.","-- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of","-  per-export escaping logic that could drift.","+- **Context:** FR-10/NFR-4 require concurrency-safe batch claiming (no email","+  sent twice by two dispatchers) without a message broker — Prisma's query","+  builder has no `SKIP LOCKED` support, and NFR-10 rules out adding","+  infrastructure (Redis/BullMQ/SQS) for a feature capped at polling-scale","+  volume.","+- **Decision:** `dispatchEmails()` uses one `prisma.$transaction` containing","+  a `$queryRaw` `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim a batch of","+  PENDING rows (flip to SENDING), then sends each via Nodemailer outside the","+  lock, then updates status (SENT, or retry backoff per FR-11, or FAILED","+  after attempt 5). A second periodic query recovers rows stuck in SENDING","+  for >10 minutes back to PENDING (NFR-4).","+- **Consequences:** No new infra; the only raw SQL in the codebase is this","+  one claim query, isolated behind `dispatchEmails()` — every other read/","+  write stays on the Prisma client API."," ","-## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule","+## ADR-5: Two thin drivers over one dispatch function — HTTP route + loop script, no scheduler"," ","-- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from","-  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP","-  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,","-  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.","-- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if","-  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI","-  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import","-  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no","-  wrapper design-system package.","-- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.","+- **Context:** FR-12 needs both an externally-cron-triggered HTTP endpoint","+  (`POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`, bearer-guarded by `CRON_SECRET`,","+  NFR-8) and a `npm run worker:email` script that loops every 15s for local/","+  simple deployments.","+- **Decision:** Both are thin callers of the same `dispatchEmails()` (ADR-4).","+  The loop script is a plain `setInterval`-driven Node script","+  (`scripts/worker-email.ts` run via `tsx`, matching the existing","+  `db:seed` pattern) — no cron library, no job-scheduler dependency.","+- **Consequences:** One dispatch implementation, two callers; adding a real","+  scheduler later (if deployment target changes) only touches the driver,","+  not `dispatchEmails()`."," ","-## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index","+## ADR-6: Bell + preferences UI stays polling, built from existing MUI/MUI X — no new UI deps"," ","-- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,","-  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from","-  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.","-- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing","-  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,","-  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).","-- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02","-  queries unaffected.","+- **Context:** FR-14 (unread-count bell poll every 30s, paused on","+  `visibilitychange`), FR-15 (Popover + List), FR-16 (/notifications list +","+  filters), FR-18 (preferences table with per-row Switches) are all additive","+  screens; NFR-1 mandates MUI-only, and NFR-10 explicitly rules out","+  websockets.","+- **Decision:** Plain `fetch` + `setInterval`/`document.visibilityState` for","+  polling (no SWR/React Query/socket library added). All visible elements","+  come from already-installed `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`","+  (Badge, IconButton, Popover, List, Table, Switch, Tabs) — same ESLint","+  `no-restricted-imports` MUI-only gate as prior PRDs enforces this.","+- **Consequences:** Zero new frontend dependencies; one shared polling hook","+  (e.g. `useUnreadCount`) can back both the bell and, if ever needed, the","+  list page — no premature abstraction beyond that single reuse point."," ","-## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation","+## ADR-7: Notification type registry is a plain TS const + literal union, not a DB table"," ","-- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation","-  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the","-  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).","-- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),","-  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the","-  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side","-  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.","-- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies","-  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.","+- **Context:** FR-2/FR-3 need a typed registry (key → label/description/","+  category/defaults/roles) where `notify()` rejects unknown type keys **at","+  compile time**.","+- **Decision:** `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a `const` object in","+  `src/server/notifications/types.ts`; its key union","+  (`keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`) is the type parameter `notify()`","+  accepts. No database-backed type table, no runtime registry lookup for","+  validity — compile-time exhaustiveness is free and stronger than a runtime","+  check.","+- **Consequences:** Adding a notification type is a code change + PR review","+  (desired: it drives UI copy and default routing), not a migration or admin","+  screen."," ","-## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing","+## ADR-8: purgeOldNotifications scheduling stays in-memory, no job table"," ","-- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working","-  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST","-  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`","-  fields PRD-01 already defined.","-- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips","-  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading","-  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the","-  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing","-  user service.","-- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);","-  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an","-  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD","-  re-implements.","+- **Context:** FR-17 needs a daily purge of notifications >180 days old;","+  explicitly \"acceptable to re-run after a restart.\"","+- **Decision:** Track last-run time in a module-level variable inside the","+  dispatch route handler (checked on each `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`","+  call, which already fires every 15s–few minutes via the cron/worker); no","+  `CronJob`/`LastRun` table, no separate scheduler.","+- **Consequences:** Matches the stated tolerance for restart-driven re-runs;","+  avoids a persistence concept this PRD doesn't otherwise need."," ","-## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated","+## ADR-9: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by the existing ESLint rule (carried over)"," ","-- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /","-  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.","-- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),","-  not generated at request time.","-- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file","-  edit, not a code change.","+- **Context:** NFR-1 requires every visible element to come from","+  `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X, with banned libraries blocked","+  by `no-restricted-imports`; email templates are the sole, explicit","+  exception (ADR-3).","+- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is for all app UI; the","+  exception glob only needs to cover `src/server/email/templates/**` so","+  `@react-email/components` imports aren't flagged there.","+- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..03; the one new","+  dependency surface (react-email) is scoped and fenced by lint, not by","+  convention alone."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n\nBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\nfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\nand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\nevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\nreal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\nreports no blockers.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n\n- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n  passing with no scope creep.\n- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n\n## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n\n- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n  browser before anything hits the network.\n\n## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n\n- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n  table.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n  request lifetime).\n\n## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n\n- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n\n## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n\n- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n  wrapper design-system package.\n- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n\n## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n\n- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n  queries unaffected.\n\n## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n\n- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n\n## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n\n- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n  user service.\n- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n  re-implements.\n\n## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n\n- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n  not generated at request time.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n  edit, not a code change.\n","userModified":false}}
