{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XFUwTuP4KMuyVtd2aocR76","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-04 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tBase platform (from `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%):\n6\tNext.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\n7\tMUI v9 + emotion. This PRD is brownfield on top of that stack — the\n8\tdecisions below are only the deltas this PRD's requirements force, not a\n9\tre-litigation of the base stack.\n10\t\n11\t## ADR-1: Email rendering — `@react-email/components` (new dependency)\n12\t\n13\t**Context.** FR-7/FR-8 require branded HTML+plain-text email templates\n14\t(invite, password-reset, generic) sharing a base layout. The codebase has\n15\tno email-rendering layer today (`sendInvite()` in\n16\t`src/server/services/users.ts` is a logging-only stub per FR-9). NFR-1\n17\tscopes MUI to *visible app UI*; it explicitly exempts email templates\n18\tbecause MUI's `sx`/emotion runtime CSS does not survive email-client HTML\n19\tsanitizers (no `<style>` tag support, inconsistent CSS-in-JS rendering in\n20\tOutlook/Gmail clients)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e898cb16-9a36-455e-8838-11a321209b69","uuid":"83d4d3f4-b633-406a-9895-c9f5671add2f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:28:45.342Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email\n\nTicket: abcd-04 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Status: complete\n\nBase platform (from `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%):\nNext.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nMUI v9 + emotion. This PRD is brownfield on top of that stack — the\ndecisions below are only the deltas this PRD's requirements force, not a\nre-litigation of the base stack.\n\n## ADR-1: Email rendering — `@react-email/components` (new dependency)\n\n**Context.** FR-7/FR-8 require branded HTML+plain-text email templates\n(invite, password-reset, generic) sharing a base layout. The codebase has\nno email-rendering layer today (`sendInvite()` in\n`src/server/services/users.ts` is a logging-only stub per FR-9). NFR-1\nscopes MUI to *visible app UI*; it explicitly exempts email templates\nbecause MUI's `sx`/emotion runtime CSS does not survive email-client HTML\nsanitizers (no `<style>` tag support, inconsistent CSS-in-JS rendering in\nOutlook/Gmail clients).","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":167}}}
