iption\": \"Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (optional, required when kind=CORE), teacher, up to 3 co-teachers, name, code (auto-filled from subject+section, editable, forced uppercase), kind, capacity, description.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses/[id]/enrollment: enrolled-students table with drop/reactivate row actions and an 'Add students' picker; for CORE courses show an info note that membership is managed via the section instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /courses/[courseId] header: subject colour band, course name, code, teacher(s) (including co-teachers), section, room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a course-tabs registry at src/config/course-tabs.ts (same shape as the existing src/config/student-tabs.ts, with a `roles` field) rendered as a scrollable MUI Tabs on the course home page; this PRD registers 'Overview' (description/teachers/counts, all roles that can view the course) and 'Roster' (TEACHER/ADMIN: full student list with avatar/name/admission number/link to student page/status; STUDENT: classmates' names only; PARENT: tab not shown).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; verified against the existing (empty) src/config/student-tabs.ts pattern this PRD is told to mirror\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add src/server/auth/course-access.ts exporting assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN: all; TEACHER: teacher or co-teacher; STUDENT: has an ACTIVE enrollment; PARENT: any linked child has an ACTIVE enrollment) and assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN, teacher, co-teacher) for later write operations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Build /my-courses: TEACHER sees MUI Cards in a responsive Grid for each non-archived course they teach/co-teach this year (name, section, enrolled count); STUDENT sees cards for their ACTIVE enrollments (name, teacher); PARENT sees the same cards grouped by child.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sidebar nav entries: 'My courses' for TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT, and 'Sections'/'Courses' grouped under an 'Administration' section for ADMIN. NavItem currently has no grouping field — src/config/navigation.ts (verified) is a flat array with only Dashboard/Notifications/Email log entries and no 'group' concept, and no admin-facing pages exist yet for the PRD-02/PRD-03 entities (academic years, subjects, rooms, grade levels, users) that would also belong in such a group. The Architect must decide whether to add a lightweight `group` field to NavItem now or ship Sections/Courses as flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav grouping PRD lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; cross-checked against the current flat src/config/navigation.ts and the absence of an 'Administration' grouping or admin pages anywhere under src/app/(app)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Register student tab 'Courses' in src/config/student-tabs.ts (visible to every role that can view the student): a table of the student's courses this year with teacher and enrollment status, plus their section and homeroom teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing getAccessibleStudentIds(user) in src/server/auth/student-access.ts so a TEACHER additionally gets students with ACTIVE enrollments in courses they teach or co-teach, plus members of the section they are homeroom teacher of.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1; verified getAccessibleStudentIds already exists and is exported from src/server/auth/student-access.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Expose the full REST surface from the API table: sections CRUD + members + move-section + core-courses + copy-to-year; courses CRUD + roster + enrollments + enrollment status PATCH; GET /api/me/courses — each with the role gating shown in the table and the existing success/list/error response envelope and pagination/sort/search query conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Every write (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*) records an AuditLog row via the existing audit() helper.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table footnote 'All writes audit (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*)'; verified audit() already exists and is exported from src/server/audit.ts\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element in the section/course/enrollment screens is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the MUI X packages (DataGrid via the existing shared DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, Snackbar+Alert via useToast()); every component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select, etc.) in this PRD's code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD); Compliance Rule 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Integrity: the one-section-per-student-per-year rule is enforced by the database unique constraint (@@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember), not only in application code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: adding 30 students to a section with 8 core courses (240 resulting enrollments) completes in under 1 second.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Privacy: on the course Roster tab and GET /api/courses/:id/roster, students see classmates' names only — no emails, admission numbers or profile links in the response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3; Acceptance Criteria #7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Scope containment: no timetable slots (PRD-06), no course content (PRD-08), no prerequisite or course-request workflows, and no automatic year-to-year student promotion — only the manual 'Copy sections to next year' shortcut.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization gap carried forward from PRD-01/PRD-04: the Platform Context describes src/server/auth/permissions.ts exposing requireUser()/requireRole(...roles), but only src/server/auth/requireRole.ts and student-access.ts exist today (no permissions.ts, no requireUser()). New route handlers in this PRD must use the existing requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)-style stand-in (as PRD-04's handoff also flagged) rather than invent a new auth helper, until PRD-01 lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement), cross-checked against the current contents of src/server/auth/ (only requireRole.ts and student-access.ts present)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
