le()` / `requireUser()` become async; update all 50 call sites with `await`\n\n**Context.** FR-28 and FR-29 replace `PLACEHOLDER_USER` with the real session.\nAuth.js `auth()` is async. Intake flagged this as a blocker. Options:\n(a) make the helpers async and add `await` at each call site;\n(b) keep them sync by reading identity from headers set by middleware;\n(c) use React `cache()` plus a sync wrapper.\n\n**Decision.** (a). `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole(...roles)`\nbecome `async` with the same arguments and the same `{id, role, ...}` return\nshape, so the signature stays compatible (FR-29). Each of the 50 call sites\nchanges from `requireRole(...)` to `await requireRole(...)`. That's a\nmechanical one-token edit, and every caller is already async. Wrap\n`getCurrentUser` in React `cache()` so a page plus its layout share one\nsession decode per request.\n\nOption (b) was rejected: identity read from headers is a spoofing risk\n(NFR-7), and it skips the FR-11 revocation check. Option (c) can't make an\nasync read sync.\n\n**Consequences.** `tsc` catches every missed `await`, because a `Promise` has\nno `.role` or `.id`. Bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statements don't fail\ntypecheck, though, and a forgotten `await` there silently does nothing.\nEnable `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises` for `src/**`, or have\ndev-planning grep for un-awaited calls. Redirect-vs-throw: in server pages,\nuse `redirect('/login')` / `redirect('/forbidden')` from `next/navigation`;\nin route handlers, throw `AppError` (UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN), which\n`withHandler` already maps. Implement this as one helper that the page and\nAPI paths both call, not two copies. `course-access.ts` and\n`student-access.ts` keep taking the resolved user object and aren't modified\n(NFR-9).\n\n_Cites: FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9_\n\n## ADR-3: Password hashing with the existing `bcrypt` at cost 12, plus a dummy compare for unknown users\n\n**Context.** FR-4 sets cost 12.