{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRYfm45mFb3fd6GpqvJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for ticket abcd-1 as 10 decision records. None of them adds a new dependency: next-auth v5 beta and bcrypt are already installed. Every requirement id cited exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**Before the next sub-tasks run:** the other files already in `artifacts/architect/` (`system-design.md`, `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, `requirements-analysis-notes.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are left over from an earlier run on ticket abcd-05. I didn't touch them because they belong to other sub-tasks. Their owners need to overwrite them. If they don't, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` already exists and could wrongly signal that the architect phase is finished.\n\nThe decisions that settle intake's blockers:\n- **Sync vs async `requireRole()` (FR-28/29):** it becomes async and keeps the same arguments and return shape. Intake estimated about 94 call sites; the actual count is 50 call sites in 43 files, all already inside async functions, so each needs only an added `await`.\n  - Typecheck catches a missing `await` wherever the result is used.\n  - It won't catch a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` with no `await`, which would silently skip the check. I recommended turning on the lint rule that flags these (`no-floating-promises`).\n- **Auth setup:** the config is split in two because Next 14 middleware runs on the Edge runtime, where bcrypt and Prisma can't load. Middleware only reads the session token. The check that a password change has logged out other sessions (FR-11) runs on the server, at most every 5 minutes.\n- **Schema (FR-1):** one migration that only adds things. The `ip` column and the extra `ARCHIVED` status stay, and only the two missing audit-log indexes plus any missing User fields are added.\n- **Rate limiter:** in-memory as the PRD asks, which means limits reset on restart and aren't shared across server instances. That's marked with a `ponytail:` comment so the limitation is tracked.\n- **MUI docs server (NFR-6):** it was reachable from this session, so that blocker doesn't hold at this stage. Dev still has to check it again.\n\nI also recommended pinning the next-auth beta to an exact version, so an update can't change its callback signatures partway through this PRD."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5332,"cache_read_input_tokens":42435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5332},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d28ca65-c0bb-4a8d-a303-0fc23bd16a10","uuid":"0e0d1374-5763-4c2e-b577-b412aa77de37","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:35:41.821Z","request_id":"req_011CghRYfWAaVieR66YPPJSy"}
