{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTNuTX6LFQfPwEHXWiA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RwB3yngx9GbhXnpwL3BAm7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\n\nTicket: SH-4 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:10:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports confidence 100%, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3, TypeScript 5.5 strict,\nPrisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI 9.5 (material, icons, x-data-grid) + emotion,\nzod 3.23, date-fns 3.6 / date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1 and Playwright 1.47.\n**This PRD adds no new runtime or dev dependency.** Everything it needs is\nalready installed: `nodemailer ^6.9.14` + `@types/nodemailer`,\n`@react-email/components 0.0.25`, `@react-email/render 1.0.1` and `tsx 4.16`.\nThe intake stack fits every FR/NFR, so the ADRs below record only the\nimplementation choices the requirements force.\n\n**Brownfield facts checked in the workspace.** These confirm or sharpen intake:\n- `prisma/schema.prisma` declares `EmailStatus`, `Notification` (with\n  `@@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])`), `NotificationPreference` (composite\n  `@@id([userId, type])`) and `EmailOutbox` (with `@@index([status, nextAttemptAt])`, no FK\n  to User, and `updatedAt` documented as the SENDING timestamp). The 4 existing\n  migrations don't create these tables.\n- `@react-email/render@1.0.1`'s `render(el, { plainText?: true })` returns a\n  **`Promise<string>`**. It's async in 1.x, so every render call must be awaited.\n- `src/lib/env.ts` already validates `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp|console`, default\n  `console`), `SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, an optional `CRON_SECRET` and `APP_URL`.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`,\n  `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError`. `src/lib/logger.ts`\n  provides `logger`. `src/lib/dates.ts` provides `formatInSchoolTz`. `src/server/db.ts`\n  exports the `prisma` singleton.\n- The existing `src/components/DataTable` wraps MUI X DataGrid with\n  URL-driven server pagination. `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts` exists.\n- Vitest `include` is `tests/unit/**` only, with `environment: 'jsdom'`.\n  There's no integration test folder yet.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: One additive Prisma migration for the existing PRD-04 models\n\n**Context.** FR-1 requires the tables. The models are already in\n`schema.prisma` but no migration creates them (an intake blocker). NFR-13\nsays never rename and never re-scaffold. NFR-5 relies on `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`.\n\n**Decision.** Run `prisma migrate dev --name notifications_email` without\ntouching the schema. It generates the `EmailStatus` enum, the 3 tables, their\nindexes and the `Notification`/`NotificationPreference` → `User` cascade FKs.\nKeep the additive `updatedAt` columns exactly as they are declared.\n\n**Consequences.** This is one purely additive migration with nothing destructive. Prisma's\n`@updatedAt` sets the column on every update made through the Prisma client, **but not\non `$executeRaw`/`$queryRaw` writes**. Any raw SQL that sets `status = 'SENDING'`\nmust also set `\"updatedAt\" = now()` itself (see ADR-3).\n\n_Cites: FR-1, NFR-5, NFR-13_\n\n## ADR-2: Registry as a `const` object with `satisfies`; `keyof typeof` drives notify()\n\n**Context.** FR-2 through FR-5 need a typed registry that rejects unknown\nkeys at compile time and that later PRDs can extend.\n\n**Decision.** In `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, define\n`export const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = { ... } as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`\nand `export type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Express\ncategories (FR-3) as a string-literal union, `NotificationCategory`, plus a\n`NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` tuple that the preferences page and its zod enum use.\n`NotificationTypeDef` adds `emailOnly?: true` / `hidden?: true` for the\n`account.*` types (FR-4, FR-28). Later PRDs extend the registry by adding\nkeys to this one object. Don't build a runtime registration API (YAGNI).\n\n**Consequences.** `NotificationPreference.type` and `Notification.type` stay\nplain `String` columns, because the DB doesn't need an enum for a list that\ngrows with every PRD. The zod validator for the preferences PUT (FR-38,\nFR-41) builds `z.enum(Object.keys(NOTIFICATION_TYPES) as [NotificationType, ...])`.\nIt can't import server-only modules, so `types.ts` must stay free of server\nimports (no `prisma`, no `env`) to remain importable from\n`src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`.\n\n_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-28, FR-38, FR-41_\n\n## ADR-3: Dispatcher claim through one raw-SQL `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 and NFR-4 require that concurrent dispatchers never send a row\ntwice. NFR-5 requires recovering rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes. Prisma 5.20\nhas no `SKIP LOCKED` in its query API.\n\n**Decision.** Each `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` run:\n1. **Recover.** Run `prisma.emailOutbox.updateMany({ where: { status: 'SENDING', updatedAt: { lt: now - 10min } }, data: { status: 'PENDING' } })`.\n2. **Claim.** Use a single statement through `prisma.$queryRaw`:\n   ```sql\n   UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status = 'SENDING', \"updatedAt\" = now()\n   WHERE id IN (\n     SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\"\n     WHERE status = 'PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now()\n     ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize}\n     FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n   RETURNING *;\n   ```\n   It runs as one autocommit statement, so the row lock is held only for the flip and is released\n   before any SMTP call. This avoids long transactions, and once a row is\n   SENDING no other dispatcher's `WHERE status='PENDING'` can match it.\n3. **Send each row**, then mark it SENT (`sentAt`) or reschedule it through Prisma `update` (ADR-4).\n\n**Consequences.** This is the only raw SQL in the PRD. Use tagged-template `$queryRaw`, never\n`$queryRawUnsafe`. Cast the enum literal (`'SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\"`) because\nPostgres won't implicitly cast text to an enum in a `SET`. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING,\nand step 1 recovers it after 10 minutes. That gives at-least-once delivery on crash, which\nthe PRD accepts. The two-concurrent-callers and stuck-row behavior is covered\nby NFR-15 integration tests (ADR-9).\n\n_Cites: FR-17, NFR-4, NFR-5, NFR-15, AC-4_\n\n## ADR-4: Retry backoff as a pure lookup table\n\n**Context.** FR-18 sets backoff delays of 1/5/15/60/240 min for attempts 1–5\nand FAILED after the 5th failure. NFR-14 requires a unit test for it.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/email/backoff.ts` exports `const BACKOFF_MIN = [1, 5, 15, 60, 240]`\nand a pure `nextRetry(attempts, now): { status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt } | { status: 'FAILED' }`,\nwhere `attempts` is the count after incrementing. No retry library.\n\n**Consequences.** This is a trivially unit-testable pure function. The admin\n\"Retry now\" action (FR-32) just resets `attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`.\n\n_Cites: FR-18, FR-32, NFR-14, AC-3_\n\n## ADR-5: Email transport: Nodemailer for SMTP, a logger-free console transport, a lazy singleton\n\n**Context.** FR-21 selects the transport by `EMAIL_TRANSPORT`. NFR-9 requires\nHTML + text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header. NFR-11 bans `console.log`\nexcept in the console transport.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`.\n- `smtp`: `nodemailer.createTransport({ host, port, secure, auth })`, created\n  lazily once per process. It sends `{ from: EMAIL_FROM, html, text, headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' } }`.\n  Nodemailer builds `multipart/alternative` automatically when both `html` and `text` are set.\n  It throws a clear error at first send if `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` is missing.\n- `console`: `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text body (the one sanctioned use, NFR-11).\n\nUse a plain `if` on the env value, with no transport interface or factory, because\nthere are only two branches.\n\n**Consequences.** Dev and CI never need SMTP credentials. Tests can assert outbox rows\nand dispatcher state transitions without a mail server. The SMTP failure path\n(AC-3) is tested by stubbing `sendMail` with `vi.mock`.\n\n_Cites: FR-17, FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11_\n\n## ADR-6: Email templates with @react-email/components, rendered at enqueue time\n\n**Context.** FR-13 through FR-15 and FR-16 require HTML and text emails. NFR-7 requires escaping user\ntext. NFR-3 says no request may wait on SMTP.\n\n**Decision.** Templates are `.tsx` components in `src/server/email/templates/`\n(`BaseLayout`, `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification`).\n`src/server/email/render.ts` exposes\n`renderEmail(template, data) → Promise<{ html, text }>`, which calls\n`await render(el)` and `await render(el, { plainText: true })` from\n`@react-email/render` 1.0.1. Rendering happens **inside the request** when\n`notify()`/`sendAuthEmail()` enqueue. The stored `html`/`text` columns\nare then a point-in-time snapshot, and the dispatcher only sends. `BaseLayout` reads\n`SchoolSettings` once per `notify()` call, not once per recipient.\n\n**Consequences.** Escaping (NFR-7) comes from React's JSX text escaping. Never use\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Rendering is CPU work. For 1,000 recipients\n(NFR-1), render the `generic-notification` template **once per notify() call**,\nnot per recipient. This works only if the template data has no per-recipient fields,\nso keep greetings generic in generic-notification. If a later PRD needs per-recipient\npersonalisation, revisit NFR-1. Email templates are exempt from the MUI rule (NFR-10).\n\n_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-7, NFR-10_\n\n## ADR-7: Background dispatch as a cron-hit HTTP route plus an optional tsx worker loop; no queue library\n\n**Context.** FR-19 and FR-20 require both a cron endpoint and a worker script. NFR-3 requires dispatch within 60 s.\nNFR-17 rules out new infrastructure (Redis/BullMQ are implicitly out).\n\n**Decision.**\n- `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` compares `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n  against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length\n  buffers. If `CRON_SECRET` is unset, it always returns 401 (NFR-8). The route\n  calls `dispatchEmails()` and returns `{ sent, failed, retried }`, then\n  calls `purgeOldNotifications()` if more than 24 h have passed since the\n  module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-27).\n- `scripts/worker-email.ts` runs a `while (true) { await dispatchEmails(); await sleep(15_000) }`\n  loop with `try/catch` + `logger.error` around each tick. It calls the service\n  directly, not over HTTP, and catches SIGINT/SIGTERM to exit cleanly. It imports\n  through `tsx`, which resolves the `@/` tsconfig paths.\n\n**Consequences.** A 15 s worker tick, or a cron schedule of 1 minute or less, meets NFR-3.\nThe `lastPurgeAt` value is tracked per process, so it resets on restart and\npurges run on every instance. The PRD accepts this. Mark it\n`ponytail: in-memory last-run, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`.\n\n_Cites: FR-19, FR-20, FR-27, NFR-3, NFR-8, NFR-17, AC-6_\n\n## ADR-8: Client UI with MUI v9 only, plain `fetch` polling, and no data-fetching library\n\n**Context.** FR-22 through FR-26, FR-28 through FR-31 and NFR-10 cover the UI. FR-23 requires a 30 s poll that pauses\nwhen the tab is hidden, and the PRD excludes websockets (NFR-17).\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Bell (FR-22–25).** A client component using `IconButton` + `Badge`\n  (`max={9}` renders \"9+\" natively) + `Popover` + `List`/`ListItemButton`.\n  Polling is a `setInterval(30_000)` started and stopped from a\n  `visibilitychange` listener in one `useEffect`. Don't add SWR or React Query,\n  because they aren't installed and one effect covers the need. Use `Typography` with\n  `sx={{ display: '-webkit-box', WebkitLineClamp: 2, WebkitBoxOrient: 'vertical', overflow: 'hidden' }}`\n  for the 2-line clamp.\n- **Relative time (FR-24).** Use `formatDistanceToNowStrict` from the installed\n  `date-fns`. Use `formatInSchoolTz` for absolute times (NFR-12).\n- **/notifications (FR-26).** Use MUI `Tabs` (All/Unread), a `Select` for the category, a `List`, and\n  `Pagination`.\n- **/account/notifications (FR-28–30).** Use `Table` with a full-width category\n  `TableRow` header per group (intake's default), and `Switch` + `Tooltip`\n  \"Required by the school\" on a disabled switch. Wrap the disabled switch in a `<span>` so the\n  tooltip still fires. Use optimistic local state with rollback, plus the existing `useToast`.\n- **/admin/email-log (FR-31–32).** Reuse the existing `src/components/DataTable`\n  (MUI X DataGrid, URL-driven pagination), with a status `Select` and a row-action `Button`.\n\nThe mui-mcp server is reachable from this session (`useMuiDocs`,\n`fetchDocs` and `generateReactCode` tools are listed), so the NFR-10 blocker doesn't\nstand at architect time. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`\nper component before writing UI, and QA greps for banned imports.\n\n**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. The bell keeps its local state, and\n\"mark read\" refetches the count instead of introducing a shared store.\n\n_Cites: FR-22, FR-23, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-10, NFR-12, NFR-17_\n\n## ADR-9: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; integration tests gated on a test DB\n\n**Context.** NFR-14 lists unit tests, NFR-15 integration tests against a DB,\nand NFR-16 Playwright tests. Vitest currently only includes `tests/unit/**`\n(jsdom), and NFR-13 requires `npm run test` to keep passing on machines without a DB.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Unit tests go in `tests/unit/`: preference resolution, `nextRetry`, link validation\n  and `notifyStudentAndParents` dedupe. These are pure functions, with Prisma mocked by `vi.mock` where needed.\n- Integration tests go in `tests/integration/*.test.ts`. Add that glob to `vitest.config.ts`\n  `include`, set `// @vitest-environment node` per file, and wrap each suite\n  in `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)` so a plain `npm run test`\n  skips it instead of failing. Write the concurrency test as\n  `Promise.all([dispatchEmails(), dispatchEmails()])` over 10 seeded PENDING rows,\n  with `sendMail` mocked to count calls, and assert each id is sent exactly once.\n- Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`, covering the bell count after the admin\n  test button, mark-all-read and a persisted preference toggle.\n\nNo new test tooling.\n\n**Consequences.** CI must set `TEST_DATABASE_URL` for NFR-15 to actually run.\nDev-planning should note this, because a green `npm run test` without it proves nothing about locking.\n\n_Cites: NFR-13, NFR-14, NFR-15, NFR-16, AC-4_\n\n## ADR-10: Link validation and field limits as shared pure helpers; validate in notify() without throwing\n\n**Context.** NFR-6 covers open-redirect-safe links, NFR-18 the title/body limits and\nFR-11 says notify() never throws.\n\n**Decision.** Add `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` to `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`.\nIt returns true only when the string starts with `/`, the second character is not `/` or `\\`, the\nstring contains no `\\`, and it has no control characters. It's shared by notify(), the zod schemas and\nthe bell's `router.push`. In notify(), an unsafe link is dropped (stored as `null`)\nwith `logger.warn`, and title/body are truncated to 140/500 characters with `logger.warn`\n(the intake default). The whole notify() body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`.\n\n**Consequences.** A bad link degrades to a notification that can't be clicked, never\nan exception in the caller's flow. A single regex-free function is trivially unit-tested (NFR-14).\n\n_Cites: FR-6, FR-11, NFR-6, NFR-14, NFR-18_\n\n---\n\n### Notes for downstream sub-tasks\n- **Intake blocker FR-4/FR-16 (confirmed).** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the\n  invite/password-reset template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly,\n  with no Notification row and no preference lookup. The `account.*` types are\n  `emailOnly` + `hidden`. The signature and both callers (users.ts:396, auth.ts:54) stay unchanged.\n- **NFR-1/FR-10 budget.** notify() makes 1 query each for users, preferences and\n  parent links where relevant, then 1 `createMany` for notifications and 1 for outbox\n  rows. That's within the limit of 3 round-trips each. Render once (ADR-6).\n- **No new dependencies anywhere in this PRD.**\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_read_input_tokens":49212,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1124},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ba1665-ff77-440a-aa0d-eea7f83f9b17","uuid":"69b62429-1eb4-44c3-bb9d-d21d661a12cc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:00:38.770Z","request_id":"req_011CghTNuEN9VStnymQFsoJf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RwB3yngx9GbhXnpwL3BAm7":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\n\nTicket: SH-4 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:10:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports confidence 100%, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3, TypeScript 5.5 strict,\nPrisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI 9.5 (material, icons, x-data-grid) + emotion,\nzod 3.23, date-fns 3.6 / date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1 and Playwright 1.47.\n**This PRD adds no new runtime or dev dependency.** Everything it needs is\nalready installed: `nodemailer ^6.9.14` + `@types/nodemailer`,\n`@react-email/components 0.0.25`, `@react-email/render 1.0.1` and `tsx 4.16`.\nThe intake stack fits every FR/NFR, so the ADRs below record only the\nimplementation choices the requirements force.\n\n**Brownfield facts checked in the workspace.** These confirm or sharpen intake:\n- `prisma/schema.prisma` declares `EmailStatus`, `Notification` (with\n  `@@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])`), `NotificationPreference` (composite\n  `@@id([userId, type])`) and `EmailOutbox` (with `@@index([status, nextAttemptAt])`, no FK\n  to User, and `updatedAt` documented as the SENDING timestamp). The 4 existing\n  migrations don't create these tables.\n- `@react-email/render@1.0.1`'s `render(el, { plainText?: true })` returns a\n  **`Promise<string>`**. It's async in 1.x, so every render call must be awaited.\n- `src/lib/env.ts` already validates `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp|console`, default\n  `console`), `SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, an optional `CRON_SECRET` and `APP_URL`.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`,\n  `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError`. `src/lib/logger.ts`\n  provides `logger`. `src/lib/dates.ts` provides `formatInSchoolTz`. `src/server/db.ts`\n  exports the `prisma` singleton.\n- The existing `src/components/DataTable` wraps MUI X DataGrid with\n  URL-driven server pagination. `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts` exists.\n- Vitest `include` is `tests/unit/**` only, with `environment: 'jsdom'`.\n  There's no integration test folder yet.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: One additive Prisma migration for the existing PRD-04 models\n\n**Context.** FR-1 requires the tables. The models are already in\n`schema.prisma` but no migration creates them (an intake blocker). NFR-13\nsays never rename and never re-scaffold. NFR-5 relies on `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`.\n\n**Decision.** Run `prisma migrate dev --name notifications_email` without\ntouching the schema. It generates the `EmailStatus` enum, the 3 tables, their\nindexes and the `Notification`/`NotificationPreference` → `User` cascade FKs.\nKeep the additive `updatedAt` columns exactly as they are declared.\n\n**Consequences.** This is one purely additive migration with nothing destructive. Prisma's\n`@updatedAt` sets the column on every update made through the Prisma client, **but not\non `$executeRaw`/`$queryRaw` writes**. Any raw SQL that sets `status = 'SENDING'`\nmust also set `\"updatedAt\" = now()` itself (see ADR-3).\n\n_Cites: FR-1, NFR-5, NFR-13_\n\n## ADR-2: Registry as a `const` object with `satisfies`; `keyof typeof` drives notify()\n\n**Context.** FR-2 through FR-5 need a typed registry that rejects unknown\nkeys at compile time and that later PRDs can extend.\n\n**Decision.** In `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, define\n`export const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = { ... } as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`\nand `export type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Express\ncategories (FR-3) as a string-literal union, `NotificationCategory`, plus a\n`NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` tuple that the preferences page and its zod enum use.\n`NotificationTypeDef` adds `emailOnly?: true` / `hidden?: true` for the\n`account.*` types (FR-4, FR-28). Later PRDs extend the registry by adding\nkeys to this one object. Don't build a runtime registration API (YAGNI).\n\n**Consequences.** `NotificationPreference.type` and `Notification.type` stay\nplain `String` columns, because the DB doesn't need an enum for a list that\ngrows with every PRD. The zod validator for the preferences PUT (FR-38,\nFR-41) builds `z.enum(Object.keys(NOTIFICATION_TYPES) as [NotificationType, ...])`.\nIt can't import server-only modules, so `types.ts` must stay free of server\nimports (no `prisma`, no `env`) to remain importable from\n`src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`.\n\n_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-28, FR-38, FR-41_\n\n## ADR-3: Dispatcher claim through one raw-SQL `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 and NFR-4 require that concurrent dispatchers never send a row\ntwice. NFR-5 requires recovering rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes. Prisma 5.20\nhas no `SKIP LOCKED` in its query API.\n\n**Decision.** Each `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` run:\n1. **Recover.** Run `prisma.emailOutbox.updateMany({ where: { status: 'SENDING', updatedAt: { lt: now - 10min } }, data: { status: 'PENDING' } })`.\n2. **Claim.** Use a single statement through `prisma.$queryRaw`:\n   ```sql\n   UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status = 'SENDING', \"updatedAt\" = now()\n   WHERE id IN (\n     SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\"\n     WHERE status = 'PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now()\n     ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize}\n     FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n   RETURNING *;\n   ```\n   It runs as one autocommit statement, so the row lock is held only for the flip and is released\n   before any SMTP call. This avoids long transactions, and once a row is\n   SENDING no other dispatcher's `WHERE status='PENDING'` can match it.\n3. **Send each row**, then mark it SENT (`sentAt`) or reschedule it through Prisma `update` (ADR-4).\n\n**Consequences.** This is the only raw SQL in the PRD. Use tagged-template `$queryRaw`, never\n`$queryRawUnsafe`. Cast the enum literal (`'SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\"`) because\nPostgres won't implicitly cast text to an enum in a `SET`. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING,\nand step 1 recovers it after 10 minutes. That gives at-least-once delivery on crash, which\nthe PRD accepts. The two-concurrent-callers and stuck-row behavior is covered\nby NFR-15 integration tests (ADR-9).\n\n_Cites: FR-17, NFR-4, NFR-5, NFR-15, AC-4_\n\n## ADR-4: Retry backoff as a pure lookup table\n\n**Context.** FR-18 sets backoff delays of 1/5/15/60/240 min for attempts 1–5\nand FAILED after the 5th failure. NFR-14 requires a unit test for it.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/email/backoff.ts` exports `const BACKOFF_MIN = [1, 5, 15, 60, 240]`\nand a pure `nextRetry(attempts, now): { status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt } | { status: 'FAILED' }`,\nwhere `attempts` is the count after incrementing. No retry library.\n\n**Consequences.** This is a trivially unit-testable pure function. The admin\n\"Retry now\" action (FR-32) just resets `attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`.\n\n_Cites: FR-18, FR-32, NFR-14, AC-3_\n\n## ADR-5: Email transport: Nodemailer for SMTP, a logger-free console transport, a lazy singleton\n\n**Context.** FR-21 selects the transport by `EMAIL_TRANSPORT`. NFR-9 requires\nHTML + text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header. NFR-11 bans `console.log`\nexcept in the console transport.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`.\n- `smtp`: `nodemailer.createTransport({ host, port, secure, auth })`, created\n  lazily once per process. It sends `{ from: EMAIL_FROM, html, text, headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' } }`.\n  Nodemailer builds `multipart/alternative` automatically when both `html` and `text` are set.\n  It throws a clear error at first send if `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` is missing.\n- `console`: `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text body (the one sanctioned use, NFR-11).\n\nUse a plain `if` on the env value, with no transport interface or factory, because\nthere are only two branches.\n\n**Consequences.** Dev and CI never need SMTP credentials. Tests can assert outbox rows\nand dispatcher state transitions without a mail server. The SMTP failure path\n(AC-3) is tested by stubbing `sendMail` with `vi.mock`.\n\n_Cites: FR-17, FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11_\n\n## ADR-6: Email templates with @react-email/components, rendered at enqueue time\n\n**Context.** FR-13 through FR-15 and FR-16 require HTML and text emails. NFR-7 requires escaping user\ntext. NFR-3 says no request may wait on SMTP.\n\n**Decision.** Templates are `.tsx` components in `src/server/email/templates/`\n(`BaseLayout`, `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification`).\n`src/server/email/render.ts` exposes\n`renderEmail(template, data) → Promise<{ html, text }>`, which calls\n`await render(el)` and `await render(el, { plainText: true })` from\n`@react-email/render` 1.0.1. Rendering happens **inside the request** when\n`notify()`/`sendAuthEmail()` enqueue. The stored `html`/`text` columns\nare then a point-in-time snapshot, and the dispatcher only sends. `BaseLayout` reads\n`SchoolSettings` once per `notify()` call, not once per recipient.\n\n**Consequences.** Escaping (NFR-7) comes from React's JSX text escaping. Never use\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Rendering is CPU work. For 1,000 recipients\n(NFR-1), render the `generic-notification` template **once per notify() call**,\nnot per recipient. This works only if the template data has no per-recipient fields,\nso keep greetings generic in generic-notification. If a later PRD needs per-recipient\npersonalisation, revisit NFR-1. Email templates are exempt from the MUI rule (NFR-10).\n\n_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-7, NFR-10_\n\n## ADR-7: Background dispatch as a cron-hit HTTP route plus an optional tsx worker loop; no queue library\n\n**Context.** FR-19 and FR-20 require both a cron endpoint and a worker script. NFR-3 requires dispatch within 60 s.\nNFR-17 rules out new infrastructure (Redis/BullMQ are implicitly out).\n\n**Decision.**\n- `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` compares `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n  against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length\n  buffers. If `CRON_SECRET` is unset, it always returns 401 (NFR-8). The route\n  calls `dispatchEmails()` and returns `{ sent, failed, retried }`, then\n  calls `purgeOldNotifications()` if more than 24 h have passed since the\n  module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-27).\n- `scripts/worker-email.ts` runs a `while (true) { await dispatchEmails(); await sleep(15_000) }`\n  loop with `try/catch` + `logger.error` around each tick. It calls the service\n  directly, not over HTTP, and catches SIGINT/SIGTERM to exit cleanly. It imports\n  through `tsx`, which resolves the `@/` tsconfig paths.\n\n**Consequences.** A 15 s worker tick, or a cron schedule of 1 minute or less, meets NFR-3.\nThe `lastPurgeAt` value is tracked per process, so it resets on restart and\npurges run on every instance. The PRD accepts this. Mark it\n`ponytail: in-memory last-run, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`.\n\n_Cites: FR-19, FR-20, FR-27, NFR-3, NFR-8, NFR-17, AC-6_\n\n## ADR-8: Client UI with MUI v9 only, plain `fetch` polling, and no data-fetching library\n\n**Context.** FR-22 through FR-26, FR-28 through FR-31 and NFR-10 cover the UI. FR-23 requires a 30 s poll that pauses\nwhen the tab is hidden, and the PRD excludes websockets (NFR-17).\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Bell (FR-22–25).** A client component using `IconButton` + `Badge`\n  (`max={9}` renders \"9+\" natively) + `Popover` + `List`/`ListItemButton`.\n  Polling is a `setInterval(30_000)` started and stopped from a\n  `visibilitychange` listener in one `useEffect`. Don't add SWR or React Query,\n  because they aren't installed and one effect covers the need. Use `Typography` with\n  `sx={{ display: '-webkit-box', WebkitLineClamp: 2, WebkitBoxOrient: 'vertical', overflow: 'hidden' }}`\n  for the 2-line clamp.\n- **Relative time (FR-24).** Use `formatDistanceToNowStrict` from the installed\n  `date-fns`. Use `formatInSchoolTz` for absolute times (NFR-12).\n- **/notifications (FR-26).** Use MUI `Tabs` (All/Unread), a `Select` for the category, a `List`, and\n  `Pagination`.\n- **/account/notifications (FR-28–30).** Use `Table` with a full-width category\n  `TableRow` header per group (intake's default), and `Switch` + `Tooltip`\n  \"Required by the school\" on a disabled switch. Wrap the disabled switch in a `<span>` so the\n  tooltip still fires. Use optimistic local state with rollback, plus the existing `useToast`.\n- **/admin/email-log (FR-31–32).** Reuse the existing `src/components/DataTable`\n  (MUI X DataGrid, URL-driven pagination), with a status `Select` and a row-action `Button`.\n\nThe mui-mcp server is reachable from this session (`useMuiDocs`,\n`fetchDocs` and `generateReactCode` tools are listed), so the NFR-10 blocker doesn't\nstand at architect time. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`\nper component before writing UI, and QA greps for banned imports.\n\n**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. The bell keeps its local state, and\n\"mark read\" refetches the count instead of introducing a shared store.\n\n_Cites: FR-22, FR-23, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-10, NFR-12, NFR-17_\n\n## ADR-9: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; integration tests gated on a test DB\n\n**Context.** NFR-14 lists unit tests, NFR-15 integration tests against a DB,\nand NFR-16 Playwright tests. Vitest currently only includes `tests/unit/**`\n(jsdom), and NFR-13 requires `npm run test` to keep passing on machines without a DB.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Unit tests go in `tests/unit/`: preference resolution, `nextRetry`, link validation\n  and `notifyStudentAndParents` dedupe. These are pure functions, with Prisma mocked by `vi.mock` where needed.\n- Integration tests go in `tests/integration/*.test.ts`. Add that glob to `vitest.config.ts`\n  `include`, set `// @vitest-environment node` per file, and wrap each suite\n  in `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)` so a plain `npm run test`\n  skips it instead of failing. Write the concurrency test as\n  `Promise.all([dispatchEmails(), dispatchEmails()])` over 10 seeded PENDING rows,\n  with `sendMail` mocked to count calls, and assert each id is sent exactly once.\n- Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`, covering the bell count after the admin\n  test button, mark-all-read and a persisted preference toggle.\n\nNo new test tooling.\n\n**Consequences.** CI must set `TEST_DATABASE_URL` for NFR-15 to actually run.\nDev-planning should note this, because a green `npm run test` without it proves nothing about locking.\n\n_Cites: NFR-13, NFR-14, NFR-15, NFR-16, AC-4_\n\n## ADR-10: Link validation and field limits as shared pure helpers; validate in notify() without throwing\n\n**Context.** NFR-6 covers open-redirect-safe links, NFR-18 the title/body limits and\nFR-11 says notify() never throws.\n\n**Decision.** Add `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` to `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`.\nIt returns true only when the string starts with `/`, the second character is not `/` or `\\`, the\nstring contains no `\\`, and it has no control characters. It's shared by notify(), the zod schemas and\nthe bell's `router.push`. In notify(), an unsafe link is dropped (stored as `null`)\nwith `logger.warn`, and title/body are truncated to 140/500 characters with `logger.warn`\n(the intake default). The whole notify() body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`.\n\n**Consequences.** A bad link degrades to a notification that can't be clicked, never\nan exception in the caller's flow. A single regex-free function is trivially unit-tested (NFR-14).\n\n_Cites: FR-6, FR-11, NFR-6, NFR-14, NFR-18_\n\n---\n\n### Notes for downstream sub-tasks\n- **Intake blocker FR-4/FR-16 (confirmed).** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the\n  invite/password-reset template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly,\n  with no Notification row and no preference lookup. The `account.*` types are\n  `emailOnly` + `hidden`. The signature and both callers (users.ts:396, auth.ts:54) stay unchanged.\n- **NFR-1/FR-10 budget.** notify() makes 1 query each for users, preferences and\n  parent links where relevant, then 1 `createMany` for notifications and 1 for outbox\n  rows. That's within the limit of 3 round-trips each. Render once (ADR-6).\n- **No new dependencies anywhere in this PRD.**\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RwB3yngx9GbhXnpwL3BAm7","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ba1665-ff77-440a-aa0d-eea7f83f9b17","uuid":"e2182a78-dba9-4629-9390-65417101aa60","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:00:38.868Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\n\nTicket: SH-4 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:10:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports confidence 100%, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3, TypeScript 5.5 strict,\nPrisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI 9.5 (material, icons, x-data-grid) + emotion,\nzod 3.23, date-fns 3.6 / date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1 and Playwright 1.47.\n**This PRD adds no new runtime or dev dependency.** Everything it needs is\nalready installed: `nodemailer ^6.9.14` + `@types/nodemailer`,\n`@react-email/components 0.0.25`, `@react-email/render 1.0.1` and `tsx 4.16`.\nThe intake stack fits every FR/NFR, so the ADRs below record only the\nimplementation choices the requirements force.\n\n**Brownfield facts checked in the workspace.** These confirm or sharpen intake:\n- `prisma/schema.prisma` declares `EmailStatus`, `Notification` (with\n  `@@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])`), `NotificationPreference` (composite\n  `@@id([userId, type])`) and `EmailOutbox` (with `@@index([status, nextAttemptAt])`, no FK\n  to User, and `updatedAt` documented as the SENDING timestamp). The 4 existing\n  migrations don't create these tables.\n- `@react-email/render@1.0.1`'s `render(el, { plainText?: true })` returns a\n  **`Promise<string>`**. It's async in 1.x, so every render call must be awaited.\n- `src/lib/env.ts` already validates `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp|console`, default\n  `console`), `SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, an optional `CRON_SECRET` and `APP_URL`.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`,\n  `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError`. `src/lib/logger.ts`\n  provides `logger`. `src/lib/dates.ts` provides `formatInSchoolTz`. `src/server/db.ts`\n  exports the `prisma` singleton.\n- The existing `src/components/DataTable` wraps MUI X DataGrid with\n  URL-driven server pagination. `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts` exists.\n- Vitest `include` is `tests/unit/**` only, with `environment: 'jsdom'`.\n  There's no integration test folder yet.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: One additive Prisma migration for the existing PRD-04 models\n\n**Context.** FR-1 requires the tables. The models are already in\n`schema.prisma` but no migration creates them (an intake blocker). NFR-13\nsays never rename and never re-scaffold. NFR-5 relies on `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`.\n\n**Decision.** Run `prisma migrate dev --name notifications_email` without\ntouching the schema. It generates the `EmailStatus` enum, the 3 tables, their\nindexes and the `Notification`/`NotificationPreference` → `User` cascade FKs.\nKeep the additive `updatedAt` columns exactly as they are declared.\n\n**Consequences.** This is one purely additive migration with nothing destructive. Prisma's\n`@updatedAt` sets the column on every update made through the Prisma client, **but not\non `$executeRaw`/`$queryRaw` writes**. Any raw SQL that sets `status = 'SENDING'`\nmust also set `\"updatedAt\" = now()` itself (see ADR-3).\n\n_Cites: FR-1, NFR-5, NFR-13_\n\n## ADR-2: Registry as a `const` object with `satisfies`; `keyof typeof` drives notify()\n\n**Context.** FR-2 through FR-5 need a typed registry that rejects unknown\nkeys at compile time and that later PRDs can extend.\n\n**Decision.** In `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, define\n`export const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = { ... } as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`\nand `export type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Express\ncategories (FR-3) as a string-literal union, `NotificationCategory`, plus a\n`NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` tuple that the preferences page and its zod enum use.\n`NotificationTypeDef` adds `emailOnly?: true` / `hidden?: true` for the\n`account.*` types (FR-4, FR-28). Later PRDs extend the registry by adding\nkeys to this one object. Don't build a runtime registration API (YAGNI).\n\n**Consequences.** `NotificationPreference.type` and `Notification.type` stay\nplain `String` columns, because the DB doesn't need an enum for a list that\ngrows with every PRD. The zod validator for the preferences PUT (FR-38,\nFR-41) builds `z.enum(Object.keys(NOTIFICATION_TYPES) as [NotificationType, ...])`.\nIt can't import server-only modules, so `types.ts` must stay free of server\nimports (no `prisma`, no `env`) to remain importable from\n`src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`.\n\n_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-28, FR-38, FR-41_\n\n## ADR-3: Dispatcher claim through one raw-SQL `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 and NFR-4 require that concurrent dispatchers never send a row\ntwice. NFR-5 requires recovering rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes. Prisma 5.20\nhas no `SKIP LOCKED` in its query API.\n\n**Decision.** Each `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` run:\n1. **Recover.** Run `prisma.emailOutbox.updateMany({ where: { status: 'SENDING', updatedAt: { lt: now - 10min } }, data: { status: 'PENDING' } })`.\n2. **Claim.** Use a single statement through `prisma.$queryRaw`:\n   ```sql\n   UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status = 'SENDING', \"updatedAt\" = now()\n   WHERE id IN (\n     SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\"\n     WHERE status = 'PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now()\n     ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize}\n     FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n   RETURNING *;\n   ```\n   It runs as one autocommit statement, so the row lock is held only for the flip and is released\n   before any SMTP call. This avoids long transactions, and once a row is\n   SENDING no other dispatcher's `WHERE status='PENDING'` can match it.\n3. **Send each row**, then mark it SENT (`sentAt`) or reschedule it through Prisma `update` (ADR-4).\n\n**Consequences.** This is the only raw SQL in the PRD. Use tagged-template `$queryRaw`, never\n`$queryRawUnsafe`. Cast the enum literal (`'SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\"`) because\nPostgres won't implicitly cast text to an enum in a `SET`. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING,\nand step 1 recovers it after 10 minutes. That gives at-least-once delivery on crash, which\nthe PRD accepts. The two-concurrent-callers and stuck-row behavior is covered\nby NFR-15 integration tests (ADR-9).\n\n_Cites: FR-17, NFR-4, NFR-5, NFR-15, AC-4_\n\n## ADR-4: Retry backoff as a pure lookup table\n\n**Context.** FR-18 sets backoff delays of 1/5/15/60/240 min for attempts 1–5\nand FAILED after the 5th failure. NFR-14 requires a unit test for it.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/email/backoff.ts` exports `const BACKOFF_MIN = [1, 5, 15, 60, 240]`\nand a pure `nextRetry(attempts, now): { status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt } | { status: 'FAILED' }`,\nwhere `attempts` is the count after incrementing. No retry library.\n\n**Consequences.** This is a trivially unit-testable pure function. The admin\n\"Retry now\" action (FR-32) just resets `attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`.\n\n_Cites: FR-18, FR-32, NFR-14, AC-3_\n\n## ADR-5: Email transport: Nodemailer for SMTP, a logger-free console transport, a lazy singleton\n\n**Context.** FR-21 selects the transport by `EMAIL_TRANSPORT`. NFR-9 requires\nHTML + text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header. NFR-11 bans `console.log`\nexcept in the console transport.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`.\n- `smtp`: `nodemailer.createTransport({ host, port, secure, auth })`, created\n  lazily once per process. It sends `{ from: EMAIL_FROM, html, text, headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' } }`.\n  Nodemailer builds `multipart/alternative` automatically when both `html` and `text` are set.\n  It throws a clear error at first send if `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` is missing.\n- `console`: `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text body (the one sanctioned use, NFR-11).\n\nUse a plain `if` on the env value, with no transport interface or factory, because\nthere are only two branches.\n\n**Consequences.** Dev and CI never need SMTP credentials. Tests can assert outbox rows\nand dispatcher state transitions without a mail server. The SMTP failure path\n(AC-3) is tested by stubbing `sendMail` with `vi.mock`.\n\n_Cites: FR-17, FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11_\n\n## ADR-6: Email templates with @react-email/components, rendered at enqueue time\n\n**Context.** FR-13 through FR-15 and FR-16 require HTML and text emails. NFR-7 requires escaping user\ntext. NFR-3 says no request may wait on SMTP.\n\n**Decision.** Templates are `.tsx` components in `src/server/email/templates/`\n(`BaseLayout`, `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification`).\n`src/server/email/render.ts` exposes\n`renderEmail(template, data) → Promise<{ html, text }>`, which calls\n`await render(el)` and `await render(el, { plainText: true })` from\n`@react-email/render` 1.0.1. Rendering happens **inside the request** when\n`notify()`/`sendAuthEmail()` enqueue. The stored `html`/`text` columns\nare then a point-in-time snapshot, and the dispatcher only sends. `BaseLayout` reads\n`SchoolSettings` once per `notify()` call, not once per recipient.\n\n**Consequences.** Escaping (NFR-7) comes from React's JSX text escaping. Never use\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Rendering is CPU work. For 1,000 recipients\n(NFR-1), render the `generic-notification` template **once per notify() call**,\nnot per recipient. This works only if the template data has no per-recipient fields,\nso keep greetings generic in generic-notification. If a later PRD needs per-recipient\npersonalisation, revisit NFR-1. Email templates are exempt from the MUI rule (NFR-10).\n\n_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-7, NFR-10_\n\n## ADR-7: Background dispatch as a cron-hit HTTP route plus an optional tsx worker loop; no queue library\n\n**Context.** FR-19 and FR-20 require both a cron endpoint and a worker script. NFR-3 requires dispatch within 60 s.\nNFR-17 rules out new infrastructure (Redis/BullMQ are implicitly out).\n\n**Decision.**\n- `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` compares `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n  against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length\n  buffers. If `CRON_SECRET` is unset, it always returns 401 (NFR-8). The route\n  calls `dispatchEmails()` and returns `{ sent, failed, retried }`, then\n  calls `purgeOldNotifications()` if more than 24 h have passed since the\n  module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-27).\n- `scripts/worker-email.ts` runs a `while (true) { await dispatchEmails(); await sleep(15_000) }`\n  loop with `try/catch` + `logger.error` around each tick. It calls the service\n  directly, not over HTTP, and catches SIGINT/SIGTERM to exit cleanly. It imports\n  through `tsx`, which resolves the `@/` tsconfig paths.\n\n**Consequences.** A 15 s worker tick, or a cron schedule of 1 minute or less, meets NFR-3.\nThe `lastPurgeAt` value is tracked per process, so it resets on restart and\npurges run on every instance. The PRD accepts this. Mark it\n`ponytail: in-memory last-run, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`.\n\n_Cites: FR-19, FR-20, FR-27, NFR-3, NFR-8, NFR-17, AC-6_\n\n## ADR-8: Client UI with MUI v9 only, plain `fetch` polling, and no data-fetching library\n\n**Context.** FR-22 through FR-26, FR-28 through FR-31 and NFR-10 cover the UI. FR-23 requires a 30 s poll that pauses\nwhen the tab is hidden, and the PRD excludes websockets (NFR-17).\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Bell (FR-22–25).** A client component using `IconButton` + `Badge`\n  (`max={9}` renders \"9+\" natively) + `Popover` + `List`/`ListItemButton`.\n  Polling is a `setInterval(30_000)` started and stopped from a\n  `visibilitychange` listener in one `useEffect`. Don't add SWR or React Query,\n  because they aren't installed and one effect covers the need. Use `Typography` with\n  `sx={{ display: '-webkit-box', WebkitLineClamp: 2, WebkitBoxOrient: 'vertical', overflow: 'hidden' }}`\n  for the 2-line clamp.\n- **Relative time (FR-24).** Use `formatDistanceToNowStrict` from the installed\n  `date-fns`. Use `formatInSchoolTz` for absolute times (NFR-12).\n- **/notifications (FR-26).** Use MUI `Tabs` (All/Unread), a `Select` for the category, a `List`, and\n  `Pagination`.\n- **/account/notifications (FR-28–30).** Use `Table` with a full-width category\n  `TableRow` header per group (intake's default), and `Switch` + `Tooltip`\n  \"Required by the school\" on a disabled switch. Wrap the disabled switch in a `<span>` so the\n  tooltip still fires. Use optimistic local state with rollback, plus the existing `useToast`.\n- **/admin/email-log (FR-31–32).** Reuse the existing `src/components/DataTable`\n  (MUI X DataGrid, URL-driven pagination), with a status `Select` and a row-action `Button`.\n\nThe mui-mcp server is reachable from this session (`useMuiDocs`,\n`fetchDocs` and `generateReactCode` tools are listed), so the NFR-10 blocker doesn't\nstand at architect time. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`\nper component before writing UI, and QA greps for banned imports.\n\n**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. The bell keeps its local state, and\n\"mark read\" refetches the count instead of introducing a shared store.\n\n_Cites: FR-22, FR-23, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-10, NFR-12, NFR-17_\n\n## ADR-9: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; integration tests gated on a test DB\n\n**Context.** NFR-14 lists unit tests, NFR-15 integration tests against a DB,\nand NFR-16 Playwright tests. Vitest currently only includes `tests/unit/**`\n(jsdom), and NFR-13 requires `npm run test` to keep passing on machines without a DB.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Unit tests go in `tests/unit/`: preference resolution, `nextRetry`, link validation\n  and `notifyStudentAndParents` dedupe. These are pure functions, with Prisma mocked by `vi.mock` where needed.\n- Integration tests go in `tests/integration/*.test.ts`. Add that glob to `vitest.config.ts`\n  `include`, set `// @vitest-environment node` per file, and wrap each suite\n  in `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)` so a plain `npm run test`\n  skips it instead of failing. Write the concurrency test as\n  `Promise.all([dispatchEmails(), dispatchEmails()])` over 10 seeded PENDING rows,\n  with `sendMail` mocked to count calls, and assert each id is sent exactly once.\n- Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`, covering the bell count after the admin\n  test button, mark-all-read and a persisted preference toggle.\n\nNo new test tooling.\n\n**Consequences.** CI must set `TEST_DATABASE_URL` for NFR-15 to actually run.\nDev-planning should note this, because a green `npm run test` without it proves nothing about locking.\n\n_Cites: NFR-13, NFR-14, NFR-15, NFR-16, AC-4_\n\n## ADR-10: Link validation and field limits as shared pure helpers; validate in notify() without throwing\n\n**Context.** NFR-6 covers open-redirect-safe links, NFR-18 the title/body limits and\nFR-11 says notify() never throws.\n\n**Decision.** Add `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` to `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`.\nIt returns true only when the string starts with `/`, the second character is not `/` or `\\`, the\nstring contains no `\\`, and it has no control characters. It's shared by notify(), the zod schemas and\nthe bell's `router.push`. In notify(), an unsafe link is dropped (stored as `null`)\nwith `logger.warn`, and title/body are truncated to 140/500 characters with `logger.warn`\n(the intake default). The whole notify() body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`.\n\n**Consequences.** A bad link degrades to a notification that can't be clicked, never\nan exception in the caller's flow. A single regex-free function is trivially unit-tested (NFR-14).\n\n_Cites: FR-6, FR-11, NFR-6, NFR-14, NFR-18_\n\n---\n\n### Notes for downstream sub-tasks\n- **Intake blocker FR-4/FR-16 (confirmed).** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the\n  invite/password-reset template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly,\n  with no Notification row and no preference lookup. The `account.*` types are\n  `emailOnly` + `hidden`. The signature and both callers (users.ts:396, auth.ts:54) stay unchanged.\n- **NFR-1/FR-10 budget.** notify() makes 1 query each for users, preferences and\n  parent links where relevant, then 1 `createMany` for notifications and 1 for outbox\n  rows. That's within the limit of 3 round-trips each. Render once (ADR-6).\n- **No new dependencies anywhere in this PRD.**\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":228,"newStart":1,"newLines":280,"lines":["-# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)","+# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)"," ","-Ticket: abcd-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:00:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-4 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:10:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-Base stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%, confirmed by","-`package.json`): Next.js 14.2 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict,","-Prisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI v9 + emotion, zod 3, react-hook-form,","-date-fns-tz. The auth dependencies are already installed: `next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25`","-and `bcrypt ^6`. **This PRD adds no new runtime dependency.** The ADRs below","-only cover the implementation choices this PRD's requirements force.","+**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports confidence 100%, and `package.json`","+confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3, TypeScript 5.5 strict,","+Prisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI 9.5 (material, icons, x-data-grid) + emotion,","+zod 3.23, date-fns 3.6 / date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1 and Playwright 1.47.","+**This PRD adds no new runtime or dev dependency.** Everything it needs is","+already installed: `nodemailer ^6.9.14` + `@types/nodemailer`,","+`@react-email/components 0.0.25`, `@react-email/render 1.0.1` and `tsx 4.16`.","+The intake stack fits every FR/NFR, so the ADRs below record only the","+implementation choices the requirements force."," ","-Brownfield facts checked in the workspace (they correct intake in places):","-- `requireRole()` is sync and returns `{id, role}`. It has **50 call sites in","-  43 files**, not ~94. Every caller is already inside an `async` server page,","-  layout or route handler.","-- `src/server/http.ts` `ApiErrorCode` already includes `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401,","-  `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429 and `INVALID_TOKEN` 410, so no envelope","-  changes are needed.","-- `AuditLog.ip String?` exists. `audit()` has no `request` param.","+**Brownfield facts checked in the workspace.** These confirm or sharpen intake:","+- `prisma/schema.prisma` declares `EmailStatus`, `Notification` (with","+  `@@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])`), `NotificationPreference` (composite","+  `@@id([userId, type])`) and `EmailOutbox` (with `@@index([status, nextAttemptAt])`, no FK","+  to User, and `updatedAt` documented as the SENDING timestamp). The 4 existing","+  migrations don't create these tables.","+- `@react-email/render@1.0.1`'s `render(el, { plainText?: true })` returns a","+  **`Promise<string>`**. It's async in 1.x, so every render call must be awaited.","+- `src/lib/env.ts` already validates `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp|console`, default","+  `console`), `SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, an optional `CRON_SECRET` and `APP_URL`.","+- `src/server/http.ts` already provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`,","+  `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError`. `src/lib/logger.ts`","+  provides `logger`. `src/lib/dates.ts` provides `formatInSchoolTz`. `src/server/db.ts`","+  exports the `prisma` singleton.","+- The existing `src/components/DataTable` wraps MUI X DataGrid with","+  URL-driven server pagination. `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts` exists.","+- Vitest `include` is `tests/unit/**` only, with `environment: 'jsdom'`.","+  There's no integration test folder yet."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-1: Auth.js v5 with a split config (edge-safe `auth.config.ts` + Node `auth.ts`)","+## ADR-1: One additive Prisma migration for the existing PRD-04 models"," ","-**Context.** FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12 and FR-34 need credential sign-in, JWT","-sessions and a `middleware.ts` gate. In Next 14, middleware runs on the Edge","-runtime, where `bcrypt` (a native addon) and Prisma's Node client can't load.","+**Context.** FR-1 requires the tables. The models are already in","+`schema.prisma` but no migration creates them (an intake blocker). NFR-13","+says never rename and never re-scaffold. NFR-5 relies on `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`."," ","-**Decision.** Use the documented Auth.js v5 split:","-- `src/server/auth/auth.config.ts` (edge-safe): `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`,","-  `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, the `authorized`/`jwt`/`session` shape","-  callbacks, and no providers that touch the DB.","-- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })] })`,","-  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut }`. It also holds the","-  DB-touching `jwt` callback logic (FR-11).","-- `middleware.ts` builds `NextAuth(authConfig).auth`. It only decodes the JWT.","-- `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` re-exports `handlers` (FR-34).","+**Decision.** Run `prisma migrate dev --name notifications_email` without","+touching the schema. It generates the `EmailStatus` enum, the 3 tables, their","+indexes and the `Notification`/`NotificationPreference` → `User` cascade FKs.","+Keep the additive `updatedAt` columns exactly as they are declared."," ","-Don't use a Prisma adapter. JWT sessions with Credentials don't need one, and","-the adapter would require Account/Session/VerificationToken models the PRD","-doesn't define.","+**Consequences.** This is one purely additive migration with nothing destructive. Prisma's","+`@updatedAt` sets the column on every update made through the Prisma client, **but not","+on `$executeRaw`/`$queryRaw` writes**. Any raw SQL that sets `status = 'SENDING'`","+must also set `\"updatedAt\" = now()` itself (see ADR-3)."," ","-**Consequences.** Middleware can't check `passwordChangedAt` because it has no","-DB access. That check lives in the Node-side `jwt` callback (ADR-4), which","-runs whenever `auth()` is called from server code. Because next-auth is a","-beta, pin the installed version exactly (drop the `^`) so a beta bump can't","-change callback signatures mid-PRD.","+_Cites: FR-1, NFR-5, NFR-13_"," ","-_Cites: FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12, FR-34, NFR-2_","+## ADR-2: Registry as a `const` object with `satisfies`; `keyof typeof` drives notify()"," ","-## ADR-2: `requireRole()` / `requireUser()` become async; update all 50 call sites with `await`","+**Context.** FR-2 through FR-5 need a typed registry that rejects unknown","+keys at compile time and that later PRDs can extend."," ","-**Context.** FR-28 and FR-29 replace `PLACEHOLDER_USER` with the real session.","-Auth.js `auth()` is async. Intake flagged this as a blocker. Options:","-(a) make the helpers async and add `await` at each call site;","-(b) keep them sync by reading identity from headers set by middleware;","-(c) use React `cache()` plus a sync wrapper.","+**Decision.** In `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, define","+`export const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = { ... } as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`","+and `export type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Express","+categories (FR-3) as a string-literal union, `NotificationCategory`, plus a","+`NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` tuple that the preferences page and its zod enum use.","+`NotificationTypeDef` adds `emailOnly?: true` / `hidden?: true` for the","+`account.*` types (FR-4, FR-28). Later PRDs extend the registry by adding","+keys to this one object. Don't build a runtime registration API (YAGNI)."," ","-**Decision.** (a). `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole(...roles)`","-become `async` with the same arguments and the same `{id, role, ...}` return","-shape, so the signature stays compatible (FR-29). Each of the 50 call sites","-changes from `requireRole(...)` to `await requireRole(...)`. That's a","-mechanical one-token edit, and every caller is already async. Wrap","-`getCurrentUser` in React `cache()` so a page plus its layout share one","-session decode per request.","+**Consequences.** `NotificationPreference.type` and `Notification.type` stay","+plain `String` columns, because the DB doesn't need an enum for a list that","+grows with every PRD. The zod validator for the preferences PUT (FR-38,","+FR-41) builds `z.enum(Object.keys(NOTIFICATION_TYPES) as [NotificationType, ...])`.","+It can't import server-only modules, so `types.ts` must stay free of server","+imports (no `prisma`, no `env`) to remain importable from","+`src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`."," ","-Option (b) was rejected: identity read from headers is a spoofing risk","-(NFR-7), and it skips the FR-11 revocation check. Option (c) can't make an","-async read sync.","+_Cites: FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-28, FR-38, FR-41_"," ","-**Consequences.** `tsc` catches every missed `await`, because a `Promise` has","-no `.role` or `.id`. Bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statements don't fail","-typecheck, though, and a forgotten `await` there silently does nothing.","-Enable `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises` for `src/**`, or have","-dev-planning grep for un-awaited calls. Redirect-vs-throw: in server pages,","-use `redirect('/login')` / `redirect('/forbidden')` from `next/navigation`;","-in route handlers, throw `AppError` (UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN), which","-`withHandler` already maps. Implement this as one helper that the page and","-API paths both call, not two copies. `course-access.ts` and","-`student-access.ts` keep taking the resolved user object and aren't modified","-(NFR-9).","+## ADR-3: Dispatcher claim through one raw-SQL `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`"," ","-_Cites: FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9_","+**Context.** FR-17 and NFR-4 require that concurrent dispatchers never send a row","+twice. NFR-5 requires recovering rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes. Prisma 5.20","+has no `SKIP LOCKED` in its query API."," ","-## ADR-3: Password hashing with the existing `bcrypt` at cost 12, plus a dummy compare for unknown users","+**Decision.** Each `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` run:","+1. **Recover.** Run `prisma.emailOutbox.updateMany({ where: { status: 'SENDING', updatedAt: { lt: now - 10min } }, data: { status: 'PENDING' } })`.","+2. **Claim.** Use a single statement through `prisma.$queryRaw`:","+   ```sql","+   UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status = 'SENDING', \"updatedAt\" = now()","+   WHERE id IN (","+     SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\"","+     WHERE status = 'PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now()","+     ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize}","+     FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)","+   RETURNING *;","+   ```","+   It runs as one autocommit statement, so the row lock is held only for the flip and is released","+   before any SMTP call. This avoids long transactions, and once a row is","+   SENDING no other dispatcher's `WHERE status='PENDING'` can match it.","+3. **Send each row**, then mark it SENT (`sentAt`) or reschedule it through Prisma `update` (ADR-4)."," ","-**Context.** FR-4 sets cost 12. NFR-3 requires constant-ish timing when the","-user doesn't exist. NFR-4 requires sign-in in under 1 s at p95.","+**Consequences.** This is the only raw SQL in the PRD. Use tagged-template `$queryRaw`, never","+`$queryRawUnsafe`. Cast the enum literal (`'SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\"`) because","+Postgres won't implicitly cast text to an enum in a `SET`. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING,","+and step 1 recovers it after 10 minutes. That gives at-least-once delivery on crash, which","+the PRD accepts. The two-concurrent-callers and stuck-row behavior is covered","+by NFR-15 integration tests (ADR-9)."," ","-**Decision.** Use `bcrypt.hash(pw, 12)` / `bcrypt.compare`. Precompute one","-module-level dummy hash at cost 12 and compare against it when the user is","-missing, disabled or locked, so every path pays one bcrypt compare. Don't use","-argon2 (it's a new native dependency and the PRD specifies bcrypt).","+_Cites: FR-17, NFR-4, NFR-5, NFR-15, AC-4_"," ","-**Consequences.** One cost-12 compare takes about 250 ms on modern hardware,","-which leaves room under the 1 s budget for the user lookup, the","-failedLoginCount update and the audit insert. Never call bcrypt twice on one","-sign-in path. bcrypt runs only in Node code, never in middleware (ADR-1).","+## ADR-4: Retry backoff as a pure lookup table"," ","-_Cites: FR-4, FR-6, NFR-3, NFR-4_","+**Context.** FR-18 sets backoff delays of 1/5/15/60/240 min for attempts 1–5","+and FAILED after the 5th failure. NFR-14 requires a unit test for it."," ","-## ADR-4: Session revocation via a `passwordChangedAt` check in the jwt callback, throttled to every 5 minutes","+**Decision.** `src/server/email/backoff.ts` exports `const BACKOFF_MIN = [1, 5, 15, 60, 240]`","+and a pure `nextRetry(attempts, now): { status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt } | { status: 'FAILED' }`,","+where `attempts` is the count after incrementing. No retry library."," ","-**Context.** FR-11 and FR-23 require that a password change or reset","-invalidates other sessions. Sessions are stateless JWTs (FR-10), so there's","-no session table.","+**Consequences.** This is a trivially unit-testable pure function. The admin","+\"Retry now\" action (FR-32) just resets `attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`."," ","-**Decision.** Store `iat` and a `checkedAt` timestamp in the token. In the","-Node `jwt` callback, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, select only","-`passwordChangedAt, status` for `token.id`. If `passwordChangedAt > iat` or","-the status isn't ACTIVE, return `null` to invalidate the session. Otherwise","-update `checkedAt`. For FR-23's \"re-issue current session\", call `unstable_update()`","-(the v5 `update`) after the change, which mints a token with a fresh `iat`.","+_Cites: FR-18, FR-32, NFR-14, AC-3_"," ","-**Consequences.** Revocation can lag by up to 5 minutes. The PRD explicitly","-accepts that window. Edge middleware can still let a revoked token through","-for page navigation in that window. The server-side `requireUser()` call","-then catches it, and that call is the real guard (NFR-7).","+## ADR-5: Email transport: Nodemailer for SMTP, a logger-free console transport, a lazy singleton"," ","-_Cites: FR-10, FR-11, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-7_","+**Context.** FR-21 selects the transport by `EMAIL_TRANSPORT`. NFR-9 requires","+HTML + text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header. NFR-11 bans `console.log`","+except in the console transport."," ","-## ADR-5: Tokens with `node:crypto` only (randomBytes, SHA-256, timingSafeEqual)","+**Decision.** `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`.","+- `smtp`: `nodemailer.createTransport({ host, port, secure, auth })`, created","+  lazily once per process. It sends `{ from: EMAIL_FROM, html, text, headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' } }`.","+  Nodemailer builds `multipart/alternative` automatically when both `html` and `text` are set.","+  It throws a clear error at first send if `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` is missing.","+- `console`: `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text body (the one sanctioned use, NFR-11)."," ","-**Context.** FR-13 needs a single AuthToken module. NFR-1 requires stored","-hashes and constant-time comparison.","+Use a plain `if` on the env value, with no transport interface or factory, because","+there are only two branches."," ","-**Decision.** `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` uses `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`","-and `createHash('sha256')`. Look up by the hash (the DB index), then confirm","-with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers. No JWT, nanoid or other library.","+**Consequences.** Dev and CI never need SMTP credentials. Tests can assert outbox rows","+and dispatcher state transitions without a mail server. The SMTP failure path","+(AC-3) is tested by stubbing `sendMail` with `vi.mock`."," ","-**Consequences.** Raw tokens exist only in the returned value and the","-emailed or logged link, never in the DB or audit metadata (FR-31). The","-\"invalidate older unused tokens\" step (FR-20, FR-26) is one `updateMany`","-that sets `usedAt` in the same `$transaction` as the create.","+_Cites: FR-17, FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11_"," ","-_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1_","+## ADR-6: Email templates with @react-email/components, rendered at enqueue time"," ","-## ADR-6: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter (a `Map` of timestamp arrays); no Redis","+**Context.** FR-13 through FR-15 and FR-16 require HTML and text emails. NFR-7 requires escaping user","+text. NFR-3 says no request may wait on SMTP."," ","-**Context.** FR-7 (10 per IP per 5 min) and FR-19 (3 per email per hour, 10","-per IP per hour) explicitly ask for an exported in-memory limiter in","-`src/server/rate-limit.ts`. The PRD adds no infrastructure (NFR-11).","+**Decision.** Templates are `.tsx` components in `src/server/email/templates/`","+(`BaseLayout`, `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification`).","+`src/server/email/render.ts` exposes","+`renderEmail(template, data) → Promise<{ html, text }>`, which calls","+`await render(el)` and `await render(el, { plainText: true })` from","+`@react-email/render` 1.0.1. Rendering happens **inside the request** when","+`notify()`/`sendAuthEmail()` enqueue. The stored `html`/`text` columns","+are then a point-in-time snapshot, and the dispatcher only sends. `BaseLayout` reads","+`SchoolSettings` once per `notify()` call, not once per recipient."," ","-**Decision.** One `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs): { ok, retryAfterMs }`","-over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`, pruning expired timestamps on","-each call. Namespace keys like `login:ip:<ip>` and `forgot:email:<email>`.","-Take the IP from the first entry of `x-forwarded-for`, using the same","-helper `audit()` uses (FR-30). Call it from the Node side (authorize and","-route handlers), not middleware, because Edge isolates don't share memory.","+**Consequences.** Escaping (NFR-7) comes from React's JSX text escaping. Never use","+`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Rendering is CPU work. For 1,000 recipients","+(NFR-1), render the `generic-notification` template **once per notify() call**,","+not per recipient. This works only if the template data has no per-recipient fields,","+so keep greetings generic in generic-notification. If a later PRD needs per-recipient","+personalisation, revisit NFR-1. Email templates are exempt from the MUI rule (NFR-10)."," ","-**Consequences.** The ceiling is per process: limits reset on restart and","-aren't shared across instances. Mark the code with a","-`ponytail: per-process limiter, swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if","-horizontally scaled` comment. With Credentials, a RATE_LIMITED outcome has","-to go through Auth.js's `CredentialsSignin` subclass `code` to reach the","-login form (FR-5, FR-7).","+_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-7, NFR-10_"," ","-_Cites: FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-8, NFR-11_","+## ADR-7: Background dispatch as a cron-hit HTTP route plus an optional tsx worker loop; no queue library"," ","-## ADR-7: Validation with the existing zod + react-hook-form; one policy schema shared by client and server","+**Context.** FR-19 and FR-20 require both a cron endpoint and a worker script. NFR-3 requires dispatch within 60 s.","+NFR-17 rules out new infrastructure (Redis/BullMQ are implicitly out)."," ","-**Context.** FR-17 defines the policy. FR-18 needs a live checklist.","-FR-16, FR-21 and FR-23 must enforce the policy server-side.","+**Decision.**","+- `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` compares `Authorization: Bearer <token>`","+  against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length","+  buffers. If `CRON_SECRET` is unset, it always returns 401 (NFR-8). The route","+  calls `dispatchEmails()` and returns `{ sent, failed, retried }`, then","+  calls `purgeOldNotifications()` if more than 24 h have passed since the","+  module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-27).","+- `scripts/worker-email.ts` runs a `while (true) { await dispatchEmails(); await sleep(15_000) }`","+  loop with `try/catch` + `logger.error` around each tick. It calls the service","+  directly, not over HTTP, and catches SIGINT/SIGTERM to exit cleanly. It imports","+  through `tsx`, which resolves the `@/` tsconfig paths."," ","-**Decision.** `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports the zod schema plus a","-pure `passwordChecks(pw, email)` that returns per-rule booleans. The","-checklist UI and the zod `superRefine` both use that function. The","-common-password check needs the file at","-`src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt`, so it runs only on the server: read","-the file once into a `Set` with `fs` in a server-only module. The client","-checklist shows the length, letter, digit and not-email rules live, and the","-common-password rule is reported from the server response.","+**Consequences.** A 15 s worker tick, or a cron schedule of 1 minute or less, meets NFR-3.","+The `lastPurgeAt` value is tracked per process, so it resets on restart and","+purges run on every instance. The PRD accepts this. Mark it","+`ponytail: in-memory last-run, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`."," ","-**Consequences.** The 1,000-word list never ships in the client bundle. The","-validator file has to stay importable from the client, so keep the `fs`","-read in a separate server-only file that adds the common-password refinement.","+_Cites: FR-19, FR-20, FR-27, NFR-3, NFR-8, NFR-17, AC-6_"," ","-_Cites: FR-17, FR-18, FR-16, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-5, NFR-8_","+## ADR-8: Client UI with MUI v9 only, plain `fetch` polling, and no data-fetching library"," ","-## ADR-8: UI with MUI v9 only (Sign-in template patterns), documented through mui-mcp","+**Context.** FR-22 through FR-26, FR-28 through FR-31 and NFR-10 cover the UI. FR-23 requires a 30 s poll that pauses","+when the tab is hidden, and the PRD excludes websockets (NFR-17)."," ","-**Context.** NFR-6 bans non-MUI UI libraries and requires every component to","-be looked up through mui-mcp. FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24 and FR-32 add auth","-pages and top-bar changes.","+**Decision.**","+- **Bell (FR-22–25).** A client component using `IconButton` + `Badge`","+  (`max={9}` renders \"9+\" natively) + `Popover` + `List`/`ListItemButton`.","+  Polling is a `setInterval(30_000)` started and stopped from a","+  `visibilitychange` listener in one `useEffect`. Don't add SWR or React Query,","+  because they aren't installed and one effect covers the need. Use `Typography` with","+  `sx={{ display: '-webkit-box', WebkitLineClamp: 2, WebkitBoxOrient: 'vertical', overflow: 'hidden' }}`","+  for the 2-line clamp.","+- **Relative time (FR-24).** Use `formatDistanceToNowStrict` from the installed","+  `date-fns`. Use `formatInSchoolTz` for absolute times (NFR-12).","+- **/notifications (FR-26).** Use MUI `Tabs` (All/Unread), a `Select` for the category, a `List`, and","+  `Pagination`.","+- **/account/notifications (FR-28–30).** Use `Table` with a full-width category","+  `TableRow` header per group (intake's default), and `Switch` + `Tooltip`","+  \"Required by the school\" on a disabled switch. Wrap the disabled switch in a `<span>` so the","+  tooltip still fires. Use optimistic local state with rollback, plus the existing `useToast`.","+- **/admin/email-log (FR-31–32).** Reuse the existing `src/components/DataTable`","+  (MUI X DataGrid, URL-driven pagination), with a status `Select` and a row-action `Button`."," ","-**Decision.** Use the installed `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` 9.5:","-Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment + IconButton (Visibility icons),","-Alert, List/ListItemIcon for the checklist, and Menu/Avatar/Chip in the top","-bar. Use the existing `useToast` for toasts (FR-21, FR-23), not notistack or","-sonner. Auth pages live in a `src/app/(auth)` route group outside the","-`(app)` shell. The mui-mcp server was reachable from this session","-(`useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools were listed), so the NFR-6 blocker doesn't","-stand at architect time. Dev must still check it itself.","+The mui-mcp server is reachable from this session (`useMuiDocs`,","+`fetchDocs` and `generateReactCode` tools are listed), so the NFR-10 blocker doesn't","+stand at architect time. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`","+per component before writing UI, and QA greps for banned imports."," ","-**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. `aria-live=\"polite\"` on the form-level","-Alert and focus-first-invalid (via react-hook-form `setFocus`) meet NFR-5.","+**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. The bell keeps its local state, and","+\"mark read\" refetches the count instead of introducing a shared store."," ","-_Cites: FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-5, NFR-6_","+_Cites: FR-22, FR-23, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-10, NFR-12, NFR-17_"," ","-## ADR-9: Schema reconciled additively with one Prisma migration","+## ADR-9: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; integration tests gated on a test DB"," ","-**Context.** FR-1 and the intake blockers list the divergences: `ip` vs","-`ipAddress`, the extra `ARCHIVED` value, different AuditLog indexes. NFR-9","-says never rename.","+**Context.** NFR-14 lists unit tests, NFR-15 integration tests against a DB,","+and NFR-16 Playwright tests. Vitest currently only includes `tests/unit/**`","+(jsdom), and NFR-13 requires `npm run test` to keep passing on machines without a DB."," ","-**Decision.** Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED` and keep the","-existing extra indexes. Add only","-`@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to","-AuditLog, plus any User auth fields the diff finds missing","-(failedLoginCount, lockedUntil, lastLoginAt, passwordChangedAt). Apply them","-in one `prisma migrate dev --name auth_reconcile` migration. FR-4's \"status","-!= ACTIVE\" check already rejects ARCHIVED.","+**Decision.**","+- Unit tests go in `tests/unit/`: preference resolution, `nextRetry`, link validation","+  and `notifyStudentAndParents` dedupe. These are pure functions, with Prisma mocked by `vi.mock` where needed.","+- Integration tests go in `tests/integration/*.test.ts`. Add that glob to `vitest.config.ts`","+  `include`, set `// @vitest-environment node` per file, and wrap each suite","+  in `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)` so a plain `npm run test`","+  skips it instead of failing. Write the concurrency test as","+  `Promise.all([dispatchEmails(), dispatchEmails()])` over 10 seeded PENDING rows,","+  with `sendMail` mocked to count calls, and assert each id is sent exactly once.","+- Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`, covering the bell count after the admin","+  test button, mark-all-read and a persisted preference toggle."," ","-**Consequences.** The migration has no destructive steps. It adds indexes and","-nullable or defaulted columns only.","+No new test tooling."," ","-_Cites: FR-1, FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, NFR-9_","+**Consequences.** CI must set `TEST_DATABASE_URL` for NFR-15 to actually run.","+Dev-planning should note this, because a green `npm run test` without it proves nothing about locking."," ","-## ADR-10: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; no new test tooling","+_Cites: NFR-13, NFR-14, NFR-15, NFR-16, AC-4_"," ","-**Decision.** Run unit and integration tests (FR-36) in `vitest`, calling the","-limiter, tokens, policy and callbackUrl modules as pure functions. Test the","-authorize function and the service functions against the test DB. Use","-`@playwright/test` (with the installed `@axe-core/playwright` for NFR-5) for","-sign-in/out, the failure message and forgot→reset. The reset link comes from","-the logged `sendAuthEmail` output (FR-22).","+## ADR-10: Link validation and field limits as shared pure helpers; validate in notify() without throwing"," ","-_Cites: FR-22, FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10_","+**Context.** NFR-6 covers open-redirect-safe links, NFR-18 the title/body limits and","+FR-11 says notify() never throws.","+","+**Decision.** Add `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` to `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`.","+It returns true only when the string starts with `/`, the second character is not `/` or `\\`, the","+string contains no `\\`, and it has no control characters. It's shared by notify(), the zod schemas and","+the bell's `router.push`. In notify(), an unsafe link is dropped (stored as `null`)","+with `logger.warn`, and title/body are truncated to 140/500 characters with `logger.warn`","+(the intake default). The whole notify() body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`.","+","+**Consequences.** A bad link degrades to a notification that can't be clicked, never","+an exception in the caller's flow. A single regex-free function is trivially unit-tested (NFR-14).","+","+_Cites: FR-6, FR-11, NFR-6, NFR-14, NFR-18_","+","+---","+","+### Notes for downstream sub-tasks","+- **Intake blocker FR-4/FR-16 (confirmed).** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the","+  invite/password-reset template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly,","+  with no Notification row and no preference lookup. The `account.*` types are","+  `emailOnly` + `hidden`. The signature and both callers (users.ts:396, auth.ts:54) stay unchanged.","+- **NFR-1/FR-10 budget.** notify() makes 1 query each for users, preferences and","+  parent links where relevant, then 1 `createMany` for notifications and 1 for outbox","+  rows. That's within the limit of 3 round-trips each. Render once (ADR-6).","+- **No new dependencies anywhere in this PRD.**"]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: abcd-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nBase stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%, confirmed by\n`package.json`): Next.js 14.2 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict,\nPrisma 5.20 / PostgreSQL, MUI v9 + emotion, zod 3, react-hook-form,\ndate-fns-tz. The auth dependencies are already installed: `next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25`\nand `bcrypt ^6`. **This PRD adds no new runtime dependency.** The ADRs below\nonly cover the implementation choices this PRD's requirements force.\n\nBrownfield facts checked in the workspace (they correct intake in places):\n- `requireRole()` is sync and returns `{id, role}`. It has **50 call sites in\n  43 files**, not ~94. Every caller is already inside an `async` server page,\n  layout or route handler.\n- `src/server/http.ts` `ApiErrorCode` already includes `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401,\n  `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429 and `INVALID_TOKEN` 410, so no envelope\n  changes are needed.\n- `AuditLog.ip String?` exists. `audit()` has no `request` param.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js v5 with a split config (edge-safe `auth.config.ts` + Node `auth.ts`)\n\n**Context.** FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12 and FR-34 need credential sign-in, JWT\nsessions and a `middleware.ts` gate. In Next 14, middleware runs on the Edge\nruntime, where `bcrypt` (a native addon) and Prisma's Node client can't load.\n\n**Decision.** Use the documented Auth.js v5 split:\n- `src/server/auth/auth.config.ts` (edge-safe): `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`,\n  `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, the `authorized`/`jwt`/`session` shape\n  callbacks, and no providers that touch the DB.\n- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })] })`,\n  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut }`. It also holds the\n  DB-touching `jwt` callback logic (FR-11).\n- `middleware.ts` builds `NextAuth(authConfig).auth`. It only decodes the JWT.\n- `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` re-exports `handlers` (FR-34).\n\nDon't use a Prisma adapter. JWT sessions with Credentials don't need one, and\nthe adapter would require Account/Session/VerificationToken models the PRD\ndoesn't define.\n\n**Consequences.** Middleware can't check `passwordChangedAt` because it has no\nDB access. That check lives in the Node-side `jwt` callback (ADR-4), which\nruns whenever `auth()` is called from server code. Because next-auth is a\nbeta, pin the installed version exactly (drop the `^`) so a beta bump can't\nchange callback signatures mid-PRD.\n\n_Cites: FR-3, FR-4, FR-10, FR-12, FR-34, NFR-2_\n\n## ADR-2: `requireRole()` / `requireUser()` become async; update all 50 call sites with `await`\n\n**Context.** FR-28 and FR-29 replace `PLACEHOLDER_USER` with the real session.\nAuth.js `auth()` is async. Intake flagged this as a blocker. Options:\n(a) make the helpers async and add `await` at each call site;\n(b) keep them sync by reading identity from headers set by middleware;\n(c) use React `cache()` plus a sync wrapper.\n\n**Decision.** (a). `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole(...roles)`\nbecome `async` with the same arguments and the same `{id, role, ...}` return\nshape, so the signature stays compatible (FR-29). Each of the 50 call sites\nchanges from `requireRole(...)` to `await requireRole(...)`. That's a\nmechanical one-token edit, and every caller is already async. Wrap\n`getCurrentUser` in React `cache()` so a page plus its layout share one\nsession decode per request.\n\nOption (b) was rejected: identity read from headers is a spoofing risk\n(NFR-7), and it skips the FR-11 revocation check. Option (c) can't make an\nasync read sync.\n\n**Consequences.** `tsc` catches every missed `await`, because a `Promise` has\nno `.role` or `.id`. Bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statements don't fail\ntypecheck, though, and a forgotten `await` there silently does nothing.\nEnable `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises` for `src/**`, or have\ndev-planning grep for un-awaited calls. Redirect-vs-throw: in server pages,\nuse `redirect('/login')` / `redirect('/forbidden')` from `next/navigation`;\nin route handlers, throw `AppError` (UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN), which\n`withHandler` already maps. Implement this as one helper that the page and\nAPI paths both call, not two copies. `course-access.ts` and\n`student-access.ts` keep taking the resolved user object and aren't modified\n(NFR-9).\n\n_Cites: FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9_\n\n## ADR-3: Password hashing with the existing `bcrypt` at cost 12, plus a dummy compare for unknown users\n\n**Context.** FR-4 sets cost 12. NFR-3 requires constant-ish timing when the\nuser doesn't exist. NFR-4 requires sign-in in under 1 s at p95.\n\n**Decision.** Use `bcrypt.hash(pw, 12)` / `bcrypt.compare`. Precompute one\nmodule-level dummy hash at cost 12 and compare against it when the user is\nmissing, disabled or locked, so every path pays one bcrypt compare. Don't use\nargon2 (it's a new native dependency and the PRD specifies bcrypt).\n\n**Consequences.** One cost-12 compare takes about 250 ms on modern hardware,\nwhich leaves room under the 1 s budget for the user lookup, the\nfailedLoginCount update and the audit insert. Never call bcrypt twice on one\nsign-in path. bcrypt runs only in Node code, never in middleware (ADR-1).\n\n_Cites: FR-4, FR-6, NFR-3, NFR-4_\n\n## ADR-4: Session revocation via a `passwordChangedAt` check in the jwt callback, throttled to every 5 minutes\n\n**Context.** FR-11 and FR-23 require that a password change or reset\ninvalidates other sessions. Sessions are stateless JWTs (FR-10), so there's\nno session table.\n\n**Decision.** Store `iat` and a `checkedAt` timestamp in the token. In the\nNode `jwt` callback, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, select only\n`passwordChangedAt, status` for `token.id`. If `passwordChangedAt > iat` or\nthe status isn't ACTIVE, return `null` to invalidate the session. Otherwise\nupdate `checkedAt`. For FR-23's \"re-issue current session\", call `unstable_update()`\n(the v5 `update`) after the change, which mints a token with a fresh `iat`.\n\n**Consequences.** Revocation can lag by up to 5 minutes. The PRD explicitly\naccepts that window. Edge middleware can still let a revoked token through\nfor page navigation in that window. The server-side `requireUser()` call\nthen catches it, and that call is the real guard (NFR-7).\n\n_Cites: FR-10, FR-11, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-7_\n\n## ADR-5: Tokens with `node:crypto` only (randomBytes, SHA-256, timingSafeEqual)\n\n**Context.** FR-13 needs a single AuthToken module. NFR-1 requires stored\nhashes and constant-time comparison.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` uses `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`\nand `createHash('sha256')`. Look up by the hash (the DB index), then confirm\nwith `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers. No JWT, nanoid or other library.\n\n**Consequences.** Raw tokens exist only in the returned value and the\nemailed or logged link, never in the DB or audit metadata (FR-31). The\n\"invalidate older unused tokens\" step (FR-20, FR-26) is one `updateMany`\nthat sets `usedAt` in the same `$transaction` as the create.\n\n_Cites: FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1_\n\n## ADR-6: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter (a `Map` of timestamp arrays); no Redis\n\n**Context.** FR-7 (10 per IP per 5 min) and FR-19 (3 per email per hour, 10\nper IP per hour) explicitly ask for an exported in-memory limiter in\n`src/server/rate-limit.ts`. The PRD adds no infrastructure (NFR-11).\n\n**Decision.** One `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs): { ok, retryAfterMs }`\nover a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`, pruning expired timestamps on\neach call. Namespace keys like `login:ip:<ip>` and `forgot:email:<email>`.\nTake the IP from the first entry of `x-forwarded-for`, using the same\nhelper `audit()` uses (FR-30). Call it from the Node side (authorize and\nroute handlers), not middleware, because Edge isolates don't share memory.\n\n**Consequences.** The ceiling is per process: limits reset on restart and\naren't shared across instances. Mark the code with a\n`ponytail: per-process limiter, swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if\nhorizontally scaled` comment. With Credentials, a RATE_LIMITED outcome has\nto go through Auth.js's `CredentialsSignin` subclass `code` to reach the\nlogin form (FR-5, FR-7).\n\n_Cites: FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-8, NFR-11_\n\n## ADR-7: Validation with the existing zod + react-hook-form; one policy schema shared by client and server\n\n**Context.** FR-17 defines the policy. FR-18 needs a live checklist.\nFR-16, FR-21 and FR-23 must enforce the policy server-side.\n\n**Decision.** `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports the zod schema plus a\npure `passwordChecks(pw, email)` that returns per-rule booleans. The\nchecklist UI and the zod `superRefine` both use that function. The\ncommon-password check needs the file at\n`src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt`, so it runs only on the server: read\nthe file once into a `Set` with `fs` in a server-only module. The client\nchecklist shows the length, letter, digit and not-email rules live, and the\ncommon-password rule is reported from the server response.\n\n**Consequences.** The 1,000-word list never ships in the client bundle. The\nvalidator file has to stay importable from the client, so keep the `fs`\nread in a separate server-only file that adds the common-password refinement.\n\n_Cites: FR-17, FR-18, FR-16, FR-21, FR-23, NFR-5, NFR-8_\n\n## ADR-8: UI with MUI v9 only (Sign-in template patterns), documented through mui-mcp\n\n**Context.** NFR-6 bans non-MUI UI libraries and requires every component to\nbe looked up through mui-mcp. FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24 and FR-32 add auth\npages and top-bar changes.\n\n**Decision.** Use the installed `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` 9.5:\nCard, TextField, Button, InputAdornment + IconButton (Visibility icons),\nAlert, List/ListItemIcon for the checklist, and Menu/Avatar/Chip in the top\nbar. Use the existing `useToast` for toasts (FR-21, FR-23), not notistack or\nsonner. Auth pages live in a `src/app/(auth)` route group outside the\n`(app)` shell. The mui-mcp server was reachable from this session\n(`useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools were listed), so the NFR-6 blocker doesn't\nstand at architect time. Dev must still check it itself.\n\n**Consequences.** No new UI dependency. `aria-live=\"polite\"` on the form-level\nAlert and focus-first-invalid (via react-hook-form `setFocus`) meet NFR-5.\n\n_Cites: FR-3, FR-15, FR-18, FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-5, NFR-6_\n\n## ADR-9: Schema reconciled additively with one Prisma migration\n\n**Context.** FR-1 and the intake blockers list the divergences: `ip` vs\n`ipAddress`, the extra `ARCHIVED` value, different AuditLog indexes. NFR-9\nsays never rename.\n\n**Decision.** Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED` and keep the\nexisting extra indexes. Add only\n`@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to\nAuditLog, plus any User auth fields the diff finds missing\n(failedLoginCount, lockedUntil, lastLoginAt, passwordChangedAt). Apply them\nin one `prisma migrate dev --name auth_reconcile` migration. FR-4's \"status\n!= ACTIVE\" check already rejects ARCHIVED.\n\n**Consequences.** The migration has no destructive steps. It adds indexes and\nnullable or defaulted columns only.\n\n_Cites: FR-1, FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, NFR-9_\n\n## ADR-10: Tests with the existing Vitest + Playwright; no new test tooling\n\n**Decision.** Run unit and integration tests (FR-36) in `vitest`, calling the\nlimiter, tokens, policy and callbackUrl modules as pure functions. Test the\nauthorize function and the service functions against the test DB. Use\n`@playwright/test` (with the installed `@axe-core/playwright` for NFR-5) for\nsign-in/out, the failure message and forgot→reset. The reset link comes from\nthe logged `sendAuthEmail` output (FR-22).\n\n_Cites: FR-22, FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10_\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RwB3yngx9GbhXnpwL3BAm7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
