{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTU3eXUyfzVGSg9UhXT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-4 (arch-research-stack). The detected stack fits every requirement, so it records 10 decisions and adds no new dependencies. Every FR/NFR/AC id it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**The decisions:**\n1. **Migration:** one additive Prisma migration (`notifications_email`) creates the three tables that are already in the schema, keeping the extra `updatedAt` columns.\n2. **Type registry:** `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a typed constant, and `notify()` only accepts its keys, so TypeScript rejects unknown types.\n3. **No double sends:** the dispatcher claims emails with a single raw SQL statement that uses `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, so two dispatchers can't grab the same row.\n4. **Retries:** the 1/5/15/60/240-minute backoff is a pure lookup table, easy to unit test.\n5. **Email transport:** a simple `if` on `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` picks Nodemailer SMTP or the console logger. Every email gets HTML and text parts plus the `List-Unsubscribe` header.\n6. **Templates:** emails are rendered when they're queued, inside the request, not when they're sent. `generic-notification` is rendered once per `notify()` call so 1,000 recipients stays under 2 seconds.\n7. **Background sending:** the cron route checks the bearer token with a constant-time compare and always returns 401 if `CRON_SECRET` is unset. The worker script is a 15-second loop. The daily purge tracks its last run in memory.\n8. **UI:** MUI only, with plain `fetch` polling (no SWR or React Query) and `Badge max={9}` for the \"9+\". The email log reuses the existing `DataTable` component.\n9. **Tests:** integration tests go in `tests/integration` and only run when `TEST_DATABASE_URL` is set, so `npm run test` still passes on machines without a database.\n10. **Links and field limits:** one shared check rejects unsafe links (`//`, backslashes). `notify()` drops bad links and truncates long text with a warning instead of throwing.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Intake's open question, settled:** `sendAuthEmail()` adds the outbox row directly, with no in-app notification. The `account.*` types are email-only and hidden from the preferences page. Intake asked the architect to confirm this.\n- **Missed timestamp:** Prisma's `@updatedAt` doesn't update on raw SQL writes. The claim statement must set `\"updatedAt\" = now()` itself, or the recovery of emails stuck in SENDING won't work.\n- **Async render:** `@react-email/render` 1.0.1's `render()` returns a Promise, so every call must be awaited.\n- **mui-mcp is reachable** from this session, so intake's UI blocker doesn't apply yet. The dev phase still has to check it.\n- **Stale files:** the other files in `artifacts/architect/` are left over from an earlier ticket (abcd-1). I didn't touch them because they belong to other sub-tasks, and those sub-tasks will overwrite them for SH-4."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":57955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ba1665-ff77-440a-aa0d-eea7f83f9b17","uuid":"3cf013ae-7864-4c17-9689-a106621e7aa3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:00:53.388Z","request_id":"req_011CghTU3Qszzyq1HgW2soJD"}
