{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDFFwUJGZ6NtqDHAgn5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-6 (status: complete). It has seven decision records, and every requirement ID it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**What it decides:**\n- **One new dependency:** `@dnd-kit/core` pinned at exactly `6.3.1`, which works with the project's React 18.3.1. `@dnd-kit/sortable` isn't needed because periods are reordered with up/down buttons. A period's position must be unique in the database, so the reorder writes in two steps inside one transaction.\n- **Times:** stored as zero-padded `'HH:MM'` strings and compared directly as strings. \"Now\" and today's weekday come from the existing `formatInSchoolTz` helper using the school's timezone setting. Nothing new is added for dates.\n- **Concurrent edits:** the clash check and the slot write run in one strict (serializable) database transaction, retried up to 3 times when two requests collide. The clash checks must read through that same transaction, or two clashing requests could both get saved.\n- **Clash detection:** the four clash rules are pure functions fed by a few batched database queries. The availability map makes a fixed number of queries, not one per grid cell, so it should stay inside the 300 ms and 400 ms targets.\n- **Drag-and-drop grid:** the grid only changes after the server accepts a drop, so a rejected drop \"snaps back\" with no rollback code. Keyboard users get a \"Place course\" dialog instead of dnd-kit's built-in keyboard support.\n- **Printing and tests:** printing uses the browser's own print layout with no library. Tests stay on the existing Vitest and Playwright setup.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The `artifacts/architect/` folder still holds files from SH-4. I only overwrote my own file. `system-design.md`, `api-contracts.json` and the hand-off file will be replaced when the later architect steps run.\n- The UI-docs server (mui-mcp) is connected right now, so that intake blocker is clear for the moment. Dev still has to look up each component there before using it.\n- I left two of intake's open questions to the design step, with notes on both: how admins find free rooms for a slot, and how the screen gets the slot count before a teaching day is turned off."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5745,"cache_read_input_tokens":44438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5745},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7632dfff-c76a-42bd-90d4-6365368b057b","uuid":"de5ab70f-0438-4637-9238-7a9aa69348cc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:34.931Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDFFXAhCfU1gwjFqMHD"}
