{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKcDkYPUiTpZ6quaaAD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-1, overwriting an old copy left from ticket SH-6. It holds seven decisions (ADR-1 to ADR-7), and every requirement id it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\nThe main conclusion is that **SH-1 needs no new dependency**. The current stack (Next.js 14, next-auth 5 beta.25, Prisma, MUI 9.5) already has every backend piece this ticket uses, so the decisions only cover what's missing:\n\n- **Login form (ADR-2):** the form signs in from the browser and checks the error code that comes back. `locked:N`, `disabled` and `rate_limited` each get their own message; any other failure shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" A small function does this mapping, and a unit test covers it.\n- **Shell (ADR-3):** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` gets the signed-in user on the server and passes it to the shell. That removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` without adding a second \"current user\" source on the client (FR-25).\n- **Invite and reset pages (ADR-4):** the page checks the link before showing the form, so an expired link never shows it. The forms post to the existing API routes, so no new routes are needed. After accepting an invite, the user is signed in with the new password and sent to `/dashboard`.\n- **Seed (ADR-5):** six active users are created or updated safely on each run. The invited user's link goes to the logger; `sendAuthEmail` is not changed.\n- **Database (ADR-6):** one new migration adds the missing `role, status` index on User. The audit log's `ip` column keeps its name.\n- **Tests (ADR-7):** one integration test file for sign-in and the three password flows, and one Playwright file that runs its tests in order. The forgot → reset test reads the reset link from the outgoing email table, so the app doesn't need a test-only route.\n\nThe intake blockers are listed under \"Downstream notes\" in the file for `arch-design-system` to include in its Overview. Keeping the `ip` column name (FR-32) still needs a person to sign off.\n\nThe other files in `artifacts/architect/` are also left from SH-6. The other three sub-tasks will overwrite them; I didn't touch them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":58011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":528},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9ff751b-b713-4810-9c30-1cad791c6970","uuid":"0397bcc6-fb1c-4aec-9f2a-86ea0342e843","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:38:58.523Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKcDYdqsaLaEoyJsVb6"}
