{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk6VMNUhv3B42hy7Mrnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The earlier ADR is stale: /login, the seed users, the index migration and a reusable SetPasswordForm now exist. I'm rewriting tech-stack-decisions.md to match.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":47929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bd6c0dc-83dd-43e6-ae41-e48cadc78ecd","uuid":"1b7209ae-420e-4a36-881a-d7fc2420fd4b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:27:27.472Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk6VMAZwhkjUb7RgGdfD","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":25,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk6VMNUhv3B42hy7Mrnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Jyp2gxjJQruQjGRiB6H622","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\nVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n\nThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\ncover only the remaining gaps.\n\n**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n\n- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\npiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\nor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\nthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\nneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\nfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\non success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\nFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\ntokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are\nadded. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.\n\n## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,\nand Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.\nNFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:\n  - seed admin signs in and signs out\n  - wrong-password message\n  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`\n  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)\n  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`\n\n  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the\nPlaywright process.\n\n## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept\n\n**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already\nmigrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.\n\n**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they\nare. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":47929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bd6c0dc-83dd-43e6-ae41-e48cadc78ecd","uuid":"d9d1f0af-097c-4c84-962c-039bb614573b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:27:58.613Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk6VMAZwhkjUb7RgGdfD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Jyp2gxjJQruQjGRiB6H622":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\nVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n\nThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\ncover only the remaining gaps.\n\n**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n\n- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\npiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\nor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\nthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\nneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\nfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\non success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\nFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\ntokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are\nadded. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.\n\n## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,\nand Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.\nNFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:\n  - seed admin signs in and signs out\n  - wrong-password message\n  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`\n  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)\n  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`\n\n  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the\nPlaywright process.\n\n## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept\n\n**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already\nmigrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.\n\n**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they\nare. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jyp2gxjJQruQjGRiB6H622","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bd6c0dc-83dd-43e6-ae41-e48cadc78ecd","uuid":"a110e7bb-209d-491d-aba0-44943cec9515","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:27:59.007Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\nVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n\nThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\ncover only the remaining gaps.\n\n**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n\n- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\npiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\nor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\nthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\nneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\nfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\non success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\nFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\ntokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are