human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":140,"newStart":1,"newLines":110,"lines":[" # Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)"," ","-Ticket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T11:45:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete"," "," **Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`"," confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,","-next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0,","-MUI 9.5.0 with emotion, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0.","-The stack fits every FR and NFR. **This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13). The ADRs below","-record only the choices the requirements force for the gaps intake listed: the auth pages, the shell","-wiring, the seed, the index migration and the tests.","+next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with","+@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,","+Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.","+**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13)."," ","-**Workspace facts I checked** (they confirm intake or add detail to it):","+This file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now","+cover only the remaining gaps."," ","-- `src/server/auth/credentials.ts`: `AuthError extends CredentialsSignin` and sets `.code` to one of `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited` or `locked:<N>`. A `DUMMY_HASH` compare runs on every path, so NFR-3 is already met.","-- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` exports `handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update`. `auth.config.ts` already sanitises redirects through `safeCallbackUrl` and sets `pages.signIn = '/login'`. The cookies are the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, `__Secure-` prefix in production (NFR-2).","-- **No `SessionProvider`, `useSession` or `next-auth/react` import exists anywhere in `src/`.** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component, and it renders the client `AppShell` from `shell.tsx`, which still contains `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).","-- `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`.","-- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `acceptInviteSchema`, `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES` and `safeCallbackUrl`. These cover every form.","-- `src/server/auth/email.ts` exports `authLink(kind, rawToken)`. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues to EmailOutbox and never logs the link.","-- `prisma/schema.prisma`: `AuditLog.ip String?`. `User` has `@@index([lastName, firstName, email])` and does not have `@@index([role, status])`. The latest migration is `20261105000000_timetable`.","-- Tests: the unit tests for tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy and auth-validators exist. `tests/integration/` has the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent `email-dispatch.test.ts`. `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec. `playwright.config.ts` runs `npm run start` against `APP_URL`.","-- The `mui-mcp` server is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear for now. Dev must still call it before writing UI.","+**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**"," ","+- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.","+- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.","+- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.","+- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).","+- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.","+- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.","+- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.","+- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.","+- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.","+"," ---"," "," ## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency"," ","-**Context.** NFR-13 requires no scope expansion and no rebuild of the existing auth modules. NFR-7 bans","-extra UI libraries. Every backend piece the gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12,","-FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).","+**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend","+piece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24)."," ","-**Decision.** Keep `package.json` as it is. Do not add an OTP/2FA library, a password-strength library","-such as zxcvbn, a form wizard, or a toast library. The strength checklist comes from the existing","-`passwordChecks()` and `PASSWORD_RULES` (FR-16). Toasts use the existing `useToast()` (NFR-6).","+**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard","+or session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use","+`useToast()` (NFR-6)."," ","-**Consequences.** The lockfile does not change. All new code is pages, shell wiring, the seed, one","-migration and tests.","+**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests."," ","-## ADR-2: Sign-in uses the client `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, with errors mapped from `result.code`","+## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`"," ","-**Context.** FR-2 requires a `/login` form that submits through Auth.js `signIn('credentials')`.","-FR-4 and FR-6 need the server's specific messages (locked N minutes, disabled, rate-limited) shown","-in an Alert. FR-7 requires the callbackUrl to be sanitised. NFR-5 requires aria-live errors and focus","-on the first invalid field. NFR-11 requires RHF with `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. NFR-2 requires CSRF.","+**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs","+the name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21","+needs an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement."," "," **Decision.**","-- `/login/page.tsx` is a Server Component that reads `searchParams` and renders a client `LoginForm`.","-- `LoginForm` calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`. In beta.25 the result carries `code` from `AuthError`. A small pure function, `loginErrorMessage(code)`, maps the codes. `locked:N` becomes \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" `disabled` becomes the disabled message. `rate_limited` becomes \"Too many attempts…\". Every other code becomes \"Email or password is incorrect.\" (FR-4, FR-6). Keep the function in the form file and export it for a unit test.","-- On success, call `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(searchParams.callbackUrl))` and then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The function already exists, and the server `redirect` callback enforces the same rule a second time.","-- The client `signIn` fetches the Auth.js CSRF token itself (NFR-2). There is no hand-rolled CSRF.","-- Do **not** use a Server Action with the server `signIn`. In beta.25 that throws `CredentialsSignin` through `redirect` plumbing, and the error is harder to surface. The client path is the documented way to show credential errors.","+- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.","+- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.","+- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25."," ","-**Consequences.** `next-auth/react` is part of the installed `next-auth`, so nothing is added. The client","-call does not need a `SessionProvider`, because `signIn` and `signOut` from `next-auth/react` work","-without one.","+**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness","+follows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session."," ","-## ADR-3: The shell gets the current user from the server `auth()` through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`","+## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs"," ","-**Context.** FR-25 says to delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keep exactly one source of \"current user\".","-FR-26 needs the name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the","-session role. NFR-9 requires server enforcement. `getCurrentUser()` / `requirePageUser()` already exist (FR-23).","+**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;","+on success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.","+FR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say","+tokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema."," "," **Decision.**","-- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (already an async Server Component) calls `requirePageUser()`, which redirects to `/login` when there is no session. The middleware already handles that case (FR-11), so this is a second guard. The layout passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`.","-- `AppShell` takes a `user` prop, uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and shows initials, the name and a role `Chip`. Its menu has an \"Account security\" `MenuItem` that links to `/account/security` (FR-21) and a \"Sign out\" item that calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react` (FR-26).","-- Do **not** add a `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would create a second \"current user\" source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.","+- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).","+- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.","+  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.","+  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).","+- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.","+- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).","+- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed."," ","-**Consequences.** The user is read once per navigation on the server, where a JWT decode costs almost","-nothing. Role or name changes appear after the next 5-minute recheck (FR-10), which is the same","-freshness the JWT already has. Any shell test has to pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.","+**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are","+added. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form."," ","-## ADR-4: The token pages verify on the server first; set-password forms are client RHF forms that post to the existing JSON APIs","+## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox"," ","-**Context.** FR-13 says `/invite/[token]` must show the invalid-link message, or the name and email","-read-only. FR-14 says that after acceptance the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19","-covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login` with a success toast. FR-20 covers `/account/security`","-→ \"Password updated\", or a field error on a wrong current password. FR-17 covers `/forgot-password`","-with a constant message. FR-12 and NFR-1 say tokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers.","+**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,","+and Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.","+NFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green."," "," **Decision.**","-- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts` without consuming the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link Alert. Otherwise they render a client form with the user's email (and name, for invites). The raw token is passed only as a prop. It is never logged and never put in audit metadata (NFR-8).","-- Forms use RHF with `zodResolver(setPasswordSchema(email))` or `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, so client and server share one schema (NFR-11). They `fetch` the existing routes: `POST /api/auth/accept-invite`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/forgot-password` and `/api/account/password`. Server `VALIDATION_ERROR` `details` are mapped back with `setError` (FR-20 \"Current password is incorrect.\").","-- Invite success: call `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service already consumed the token, so a later visit shows the invalid-link message.","-- Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `LoginForm` shows `useToast` \"Password updated, sign in with your new password\" once on mount when `reset=1` is present (FR-19).","-- `/forgot-password` always shows the same success Alert after any 2xx or 429 response, so there is no enumeration (FR-17).","-- One shared client component, `PasswordChecklist({ password, email })`, renders `PASSWORD_RULES` as an MUI `List` with CheckCircle and RadioButtonUnchecked icons plus text. Colour is never the only signal. It is used under every new-password field (FR-16).","-- Accessibility: one `Alert role=\"alert\"` / `aria-live=\"polite\"` region per form. Field helperText comes from RHF. RHF's default `shouldFocusError: true` moves focus to the first invalid field (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.","+- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.","+- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:","+  - seed admin signs in and signs out","+  - wrong-password message","+  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`","+  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)","+  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`"," ","-**Consequences.** No new API routes and no new services. Only pages and client forms are added.","-Verifying the token on the server before render means that an expired link never shows the form.","+  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed."," ","-## ADR-5: Seed users are upserted with bcrypt cost 12; the invite link is logged through the logger","+**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the","+Playwright process."," ","-**Context.** FR-28 requires six ACTIVE users with password `SchoolHub123!`, created idempotently. FR-29","-and FR-30 require one INVITED user whose invite link is logged. FR-31 says not to change `sendAuthEmail`.","-NFR-12 bans `console.log`.","+## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept"," ","-**Decision.**","-- In `prisma/seed.ts`, add a users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notification block, which skips users that don't exist. Hash once with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`. Then call `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email }, create: {..., status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for each user. `update: {}` keeps re-runs idempotent and leaves edited users alone.","-- `invited@schoolhub.test`: upsert with `status: 'INVITED'` and `passwordHash: null`. Then call `createInviteToken(user.id)` from `services/users.ts` (it invalidates older invites) and `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. Call these only while the user is still INVITED. Do not call `sendAuthEmail`.","+**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already","+migrated. NFR-13 forbids renames."," ","-**Consequences.** Each re-seed issues a fresh invite link and invalidates the previous one, which is the","-expected dev behaviour. The bcrypt hash adds about 250 ms to the seed run.","+**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they","+are. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off."," ","-## ADR-6: Add `@@index([role, status])` in a new additive migration; keep `AuditLog.ip`","+**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration."," ","-**Context.** FR-33 says the PRD's User model declares `@@index([role, status])`. FR-32 says not to rename","-existing fields, so `ip` stays. NFR-13 requires no renames.","-","-**Decision.** Add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`, and generate","-`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/` with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`.","-It contains a single `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` does not change. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.","-","-**Consequences.** The migration is additive and does not touch existing data. Use a migration","-timestamp later than `20261105000000_timetable`.","-","-## ADR-7: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox","-","-**Context.** FR-34 asks for integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and","-change-password, plus Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset.","-NFR-5 covers accessibility. NFR-13 requires `lint`, `typecheck` and `test` to stay green.","-","-**Decision.**","-- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, the same as `email-dispatch.test.ts`. It calls `authorizeCredentials` and the services directly with a stub `Request`, covering each branch (invalid, disabled, locked:N, lockout at 5, rate_limited, success resets the count) and each service's happy path and token reuse. Call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`.","-- `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`: covers the `loginErrorMessage` code map from ADR-2.","-- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: covers sign-in as the seed admin, sign-out, the wrong-password message, and the redirect for an unauthenticated `/dashboard`. For forgot → reset, the spec reads the newest `EmailOutbox` row for the address through `@prisma/client` in the test process and extracts the `/reset-password/…` URL from the body. That way it needs no test-only API route in the app. Run `@axe-core/playwright` `AxeBuilder` once on `/login` (NFR-5).","-","-**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed (ADR-5) and on `DATABASE_URL`","-being visible to the Playwright process. Because the specs change shared users (password reset,","-lockout), mark `auth.spec.ts` as `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`. The","-reset flow should use `student2@` so that admin sign-in in parallel specs is not affected.","-"," ---"," "," ## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`"," ","-- Intake blockers that system-design must surface: the brownfield \"design gaps only\" rule, FR-32 (`ip`, LOW confidence), FR-33 (additive index), FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link, `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is) and NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory).","-- No new API endpoints are implied. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.","-- Do not modify `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).","+- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).","+- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.","+- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.","+- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13)."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T11:45:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0,\nMUI 9.5.0 with emotion, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0.\nThe stack fits every FR and NFR. **This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13). The ADRs below\nrecord only the choices the requirements force for the gaps intake listed: the auth pages, the shell\nwiring, the seed, the index migration and the tests.\n\n**Workspace facts I checked** (they confirm intake or add detail to it):\n\n- `src/server/auth/credentials.ts`: `AuthError extends CredentialsSignin` and sets `.code` to one of `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited` or `locked:<N>`. A `DUMMY_HASH` compare runs on every path, so NFR-3 is already met.\n- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` exports `handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update`. `auth.config.ts` already sanitises redirects through `safeCallbackUrl` and sets `pages.signIn = '/login'`. The cookies are the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, `__Secure-` prefix in production (NFR-2).\n- **No `SessionProvider`, `useSession` or `next-auth/react` import exists anywhere in `src/`.** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component, and it renders the client `AppShell` from `shell.tsx`, which still contains `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`.\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `acceptInviteSchema`, `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES` and `safeCallbackUrl`. These cover every form.\n- `src/server/auth/email.ts` exports `authLink(kind, rawToken)`. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues to EmailOutbox and never logs the link.\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: `AuditLog.ip String?`. `User` has `@@index([lastName, firstName, email])` and does not have `@@index([role, status])`. The latest migration is `20261105000000_timetable`.\n- Tests: the unit tests for tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy and auth-validators exist. `tests/integration/` has the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent `email-dispatch.test.ts`. `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec. `playwright.config.ts` runs `npm run start` against `APP_URL`.\n- The `mui-mcp` server is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear for now. Dev must still call it before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 requires no scope expansion and no rebuild of the existing auth modules. NFR-7 bans\nextra UI libraries. Every backend piece the gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12,\nFR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` as it is. Do not add an OTP/2FA library, a password-strength library\nsuch as zxcvbn, a form wizard, or a toast library. The strength checklist comes from the existing\n`passwordChecks()` and `PASSWORD_RULES` (FR-16). Toasts use the existing `useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** The lockfile does not change. All new code is pages, shell wiring, the seed, one\nmigration and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: Sign-in uses the client `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, with errors mapped from `result.code`\n\n**Context.** FR-2 requires a `/login` form that submits through Auth.js `signIn('credentials')`.\nFR-4 and FR-6 need the server's specific messages (locked N minutes, disabled, rate-limited) shown\nin an Alert. FR-7 requires the callbackUrl to be sanitised. NFR-5 requires aria-live errors and focus\non the first invalid field. NFR-11 requires RHF with `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. NFR-2 requires CSRF.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `/login/page.tsx` is a Server Component that reads `searchParams` and renders a client `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm` calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`. In beta.25 the result carries `code` from `AuthError`. A small pure function, `loginErrorMessage(code)`, maps the codes. `locked:N` becomes \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" `disabled` becomes the disabled message. `rate_limited` becomes \"Too many attempts…\". Every other code becomes \"Email or password is incorrect.\" (FR-4, FR-6). Keep the function in the form file and export it for a unit test.\n- On success, call `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(searchParams.callbackUrl))` and then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The function already exists, and the server `redirect` callback enforces the same rule a second time.\n- The client `signIn` fetches the Auth.js CSRF token itself (NFR-2). There is no hand-rolled CSRF.\n- Do **not** use a Server Action with the server `signIn`. In beta.25 that throws `CredentialsSignin` through `redirect` plumbing, and the error is harder to surface. The client path is the documented way to show credential errors.\n\n**Consequences.** `next-auth/react` is part of the installed `next-auth`, so nothing is added. The client\ncall does not need a `SessionProvider`, because `signIn` and `signOut` from `next-auth/react` work\nwithout one.\n\n## ADR-3: The shell gets the current user from the server `auth()` through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 says to delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keep exactly one source of \"current user\".\nFR-26 needs the name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the\nsession role. NFR-9 requires server enforcement. `getCurrentUser()` / `requirePageUser()` already exist (FR-23).\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (already an async Server Component) calls `requirePageUser()`, which redirects to `/login` when there is no session. The middleware already handles that case (FR-11), so this is a second guard. The layout passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes a `user` prop, uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and shows initials, the name and a role `Chip`. Its menu has an \"Account security\" `MenuItem` that links to `/account/security` (FR-21) and a \"Sign out\" item that calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react` (FR-26).\n- Do **not** add a `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would create a second \"current user\" source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** The user is read once per navigation on the server, where a JWT decode costs almost\nnothing. Role or name changes appear after the next 5-minute recheck (FR-10), which is the same\nfreshness the JWT already has. Any shell test has to pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-4: The token pages verify on the server first; set-password forms are client RHF forms that post to the existing JSON APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says `/invite/[token]` must show the invalid-link message, or the name and email\nread-only. FR-14 says that after acceptance the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19\ncovers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login` with a success toast. FR-20 covers `/account/security`\n→ \"Password updated\", or a field error on a wrong current password. FR-17 covers `/forgot-password`\nwith a constant message. FR-12 and NFR-1 say tokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts` without consuming the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link Alert. Otherwise they render a client form with the user's email (and name, for invites). The raw token is passed only as a prop. It is never logged and never put in audit metadata (NFR-8).\n- Forms use RHF with `zodResolver(setPasswordSchema(email))` or `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, so client and server share one schema (NFR-11). They `fetch` the existing routes: `POST /api/auth/accept-invite`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/forgot-password` and `/api/account/password`. Server `VALIDATION_ERROR` `details` are mapped back with `setError` (FR-20 \"Current password is incorrect.\").\n- Invite success: call `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service already consumed the token, so a later visit shows the invalid-link message.\n- Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `LoginForm` shows `useToast` \"Password updated, sign in with your new password\" once on mount when `reset=1` is present (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` always shows the same success Alert after any 2xx or 429 response, so there is no enumeration (FR-17).\n- One shared client component, `PasswordChecklist({ password, email })`, renders `PASSWORD_RULES` as an MUI `List` with CheckCircle and RadioButtonUnchecked icons plus text. Colour is never the only signal. It is used under every new-password field (FR-16).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert role=\"alert\"` / `aria-live=\"polite\"` region per form. Field helperText comes from RHF. RHF's default `shouldFocusError: true` moves focus to the first invalid field (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes and no new services. Only pages and client forms are added.\nVerifying the token on the server before render means that an expired link never shows the form.\n\n## ADR-5: Seed users are upserted with bcrypt cost 12; the invite link is logged through the logger\n\n**Context.** FR-28 requires six ACTIVE users with password `SchoolHub123!`, created idempotently. FR-29\nand FR-30 require one INVITED user whose invite link is logged. FR-31 says not to change `sendAuthEmail`.\nNFR-12 bans `console.log`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- In `prisma/seed.ts`, add a users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notification block, which skips users that don't exist. Hash once with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`. Then call `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email }, create: {..., status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for each user. `update: {}` keeps re-runs idempotent and leaves edited users alone.\n- `invited@schoolhub.test`: upsert with `status: 'INVITED'` and `passwordHash: null`. Then call `createInviteToken(user.id)` from `services/users.ts` (it invalidates older invites) and `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. Call these only while the user is still INVITED. Do not call `sendAuthEmail`.\n\n**Consequences.** Each re-seed issues a fresh invite link and invalidates the previous one, which is the\nexpected dev behaviour. The bcrypt hash adds about 250 ms to the seed run.\n\n## ADR-6: Add `@@index([role, status])` in a new additive migration; keep `AuditLog.ip`\n\n**Context.** FR-33 says the PRD's User model declares `@@index([role, status])`. FR-32 says not to rename\nexisting fields, so `ip` stays. NFR-13 requires no renames.\n\n**Decision.** Add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`, and generate\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/` with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`.\nIt contains a single `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` does not change. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** The migration is additive and does not touch existing data. Use a migration\ntimestamp later than `20261105000000_timetable`.\n\n## ADR-7: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 asks for integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and\nchange-password, plus Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset.\nNFR-5 covers accessibility. NFR-13 requires `lint`, `typecheck` and `test` to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, the same as `email-dispatch.test.ts`. It calls `authorizeCredentials` and the services directly with a stub `Request`, covering each branch (invalid, disabled, locked:N, lockout at 5, rate_limited, success resets the count) and each service's happy path and token reuse. Call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`: covers the `loginErrorMessage` code map from ADR-2.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: covers sign-in as the seed admin, sign-out, the wrong-password message, and the redirect for an unauthenticated `/dashboard`. For forgot → reset, the spec reads the newest `EmailOutbox` row for the address through `@prisma/client` in the test process and extracts the `/reset-password/…` URL from the body. That way it needs no test-only API route in the app. Run `@axe-core/playwright` `AxeBuilder` once on `/login` (NFR-5).\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed (ADR-5) and on `DATABASE_URL`\nbeing visible to the Playwright process. Because the specs change shared users (password reset,\nlockout), mark `auth.spec.ts` as `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`. The\nreset flow should use `student2@` so that admin sign-in in parallel specs is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Intake blockers that system-design must surface: the brownfield \"design gaps only\" rule, FR-32 (`ip`, LOW confidence), FR-33 (additive index), FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link, `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is) and NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory).\n- No new API endpoints are implied. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not modify `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Jyp2gxjJQruQjGRiB6H622","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
