ceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL`\n\n`SchoolSettings` gains an `AttendanceMode` enum column `attendanceMode` (default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. `date` is stored as `@db.Date`.\n\n**Consequences.** `prisma db push` and any schema drift check will not see these SQL objects, so tests must run `prisma migrate reset`/`deploy` and must not use `db push`. The service also checks the one-of rule (FR-2), so callers get a clean `VALIDATION_ERROR` before the database rejects the row. Prisma cannot `upsert` on a partial index (see ADR-3).\n\nDrivers: FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-40, NFR-8.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Save a register in one interactive transaction that only writes changed rows\n\n**Context.** FR-14 requires an atomic create-or-update of the session and all its records. NFR-1 requires a 35-student save to finish in under 500 ms. FR-18 requires an audit entry for each changed status, and FR-21/22 need the previous status to detect changes. A partial unique index cannot be used as an upsert target.\n\n**Decision.** `saveRegister()` in `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` uses `prisma.$transaction(async tx => …)` and runs these steps:\n1. `findFirst` the session by (courseId, date, periodId) or (sectionId, date). Create it if it does not exist. If the create fails with `P2002`, a concurrent first save won the race: re-read the session and continue.\n2. Load the existing records for the session in a single query to get the previous statuses.\n3. Insert new students with `createMany`. Update only the rows whose status, minutesLate or note actually changed; `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` makes these targeted updates.\n4. Validate the roster (NFR-3) against ACTIVE enrollments on that date, or section members for a daily register, in one query before writing.\n5. Return the diff `{studentId, prev, next}[]`. Write `audit()` entries for changed records inside the transaction, or right after commit if `audit()` cannot take `tx`. Dev should check `src/server/audit.ts`.\n\n**Consequences.** About 5 to 40 statements run per save, which fits easily in 500 ms. The diff is computed by a pure function (`diffRecords(prev, next)`) that unit tests can cover (FR-39). No raw `INSERT … ON CONFLICT` is needed.\n\nDrivers: FR-14, FR-18, FR-21, FR-22, FR-39, FR-40, NFR-1, NFR-3.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Send notifications synchronously after commit through the existing notify pipeline, with no new job queue\n\n**Context.** FR-20 to FR-23 add four notification types. NFR-5 requires delivery within 5 minutes, with in-app notifications immediate and email through `EmailOutbox`. `notifyStudentAndParents()`/`notify()` already exist and never throw. There is no job runner or cron in `src/server`.\n\n**Decision.** After the transaction commits, loop over the diff and call `notifyStudentAndParents()` when:\n- a status changes from something other than ABSENT to ABSENT (`attendance.absent`);\n- a status changes from something other than LATE to LATE (`attendance.late`);\n- a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT (`attendance.corrected`).\n\nRe-saving an unchanged register produces no diff and therefore no notifications, which covers the dedupe rule in FR-22. Register all four keys in `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`, using intake's FR-23 defaults for `corrected`/`register_missing`. For daily registers, the body is `<Section> daily register, <date>`, following the clarification default.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no worker or queue infrastructure. Emails go through the existing outbox, so the 5-minute target depends on the existing outbox drain. Save latency grows by about one insert per notified student, which is fine at class size. If the notification loop ever pushes saves past NFR-1, move it to a fire-and-forget call after the response is sent.\n\nDrivers: FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-5.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Compute missing registers and \"today\" on demand in the school timezone, with no scheduler\n\n**Context.** FR-31 flags a register as missing if it is still not taken 15 minutes after the period starts, in the school timezone. FR-6, FR-8 and FR-19 depend on \"today\" and on 14-day windows. `Period.startTime` is a string, and `SchoolSettings.timezone` exists. `src/lib/dates.ts` already wraps `formatInTimeZone`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Compute `schoolToday()` as `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'yyyy-MM-dd')`. Every date-only comparison (future-date refusal, 14-day open/edit window, current period) uses this school-local date string compared with `@db.Date`. Never use server-local `new Date()`.\n- `GET /api/admin/attendance/overview` computes the missing list when it is requested. It expands `getScheduleForDate()` for each course meeting today, filters to meetings where `startTime + 15 min < now` in the school timezone, and subtracts the sessions that exist. \"Remind teacher\" is a manual POST.\n- Put the edit-window rule in a pure function, `canEdit(role, registerDate, today)` (FR-39).\n\n**Consequences.** No cron and no stored \"missing\" state. The overview always reflects reality. Automatic reminders are out of scope; add a scheduler only if the PRD later asks for automatic sending.\n\nDrivers: FR-6, FR-8, FR-19, FR-30, FR-31, FR-39, NFR-8.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Aggregate per student in TypeScript and school-wide with Prisma `groupBy`\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires the student tab to load in under 400 ms with 1,200 records. FR-25/26/27 need the summary, the calendar and the table from the same data. FR-28 defines the rate formula and the mode-dependent record set. FR-32/33 aggregate across all students for up to 366 days.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Student tab**: run one `findMany` over records joined to the session date and period, filtered by date range and by the mode's session kind (`courseId != null` for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, `sectionId != null` for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure functions then compute the term and year summaries (`attendanceRate()`), the per-day calendar colours and the table rows. 1,200 narrow rows is a few milliseconds of work.\n- **Report and below-threshold**: use `prisma.attendanceRecord.groupBy({ by: ['studentId','status'], where: { session: { date range, kind } } , _count })` and fold the result into per-student rows in TypeScript. If that turns out slow in practice, fall back to a single `$queryRaw` with `GROUP BY`.\n- Records from DROPPED enrollments are never filtered out (FR-28).\n- `attendanceRate()` lives in one place and is shared by the tab, matrix, report and threshold views (FR-39).\n\n**Consequences.** There are no materialised views or cached counters, and no index beyond FR-1's `[studentId, createdAt]` plus the session indexes. Notes are stripped in the service according to role (FR-27), not in the UI.\n\nDrivers: FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-32, FR-33, FR-39, NFR-1.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Keep offline resilience to localStorage drafts, with no service worker or IndexedDB\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 requires that unsaved marks survive a network failure and that the next visit offers a restore. The app already uses `window.localStorage` (`src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** The register's client component writes its draft to `localStorage` under the key `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>` when a save fails. On mount it shows a \"Restore unsaved attendance\" action if a draft exists, and it clears the draft after a successful save.\n\n**Consequences.** This is not offline-first. The page itself must still load. That is all NFR-2 asks for. Add a service worker only if a full offline mode is requested.\n\nDrivers: NFR-2, NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Reuse the existing auth, settings and config extension points\n\n**Context.** NFR-7 requires server-side access control everywhere. FR-5 needs an admin editor for settings, but there is no settings page and `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty. FR-24, FR-29 and FR-34 extend the tab and nav configuration.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Access.** Use `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `assertCanManageCourse`/`assertCanViewCourse` and `assertCanViewStudent`/`getAccessibleStudentIds` as they are. The one new check, homeroom access (`section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id || ADMIN`) for FR-15, is a short function in the attendance service. EXCUSED is rejected server-side for anyone who is not an admin (FR-10).\n- **Settings (FR-5).** Use the smallest option. Extend `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` with the two new fields and add `PATCH /api/settings/school`, which is ADMIN only, Zod-validated (threshold 0–100) and calls `audit()`. The editor is an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. A general settings page is out of scope.\n- **Tabs and nav.** Add entries to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts` and `navigation.ts`. Do not move or rename existing entries.\n- **Daily register route (FR-16).** Use `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=`, rendering the same register client component as the course route.\n\n**Consequences.** No new auth abstraction is needed. The FR-5 and FR-16 defaults are open for the user to override (see blockers in the intake handoff).\n\nDrivers: FR-5, FR-10, FR-15, FR-16, FR-24, FR-29, FR-34, FR-35, NFR-7, NFR-10.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Test with the existing Vitest and Playwright setups\n\n**Context.** FR-39 to FR-41 define the tests. Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2 are installed.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Unit (Vitest).** Cover the pure functions `attendanceRate`, `canEdit` and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`.\n- **Integration (Vitest against a migrated test database).** Cover `saveRegister` atomicity, NFR-3 roster rejection, and violations of the CHECK constraint and both partial indexes. The database must be created through migrations, per ADR-2.\n- **End-to-end (Playwright).** Run the take-attendance flow at a 375×667 viewport, and a parent's notification plus the calendar absence.\n- **Seed (FR-38).** Use a small seeded PRNG (mulberry32, a few lines) in the seed script rather than adding a dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling is added.\n\nDrivers: FR-38, FR-39, FR-40, FR-41, NFR-10.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VswcxUARoEQeGCiCXRhW48","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ed0f281-d368-4eed-bb70-33d048642e31","uuid":"965fb73b-fa8a-4813-a1af-fb124f49bb9c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:32:06.990Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2. Nothing in the requirements needs a different stack, so the decisions below cover how this feature uses the stack that is already there.\n\nThis file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) version that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no new dependencies\n\n**Context.** The feature needs a register UI with exclusive toggles (FR-9), a calendar with a custom day slot (FR-26), a scrollable matrix (FR-29), date pickers that block future dates (FR-8), CSV export (FR-32), timezone-aware \"today\" logic (FR-31, NFR-8), and shared validation (FR-36). NFR-6 allows MUI only, and NFR-10 asks for brownfield safety.\n\n**Decision.** Use only installed packages:\n- UI: `@mui/material` `ToggleButtonGroup`, `Paper` (sticky save bar), `Tooltip` and `Badge`; `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate`) and `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot; `@mui/x-data-grid` `DataGrid` for the course matrix and the admin report.\n- Validation: `zod`, in `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`.\n- Dates: `date-fns` and `date-fns-tz`, through the existing `src/lib/dates.ts`.\n- CSV: the existing `toCsv()`/`escapeCsvCell()` in `src/server/csv.ts`. `papaparse` is not needed for export.\n\nBefore writing any component, Dev must look it up through the mui-mcp server (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0). The server was reachable in this session.\n\n**Consequences.** There are no lockfile changes and no banned imports for QA to catch. The free (MIT) `DataGrid` has no column pinning and caps pages at 100 rows. That is acceptable: the matrix scrolls horizontally (FR-29) and pagination is capped at 100 anyway (NFR-8). Do not use `DataGridPro` features.\n\nDrivers: FR-8, FR-9, FR-26, FR-29, FR-32, FR-36, NFR-6, NFR-8, NFR-10.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Use a Prisma schema plus hand-written SQL in one migration for constraints Prisma can't express\n\n**Context.** FR-1 specifies the `AttendanceStatus` enum and the `AttendanceSession`/`AttendanceRecord` models. FR-2 needs \"exactly one of courseId/sectionId\". FR-3 needs two partial unique indexes. Prisma 5.20 cannot express CHECK constraints or partial (`WHERE`) indexes. FR-4 adds two `SchoolSettings` columns. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n\n**Decision.** Create one new migration, `2026110700000_attendance` or any timestamp later than the latest one. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then append the following raw SQL by hand:\n- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)`\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL`\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL`\n\n`SchoolSettings` gains an `AttendanceMode` enum column `attendanceMode` (default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. `date` is stored as `@db.Date`.\n\n**Consequences.** `prisma db push` and any schema drift check will not see these SQL objects, so tests must run `prisma migrate reset`/`deploy` and must not use `db push`. The service also checks the one-of rule (FR-2), so callers get a clean `VALIDATION_ERROR` before the database rejects the row. Prisma cannot `upsert` on a partial index (see ADR-3).\n\nDrivers: FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-40, NFR-8.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Save a register in one interactive transaction that only writes changed rows\n\n**Context.** FR-14 requires an atomic create-or-update of the session and all its records. NFR-1 requires a 35-student save to finish in under 500 ms. FR-18 requires an audit entry for each changed status, and FR-21/22 need the previous status to detect changes. A partial unique index cannot be used as an upsert target.\n\n**Decision.** `saveRegister()` in `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` uses `prisma.$transaction(async tx => …)` and runs these steps:\n1. `findFirst` the session by (courseId, date, periodId) or (sectionId, date). Create it if it does not exist. If the create fails with `P2002`, a concurrent first save won the race: re-read the session and continue.\n2. Load the existing records for the session in a single query to get the previous statuses.\n3. Insert new students with `createMany`. Update only the rows whose status, minutesLate or note actually changed; `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` makes these targeted updates.\n4. Validate the roster (NFR-3) against ACTIVE enrollments on that date, or section members for a daily register, in one query before writing.\n5. Return the diff `{studentId, prev, next}[]`. Write `audit()` entries for changed records inside the transaction, or right after commit if `audit()` cannot take `tx`. Dev should check `src/server/audit.ts`.\n\n**Consequences.** About 5 to 40 statements run per save, which fits easily in 500 ms. The diff is computed by a pure function (`diffRecords(prev, next)`) that unit tests can cover (FR-39). No raw `INSERT … ON CONFLICT` is needed.\n\nDrivers: FR-14, FR-18, FR-21, FR-22, FR-39, FR-40, NFR-1, NFR-3.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Send notifications synchronously after commit through the existing notify pipeline, with no new job queue\n\n**Context.** FR-20 to FR-23 add four notification types. NFR-5 requires delivery within 5 minutes, with in-app notifications immediate and email through `EmailOutbox`. `notifyStudentAndParents()`/`notify()` already exist and never throw. There is no job runner or cron in `src/server`.\n\n**Decision.** After the transaction commits, loop over the diff and call `notifyStudentAndParents()` when:\n- a status changes from something other than ABSENT to ABSENT (`attendance.absent`);\n- a status changes from something other than LATE to LATE (`attendance.late`);\n- a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT (`attendance.corrected`).\n\nRe-saving an unchanged register produces no diff and therefore no notifications, which covers the dedupe rule in FR-22. Register all four keys in `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`, using intake's FR-23 defaults for `corrected`/`register_missing`. For daily registers, the body is `<Section> daily register, <date>`, following the clarification default.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no worker or queue infrastructure. Emails go through the existing outbox, so the 5-minute target depends on the existing outbox drain. Save latency grows by about one insert per notified student, which is fine at class size. If the notification loop ever pushes saves past NFR-1, move it to a fire-and-forget call after the response is sent.\n\nDrivers: FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-5.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Compute missing registers and \"today\" on demand in the school timezone, with no scheduler\n\n**Context.** FR-31 flags a register as missing if it is still not taken 15 minutes after the period starts, in the school timezone. FR-6, FR-8 and FR-19 depend on \"today\" and on 14-day windows. `Period.startTime` is a string, and `SchoolSettings.timezone` exists. `src/lib/dates.ts` already wraps `formatInTimeZone`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Compute `schoolToday()` as `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'yyyy-MM-dd')`. Every date-only comparison (future-date refusal, 14-day open/edit window, current period) uses this school-local date string compared with `@db.Date`. Never use server-local `new Date()`.\n- `GET /api/admin/attendance/overview` computes the missing list when it is requested. It expands `getScheduleForDate()` for each course meeting today, filters to meetings where `startTime + 15 min < now` in the school timezone, and subtracts the sessions that exist. \"Remind teacher\" is a manual POST.\n- Put the edit-window rule in a pure function, `canEdit(role, registerDate, today)` (FR-39).\n\n**Consequences.** No cron and no stored \"missing\" state. The overview always reflects reality. Automatic reminders are out of scope; add a scheduler only if the PRD later asks for automatic sending.\n\nDrivers: FR-6, FR-8, FR-19, FR-30, FR-31, FR-39, NFR-8.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Aggregate per student in TypeScript and school-wide with Prisma `groupBy`\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires the student tab to load in under 400 ms with 1,200 records. FR-25/26/27 need the summary, the calendar and the table from the same data. FR-28 defines the rate formula and the mode-dependent record set. FR-32/33 aggregate across all students for up to 366 days.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Student tab**: run one `findMany` over records joined to the session date and period, filtered by date range and by the mode's session kind (`courseId != null` for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, `sectionId != null` for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure functions then compute the term and year summaries (`attendanceRate()`), the per-day calendar colours and the table rows. 1,200 narrow rows is a few milliseconds of work.\n- **Report and below-threshold**: use `prisma.attendanceRecord.groupBy({ by: ['studentId','status'], where: { session: { date range, kind } } , _count })` and fold the result into per-student rows in TypeScript. If that turns out slow in practice, fall back to a single `$queryRaw` with `GROUP BY`.\n- Records from DROPPED enrollments are never filtered out (FR-28).\n- `attendanceRate()` lives in one place and is shared by the tab, matrix, report and threshold views (FR-39).\n\n**Consequences.** There are no materialised views or cached counters, and no index beyond FR-1's `[studentId, createdAt]` plus the session indexes. Notes are stripped in the service according to role (FR-27), not in the UI.\n\nDrivers: FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-32, FR-33, FR-39, NFR-1.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Keep offline resilience to localStorage drafts, with no service worker or IndexedDB\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 requires that unsaved marks survive a network failure and that the next visit offers a restore. The app already uses `window.localStorage` (`src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** The register's client component writes its draft to `localStorage` under the key `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>` when a save fails. On mount it shows a \"Restore unsaved attendance\" action if a draft exists, and it clears the draft after a successful save.\n\n**Consequences.** This is not offline-first. The page itself must still load. That is all NFR-2 asks for. Add a service worker only if a full offline mode is requested.\n\nDrivers: NFR-2, NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Reuse the existing auth, settings and config extension points\n\n**Context.** NFR-7 requires server-side access control everywhere. FR-5 needs an admin editor for settings, but there is no settings page and `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty. FR-24, FR-29 and FR-34 extend the tab and nav configuration.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Access.** Use `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `assertCanManageCourse`/`assertCanViewCourse` and `assertCanViewStudent`/`getAccessibleStudentIds` as they are. The one new check, homeroom access (`section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id || ADMIN`) for FR-15, is a short function in the attendance service. EXCUSED is rejected server-side for anyone who is not an admin (FR-10).\n- **Settings (FR-5).** Use the smallest option. Extend `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` with the two new fields and add `PATCH /api/settings/school`, which is ADMIN only, Zod-validated (threshold 0–100) and calls `audit()`. The editor is an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. A general settings page is out of scope.\n- **Tabs and nav.** Add entries to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts` and `navigation.ts`. Do not move or rename existing entries.\n- **Daily register route (FR-16).** Use `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=`, rendering the same register client component as the course route.\n\n**Consequences.** No new auth abstraction is needed. The FR-5 and FR-16 defaults are open for the user to override (see blockers in the intake handoff).\n\nDrivers: FR-5, FR-10, FR-15, FR-16, FR-24, FR-29, FR-34, FR-35, NFR-7, NFR-10.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Test with the existing Vitest and Playwright setups\n\n**Context.** FR-39 to FR-41 define the tests. Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2 are installed.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Unit (Vitest).** Cover the pure functions `attendanceRate`, `canEdit` and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`.\n- **Integration (Vitest against a migrated test database).** Cover `saveRegister` atomicity, NFR-3 roster rejection, and violations of the CHECK constraint and both partial indexes. The database must be created through migrations, per ADR-2.\n- **End-to-end (Playwright).** Run the take-attendance flow at a 375×667 viewport, and a parent's notification plus the calendar absence.\n- **Seed (FR-38).** Use a small seeded PRNG (mulberry32, a few lines) in the seed script rather than adding a dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling is added.\n\nDrivers: FR-38, FR-39, FR-40, FR-41, NFR-10.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":110,"newStart":1,"newLines":151,"lines":["-# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)","+# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)"," ","-Ticket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:00:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`","-confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,","-next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with","-@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,","-Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.","-**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).","+**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2. Nothing in the requirements needs a different stack, so the decisions below cover how this feature uses the stack that is already there."," ","-This file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now","-cover only the remaining gaps.","+This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) version that was in this folder."," ","-**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**","+---"," ","-- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.","-- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.","-- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.","-- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).","-- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.","-- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.","-- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.","-- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.","-- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.","+## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no new dependencies"," ","+**Context.** The feature needs a register UI with exclusive toggles (FR-9), a calendar with a custom day slot (FR-26), a scrollable matrix (FR-29), date pickers that block future dates (FR-8), CSV export (FR-32), timezone-aware \"today\" logic (FR-31, NFR-8), and shared validation (FR-36). NFR-6 allows MUI only, and NFR-10 asks for brownfield safety.","+","+**Decision.** Use only installed packages:","+- UI: `@mui/material` `ToggleButtonGroup`, `Paper` (sticky save bar), `Tooltip` and `Badge`; `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate`) and `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot; `@mui/x-data-grid` `DataGrid` for the course matrix and the admin report.","+- Validation: `zod`, in `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`.","+- Dates: `date-fns` and `date-fns-tz`, through the existing `src/lib/dates.ts`.","+- CSV: the existing `toCsv()`/`escapeCsvCell()` in `src/server/csv.ts`. `papaparse` is not needed for export.","+","+Before writing any component, Dev must look it up through the mui-mcp server (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0). The server was reachable in this session.","+","+**Consequences.** There are no lockfile changes and no banned imports for QA to catch. The free (MIT) `DataGrid` has no column pinning and caps pages at 100 rows. That is acceptable: the matrix scrolls horizontally (FR-29) and pagination is capped at 100 anyway (NFR-8). Do not use `DataGridPro` features.","+","+Drivers: FR-8, FR-9, FR-26, FR-29, FR-32, FR-36, NFR-6, NFR-8, NFR-10.","+"," ---"," ","-## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency","+## ADR-2: Use a Prisma schema plus hand-written SQL in one migration for constraints Prisma can't express"," ","-**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend","-piece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).","+**Context.** FR-1 specifies the `AttendanceStatus` enum and the `AttendanceSession`/`AttendanceRecord` models. FR-2 needs \"exactly one of courseId/sectionId\". FR-3 needs two partial unique indexes. Prisma 5.20 cannot express CHECK constraints or partial (`WHERE`) indexes. FR-4 adds two `SchoolSettings` columns. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`."," ","-**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard","-or session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use","-`useToast()` (NFR-6).","+**Decision.** Create one new migration, `2026110700000_attendance` or any timestamp later than the latest one. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then append the following raw SQL by hand:","+- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)`","+- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL`","+- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL`"," ","-**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.","+`SchoolSettings` gains an `AttendanceMode` enum column `attendanceMode` (default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. `date` is stored as `@db.Date`."," ","-## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`","+**Consequences.** `prisma db push` and any schema drift check will not see these SQL objects, so tests must run `prisma migrate reset`/`deploy` and must not use `db push`. The service also checks the one-of rule (FR-2), so callers get a clean `VALIDATION_ERROR` before the database rejects the row. Prisma cannot `upsert` on a partial index (see ADR-3)."," ","-**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs","-the name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21","-needs an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.","+Drivers: FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-40, NFR-8."," ","-**Decision.**","-- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.","-- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.","-- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.","+---"," ","-**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness","-follows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.","+## ADR-3: Save a register in one interactive transaction that only writes changed rows"," ","-## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs","+**Context.** FR-14 requires an atomic create-or-update of the session and all its records. NFR-1 requires a 35-student save to finish in under 500 ms. FR-18 requires an audit entry for each changed status, and FR-21/22 need the previous status to detect changes. A partial unique index cannot be used as an upsert target."," ","-**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;","-on success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.","-FR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say","-tokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.","+**Decision.** `saveRegister()` in `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` uses `prisma.$transaction(async tx => …)` and runs these steps:","+1. `findFirst` the session by (courseId, date, periodId) or (sectionId, date). Create it if it does not exist. If the create fails with `P2002`, a concurrent first save won the race: re-read the session and continue.","+2. Load the existing records for the session in a single query to get the previous statuses.","+3. Insert new students with `createMany`. Update only the rows whose status, minutesLate or note actually changed; `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` makes these targeted updates.","+4. Validate the roster (NFR-3) against ACTIVE enrollments on that date, or section members for a daily register, in one query before writing.","+5. Return the diff `{studentId, prev, next}[]`. Write `audit()` entries for changed records inside the transaction, or right after commit if `audit()` cannot take `tx`. Dev should check `src/server/audit.ts`."," ","+**Consequences.** About 5 to 40 statements run per save, which fits easily in 500 ms. The diff is computed by a pure function (`diffRecords(prev, next)`) that unit tests can cover (FR-39). No raw `INSERT … ON CONFLICT` is needed.","+","+Drivers: FR-14, FR-18, FR-21, FR-22, FR-39, FR-40, NFR-1, NFR-3.","+","+---","+","+## ADR-4: Send notifications synchronously after commit through the existing notify pipeline, with no new job queue","+","+**Context.** FR-20 to FR-23 add four notification types. NFR-5 requires delivery within 5 minutes, with in-app notifications immediate and email through `EmailOutbox`. `notifyStudentAndParents()`/`notify()` already exist and never throw. There is no job runner or cron in `src/server`.","+","+**Decision.** After the transaction commits, loop over the diff and call `notifyStudentAndParents()` when:","+- a status changes from something other than ABSENT to ABSENT (`attendance.absent`);","+- a status changes from something other than LATE to LATE (`attendance.late`);","+- a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT (`attendance.corrected`).","+","+Re-saving an unchanged register produces no diff and therefore no notifications, which covers the dedupe rule in FR-22. Register all four keys in `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`, using intake's FR-23 defaults for `corrected`/`register_missing`. For daily registers, the body is `<Section> daily register, <date>`, following the clarification default.","+","+**Consequences.** There is no worker or queue infrastructure. Emails go through the existing outbox, so the 5-minute target depends on the existing outbox drain. Save latency grows by about one insert per notified student, which is fine at class size. If the notification loop ever pushes saves past NFR-1, move it to a fire-and-forget call after the response is sent.","+","+Drivers: FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-5.","+","+---","+","+## ADR-5: Compute missing registers and \"today\" on demand in the school timezone, with no scheduler","+","+**Context.** FR-31 flags a register as missing if it is still not taken 15 minutes after the period starts, in the school timezone. FR-6, FR-8 and FR-19 depend on \"today\" and on 14-day windows. `Period.startTime` is a string, and `SchoolSettings.timezone` exists. `src/lib/dates.ts` already wraps `formatInTimeZone`.","+"," **Decision.**","-- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).","-- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.","-  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.","-  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).","-- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.","-- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).","-- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.","+- Compute `schoolToday()` as `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'yyyy-MM-dd')`. Every date-only comparison (future-date refusal, 14-day open/edit window, current period) uses this school-local date string compared with `@db.Date`. Never use server-local `new Date()`.","+- `GET /api/admin/attendance/overview` computes the missing list when it is requested. It expands `getScheduleForDate()` for each course meeting today, filters to meetings where `startTime + 15 min < now` in the school timezone, and subtracts the sessions that exist. \"Remind teacher\" is a manual POST.","+- Put the edit-window rule in a pure function, `canEdit(role, registerDate, today)` (FR-39)."," ","-**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are","-added. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.","+**Consequences.** No cron and no stored \"missing\" state. The overview always reflects reality. Automatic reminders are out of scope; add a scheduler only if the PRD later asks for automatic sending."," ","-## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox","+Drivers: FR-6, FR-8, FR-19, FR-30, FR-31, FR-39, NFR-8."," ","-**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,","-and Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.","-NFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.","+---"," ","+## ADR-6: Aggregate per student in TypeScript and school-wide with Prisma `groupBy`","+","+**Context.** NFR-1 requires the student tab to load in under 400 ms with 1,200 records. FR-25/26/27 need the summary, the calendar and the table from the same data. FR-28 defines the rate formula and the mode-dependent record set. FR-32/33 aggregate across all students for up to 366 days.","+"," **Decision.**","-- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.","-- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:","-  - seed admin signs in and signs out","-  - wrong-password message","-  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`","-  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)","-  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`","+- **Student tab**: run one `findMany` over records joined to the session date and period, filtered by date range and by the mode's session kind (`courseId != null` for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, `sectionId != null` for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure functions then compute the term and year summaries (`attendanceRate()`), the per-day calendar colours and the table rows. 1,200 narrow rows is a few milliseconds of work.","+- **Report and below-threshold**: use `prisma.attendanceRecord.groupBy({ by: ['studentId','status'], where: { session: { date range, kind } } , _count })` and fold the result into per-student rows in TypeScript. If that turns out slow in practice, fall back to a single `$queryRaw` with `GROUP BY`.","+- Records from DROPPED enrollments are never filtered out (FR-28).","+- `attendanceRate()` lives in one place and is shared by the tab, matrix, report and threshold views (FR-39)."," ","-  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.","+**Consequences.** There are no materialised views or cached counters, and no index beyond FR-1's `[studentId, createdAt]` plus the session indexes. Notes are stripped in the service according to role (FR-27), not in the UI."," ","-**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the","-Playwright process.","+Drivers: FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-32, FR-33, FR-39, NFR-1."," ","-## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept","+---"," ","-**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already","-migrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.","+## ADR-7: Keep offline resilience to localStorage drafts, with no service worker or IndexedDB"," ","-**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they","-are. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.","+**Context.** NFR-2 requires that unsaved marks survive a network failure and that the next visit offers a restore. The app already uses `window.localStorage` (`src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`)."," ","-**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.","+**Decision.** The register's client component writes its draft to `localStorage` under the key `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>` when a save fails. On mount it shows a \"Restore unsaved attendance\" action if a draft exists, and it clears the draft after a successful save."," ","+**Consequences.** This is not offline-first. The page itself must still load. That is all NFR-2 asks for. Add a service worker only if a full offline mode is requested.","+","+Drivers: NFR-2, NFR-4.","+"," ---"," ","-## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`","+## ADR-8: Reuse the existing auth, settings and config extension points"," ","-- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).","-- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.","-- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.","-- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).","+**Context.** NFR-7 requires server-side access control everywhere. FR-5 needs an admin editor for settings, but there is no settings page and `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty. FR-24, FR-29 and FR-34 extend the tab and nav configuration.","+","+**Decision.**","+- **Access.** Use `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `assertCanManageCourse`/`assertCanViewCourse` and `assertCanViewStudent`/`getAccessibleStudentIds` as they are. The one new check, homeroom access (`section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id || ADMIN`) for FR-15, is a short function in the attendance service. EXCUSED is rejected server-side for anyone who is not an admin (FR-10).","+- **Settings (FR-5).** Use the smallest option. Extend `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` with the two new fields and add `PATCH /api/settings/school`, which is ADMIN only, Zod-validated (threshold 0–100) and calls `audit()`. The editor is an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. A general settings page is out of scope.","+- **Tabs and nav.** Add entries to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts` and `navigation.ts`. Do not move or rename existing entries.","+- **Daily register route (FR-16).** Use `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=`, rendering the same register client component as the course route.","+","+**Consequences.** No new auth abstraction is needed. The FR-5 and FR-16 defaults are open for the user to override (see blockers in the intake handoff).","+","+Drivers: FR-5, FR-10, FR-15, FR-16, FR-24, FR-29, FR-34, FR-35, NFR-7, NFR-10.","+","+---","+","+## ADR-9: Test with the existing Vitest and Playwright setups","+","+**Context.** FR-39 to FR-41 define the tests. Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2 are installed.","+","+**Decision.**","+- **Unit (Vitest).** Cover the pure functions `attendanceRate`, `canEdit` and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`.","+- **Integration (Vitest against a migrated test database).** Cover `saveRegister` atomicity, NFR-3 roster rejection, and violations of the CHECK constraint and both partial indexes. The database must be created through migrations, per ADR-2.","+- **End-to-end (Playwright).** Run the take-attendance flow at a 375×667 viewport, and a parent's notification plus the calendar absence.","+- **Seed (FR-38).** Use a small seeded PRNG (mulberry32, a few lines) in the seed script rather than adding a dependency.","+","+**Consequences.** No new test tooling is added.","+","+Drivers: FR-38, FR-39, FR-40, FR-41, NFR-10."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\nVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n\nThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\ncover only the remaining gaps.\n\n**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n\n- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\npiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\nor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\nthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\nneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\nfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\non success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\nFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\ntokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are\nadded. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.\n\n## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,\nand Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.\nNFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:\n  - seed admin signs in and signs out\n  - wrong-password message\n  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`\n  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)\n  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`\n\n  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the\nPlaywright process.\n\n## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept\n\n**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already\nmigrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.\n\n**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they\nare. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VswcxUARoEQeGCiCXRhW48","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
