:\ndev-log.md\ndev-rerun-count.json\nsecurity-scan-report.json\ntask-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/qa:\ncoverage-report.md\nqa-report.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-08: File Storage & Course Content (Modules and Lessons) (SCH-008)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-8 and the PRD header says SCH-008. All artifacts use SH-8. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-7 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no file storage or course content code yet. There are no FileObject/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress models, no ContentStatus enum, no src/server/storage.ts, no src/server/files/, no content routes or pages, and no UPLOAD_DIR/MAX_UPLOAD_MB entries in .env.example.\",\n    \"MISSING DEPENDENCIES: the PRD needs file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable, and none of them are in package.json. @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 is installed. All of these are on the PRD's allowed list of non-visual libraries.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse()/assertCanManageCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts, assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts, and requireUser()/requireRole() in src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) in src/server/rate-limit.ts (a per-process sliding window) for the 60 uploads/hour limit. audit() comes from src/server/audit.ts, notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts, and the type keys live in NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: the course tab registry src/config/course-tabs.ts (currently overview, roster and attendance) and the student tab registry src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently courses and attendance). The 'Content' and 'Learning' tabs are added there.\",\n    \"DAILY MAINTENANCE HOOK: PRD-04's 'daily maintenance run' is the once-per-day purgeOldNotifications() call inside src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, which is gated by an in-memory lastPurgeAt. purgeOrphanFiles() should be called next to it.\",\n    \"LOGO: SchoolSettings.logoUrl (String?) is in prisma/schema.prisma:195 and in UpdateSchoolSettingsInput (src/server/services/settings.ts), the email BaseLayout and render.ts use it, and PATCH /api/settings/school exists. However, there is NO /admin/settings/school page in src/app/(app)/admin/, so FR-9's 'replace the logo URL field' has no field to replace.\",\n    \"SHARED COMPONENTS: they live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, FormField, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker...), not in src/components/shared/. New shared components (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView) should follow the existing src/components/<Name>/ layout.\",\n    \"No .gitignore was found at the workspace root. UPLOAD_DIR (./uploads) must be git-ignored, so either create one or add the entry if a .gitignore exists elsewhere.\",\n    \"VERIFIED: assertCanViewCourse already allows PARENT when a linked student has an ACTIVE enrollment, and STUDENT only when ACTIVE-enrolled. Use it unchanged.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n      \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-3.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"description\": \"Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n      \"description\": \"Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n      \"description\": \"Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table; Acceptance Criterion 7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"description\": \"Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"description\": \"Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"description\": \"Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.1; NFR Accessibility\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"description\": \"The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n      \"description\": \"Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"description\": \"Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"description\": \"Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.5; Acceptance Criterion 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"description\": \"Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"description\": \"For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.3; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"description\": \"Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.4; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-35\",\n      \"description\": \"Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.1; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-36\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-37\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents can view a course's Content tab only when a linked student is ACTIVE-enrolled. The existing assertCanViewCourse already enforces this (verified in src/server/auth/course-access.ts PARENT branch), so reuse it as is.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Roles (parents see data for linked students)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-38\",\n      \"description\": \"Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-39\",\n      \"description\": \"Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.'\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-8.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-40\",\n      \"description\": \"Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (storage of the URL in logoUrl inferred; existing column reused, no rename)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-41\",\n      \"description\": \"SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-9.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-42\",\n      \"description\": \"/admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (references a page from PRD-02 not found in src/app/(app)/admin/)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-43\",\n      \"description\": \"Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table; Code layout (response shape)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-44\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"API table ('view (visibility rules)'); FR-3.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-45\",\n      \"description\": \"Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (feature-named subdirectory precedent)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n      \"description\": \"Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit().\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (AuditLog rule)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-47\",\n      \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Seed Data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-48\",\n      \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Security); FR-1.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Performance)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 requires intake to record it)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context; Assumptions and constraints\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (timestamps); FR-5.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Out of Scope\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions; Fixed technology decisions (.env.example)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-42: /admin/settings/school (said to come from PRD-02) does not exist in the workspace. Should intake create a minimal school settings page to host the logo upload?\",\n        \"FR-6: How should txt/csv (no magic number) and docx/xlsx/pptx (sniff as zip) pass magic-number validation?\",\n        \"FR-40: Should SchoolSettings.logoUrl store '/api/files/<id>', or should a new logoFileId column be added?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-42 default: create a minimal ADMIN /admin/settings/school page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school.\",\n        \"FR-6 default: accept text types when no signature is detected, accept OOXML when the sniffed type is zip or the matching OOXML mime, and reject everything else that mismatches.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: store '/api/files/<id>' in the existing logoUrl column, with no schema change. Email templates then need an absolute URL (APP_URL prefix).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"The run mode declares '--tech-stack react', and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18 and TypeScript strict, Prisma on PostgreSQL 16, and Auth.js v5. @mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/material-nextjs, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers and @mui/x-charts are all at 9.5.0, with @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1. This PRD needs new allowed non-visual deps that are not installed yet: file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable. The date-time picker comes from the installed @mui/x-date-pickers. Styling goes only through the MUI theme, sx and styled().\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 60,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"GREENFIELD within brownfield: there is no file storage or content code yet. Design the FileObject/ContentStatus/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress migration, src/server/storage.ts, src/server/files/ (access registry, purge), src/server/content/content-service.ts, src/lib/validators/content.ts, the 15 API endpoints, the Content course tab, the lesson editor and viewer pages, the Learning student tab, the FileUpload/FileList/MarkdownView components, seed data plus prisma/seed-assets PDF, and the tests.\",\n    \"NEW DEPS required (all PRD-allowed): file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse (already handles PARENT via linked ACTIVE enrollment), assertCanManageCourse, assertCanViewStudent, rateLimit(), audit(), notify() + NOTIFICATION_TYPES, the courseTabs/studentTabs registries, updateSchoolSettings(), and the components in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, PageHeader, Toast/useToast).\",\n    \"FR-12: hook purgeOrphanFiles() into the once-daily purge block in src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, next to purgeOldNotifications().\",\n    \"FR-42 (LOW): /admin/settings/school does not exist. Default: create a minimal ADMIN page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school. FR-40 stores '/api/files/<id>' in the existing SchoolSettings.logoUrl, and email templates need an APP_URL-absolute URL.\",\n    \"FR-6 (MEDIUM): define sniffing rules for txt/csv (no signature) and OOXML (zip signature).\",\n    \"No root .gitignore was found. Ensure ./uploads is git-ignored.\",\n    \"NFR-7: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0156fK7hp4Ph7duHrXKE2iBN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
