{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnBAff7aUN6AaYSSNWJG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the SH-8 stack decisions to `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md`, replacing the old SH-7 file. It has nine decision records, each citing the FR/NFR ids that drove it, and every id cited exists in `requirements.json`. The current stack (Next 14, Prisma, Auth.js, MUI 9.5.0) covers everything the requirements need. These six decisions affect what dev builds:\n\n- **New libraries are pinned.** The latest `file-type` needs Node 22, but the project supports Node 18.18 and up, so it's pinned to 20.5.0. The other four are `react-markdown` 10.1.0, `remark-gfm` 4.0.1, `rehype-sanitize` 6.0.0 and `@dnd-kit/sortable` 10.0.0.\n- **Uploads use `busboy`, not `request.formData()`.** `formData()` loads the whole file into memory, which breaks NFR-5 for 25 MB files. `busboy` 1.6.0 is already installed because Next.js depends on it, so nothing new gets added. The catch: if a future Next.js upgrade drops it, we'll need to add it ourselves. This is the one place the design leans on a library outside the approved list.\n- **Video embeds need a config change.** The site's security policy in `next.config.js` currently blocks all iframes, so YouTube and Vimeo videos (FR-30) wouldn't load. One line adding those two sites fixes it.\n- **Logo files need a public path.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 to signed-out users on any `/api/` path not on the public list. `/api/files/` has to go on that list so logos load without signing in. Each file request then goes through the access check, which refuses signed-out users for anything that isn't a logo.\n- **File-type checks use one table.** It covers every allowed extension. txt, csv and SVG must have no detectable signature. docx, xlsx and pptx may look like zip files. SVG is accepted only as a logo.\n- **The repo has no root `.gitignore`.** One needs creating with `uploads/` in it.\n\nThe file ends with three open risks: dev must check every MUI component against the docs server, the `busboy` dependency above, and the low-confidence logo and settings-page defaults.\n\nI didn't write any other sub-task's files. The other architect files still hold SH-7 content and will be overwritten by their own sub-tasks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6188,"cache_read_input_tokens":47424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6188},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6161ef1e-09c5-429b-90ef-ea4fc0ebef55","uuid":"56bf1670-5c6f-43de-ae15-dc5ddc047077","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:50:05.724Z","request_id":"req_011CgnBAfEZuWa6qD9a3LK8V"}
