{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LBgSiKikdQeqdFMJomNiuy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tapprovals\n2\tarchitect\n3\tdev\n4\tdev-planning\n5\tintake\n6\tqa\n7\trun-summary.json\n8\ttelemetry\n9\tui-verification\n10\t\n11\tartifacts/approvals:\n12\tarchitect-approval.json\n13\tdev-planning-approval.json\n14\tintake-approval.json\n15\t\n16\tartifacts/architect:\n17\tapi-contracts.json\n18\thandoff-to-dev-planning.json\n19\trequirements-analysis-notes.md\n20\tsystem-design.md\n21\ttech-stack-decisions.md\n22\tthreat-model-notes.json\n23\t\n24\tartifacts/dev:\n25\tdev-log.md\n26\tdev-rerun-count.json\n27\tsecurity-scan-report.json\n28\ttask-completion-markers.json\n29\t\n30\tartifacts/dev-planning:\n31\tfile-ownership-matrix.json\n32\tfile-structure.md\n33\timplementation-plan.json\n34\tmodule-dependencies.json\n35\t\n36\tartifacts/intake:\n37\thandoff-to-architect.json\n38\trequirements.json\n39\ttech-stack.json\n40\tuser-stories.md\n41\t\n42\tartifacts/qa:\n43\tcoverage-report.md\n44\tqa-report.md\n45\t\n46\tartifacts/telemetry:\n47\tapi-retries.jsonl\n48\tdaemon-handoff.json\n49\tknowledge-log.jsonl\n50\tmetering.jsonl\n51\t{\n52\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n53\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T09:00:00Z\",\n54\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n55\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n56\t  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-09: Assignments & Submissions\",\n57\t  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-009 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-9.\",\n58\t  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n59\t  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n60\t    {\n61\t      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n62\t      \"description\": \"Add the Prisma enums SubmissionType (ONLINE_TEXT, FILE_UPLOAD, TEXT_AND_FILE, NO_SUBMISSION), AssignmentStatus (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and SubmissionStatus (SUBMITTED, RETURNED) in a new prisma migrate migration.\",\n63\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n64\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (enum block)\"\n65\t    },\n66\t    {\n67\t      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n68\t      \"description\": \"Add an Assignment model with the fields listed in FR-1. Also add allowExtraCredit Boolean @default(false) (from FR-5.6), notifiedAt DateTime? (from FR-7.1) and archivedAt DateTime? (from the API table). Add a Course→Assignment relation (onDelete Cascade), a rubricId @unique relation to Rubric, and @@index([courseId, dueAt]).\",\n69\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n70\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 model Assignment; FR-5.6; FR-7.1; API table (DELETE row)\"\n71\t    },\n72\t    {\n73\t      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n74\t      \"description\": \"Add the models AssignmentAttachment (assignment↔FileObject), Rubric and RubricCriterion. RubricCriterion has title, description?, maxPoints Decimal(6,2), order, and levels Json [{label, points, description}].\",\n75\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n76\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 models AssignmentAttachment, Rubric, RubricCriterion\"\n77\t    },\n78\t    {\n79\t      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n80\t      \"description\": \"Add the models Submission (@@unique([assignmentId, studentId]), with Decimal rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore and Json rubricScores [{criterionId, points, comment}]), SubmissionFile (submission↔FileObject) and SubmissionHistory (attemptNumber, text, fileIds String[], submittedAt).\",\n81\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n82\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 models Submission, SubmissionFile, SubmissionHistory\"\n83\t    },\n84\t    {\n85\t      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n86\t      \"description\": \"Add a GradeExemption model with a composite id (assignmentId, studentId), an optional reason and createdAt.\",\n87\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n88\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 model GradeExemption\"\n89\t    },\n90\t    {\n91\t      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n92\t      \"description\": \"Add an AssignmentReminder table {assignmentId, studentId, kind} with a unique key on all three columns. It makes the due_soon and missing reminders idempotent.\",\n93\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n94\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.2 (AssignmentReminder table)\"\n95\t    },\n96\t    {\n97\t      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n98\t      \"description\": \"Enforce the field limits in Zod schemas in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts, shared by forms and handlers: title ≤150; instructions ≤50,000; maxPoints 0–1000; lateCutoffAt > dueAt; latePenaltyPercentPerDay and maxLatePenaltyPercent 0–100; maxFileCount 1–10; submission text ≤50,000; feedback ≤10,000.\",\n99\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n100\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 field comments; Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation)\"\n101\t    },\n102\t    {\n103\t      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n104\t      \"description\": \"A teacher can record a grade for a student who did not submit. The service creates a Submission with text = null, no files, submittedAt = gradedAt and attemptNumber = 0 (the offline/no-submission marker).\",\n105\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n106\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 (paragraph after the schema); FR-5.5\"\n107\t    },\n108\t    {\n109\t      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n110\t      \"description\": \"Build the create/edit page at /courses/[courseId]/assignments/new. Fields: title, Markdown instructions (the PRD-08 editor), attachments (FileUpload, context 'assignment'), submission type, max points, due date-time (school timezone), optional available-from, late policy (allow-late toggle → cutoff, penalty per day, maximum penalty), maximum file count, allow extra credit, and an optional rubric builder.\",\n111\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n112\t      \"source\": \"FR-2.1; FR-5.6\"\n113\t    },\n114\t    {\n115\t      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n116\t      \"description\": \"Default the due date-time to the next teaching day at 23:59 in the school timezone. 'Teaching day' is taken from the existing SchoolDay.isTeaching weekday table, because holidays are not modelled before PRD-14.\",\n117\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n118\t      \"source\": \"FR-2.1 (default next teaching day 23:59); prisma SchoolDay model (PRD-06)\"\n119\t    },\n120\t    {\n121\t      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n122\t      \"description\": \"Rubric builder: add, reorder and remove criteria (title, description, levels with label + points + description). The sum of the criterion maximums must equal max points. Otherwise show the inline error 'Rubric totals {sum} points but the assignment is worth {maxPoints}.', and the server rejects the save with VALIDATION_ERROR.\",\n123\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n124\t      \"source\": \"FR-2.2; Acceptance Criteria 5\"\n125\t    },\n126\t    {\n127\t      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n128\t      \"description\": \"Offer 'Save draft' (DRAFT), 'Publish' (PUBLISHED) and 'Schedule' (SCHEDULED). Schedule requires an available-from in the future, and the assignment stays hidden from students and parents until then.\",\n129\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n130\t      \"source\": \"FR-2.3; FR-1 (availableFrom comment)\"\n131\t    },\n132\t    {\n133\t      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n134\t      \"description\": \"A SCHEDULED assignment counts as visible once availableFrom ≤ server now. Visibility is computed at read time. No background job rewrites the status to PUBLISHED.\",\n135\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n136\t      \"source\": \"FR-2.3 ('becomes visible then'); FR-7.1 ('when scheduled becomes visible on first student list load')\"\n137\t    },\n138\t    {\n139\t      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n140\t      \"description\": \"Editing the due date or max points of a published assignment that has submissions shows a warning. Changing max points recalculates nothing: existing scores are kept, and a banner prompts the teacher to review grades.\",\n141\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n142\t      \"source\": \"FR-2.4\"\n143\t    },\n144\t    {\n145\t      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n146\t      \"description\": \"A 'Duplicate to other courses' action copies the assignment as DRAFT to selected courses the teacher manages (POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}). The copy keeps the instructions, attachments, settings and rubric. The copy keeps the same due date-time, and availableFrom/lateCutoffAt keep their offsets from dueAt.\",\n147\t      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n148\t      \"source\": \"FR-2.5 ('with the same relative due date'); API table (duplicate row)\"\n149\t    },\n150\t    {\n151\t      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n152\t      \"description\": \"Register an 'Assignments' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts for all roles that can view the course.\",\n153\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n154\t      \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n155\t    },\n156\t    {\n157\t      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n158\t      \"description\": \"Teacher/admin view of the course Assignments tab: a table with title, due date, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted and a 'Grade' button.\",\n159\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n160\t      \"source\": \"FR-3.1 (teacher view)\"\n161\t    },\n162\t    {\n163\t      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n164\t      \"description\": \"Student view of the course Assignments tab: a list grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned. Parents see the same view, read-only, for their linked child.\",\n165\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n166\t      \"source\": \"FR-3.1 (student view, parent view)\"\n167\t    },\n168\t    {\n169\t      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n170\t      \"description\": \"The assignment page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId] shows the instructions (sanitised Markdown), attachments, due date, late policy summary, rubric (if any) and the submission panel. When under 48 hours remain, it adds a live countdown such as 'Due in 5 h 12 min'.\",\n171\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n172\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"\n173\t    },\n174\t    {\n175\t      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n176\t      \"description\": \"The submission panel shows a Markdown text editor and/or file upload, depending on submissionType (NO_SUBMISSION shows neither). File upload respects maxFileCount. Draft text autosaves to localStorage only, never to the server.\",\n177\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n178\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.2\"\n179\t    },\n180\t    {\n181\t      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n182\t      \"description\": \"Clicking Submit opens a confirmation Dialog before the POST.\",\n183\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n184\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"\n185\t    },\n186\t    {\n187\t      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n188\t      \"description\": \"Server submission rules: the assignment is visible; the student is ACTIVE-enrolled in the course; the student is not exempt. If now > dueAt, allowLate must be true and now ≤ lateCutoffAt (when set). Otherwise return VALIDATION_ERROR 'The deadline has passed and late submissions are closed.'\",\n189\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n190\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.3; Acceptance Criteria 2\"\n191\t    },\n192\t    {\n193\t      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n194\t      \"description\": \"On submit, compute isLate = submittedAt > dueAt and lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h), using server time. For example, due Mon 23:59 and submitted Wed 10:00 gives lateDays = 2.\",\n195\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n196\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.4; Acceptance Criteria 1\"\n197\t    },\n198\t    {\n199\t      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n200\t      \"description\": \"Resubmission is allowed until dueAt (or lateCutoffAt / indefinitely when late is allowed) and only while status = SUBMITTED. It copies the previous attempt into SubmissionHistory, increments attemptNumber, and clears rawScore, penaltyPercent, finalScore, feedback, rubricScores, gradedById and gradedAt. Once the work is RETURNED, resubmission is refused.\",\n201\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n202\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.5; Acceptance Criteria 3, 4\"\n203\t    },\n204\t    {\n205\t      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n206\t      \"description\": \"After submitting, the student sees a receipt such as 'Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)', in the school timezone, plus the files and text submitted.\",\n207\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n208\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.6\"\n209\t    },\n210\t    {\n211\t      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n212\t      \"description\": \"After return, the student sees the final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and the late penalty applied.\",\n213\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n214\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.7\"\n215\t    },\n216\t    {\n217\t      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n218\t      \"description\": \"Until the work is returned, the student and parent see 'Submitted — awaiting grading'. No score, rubric scores or feedback are sent in the API response.\",\n219\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n220\t      \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria 7; FR-5.4 ('Save' = not yet visible to student)\"\n221\t    },\n222\t    {\n223\t      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n224\t      \"description\": \"Grading page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade, left panel: an MUI List of all enrolled students with status Chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter, and sorting by name or submission time.\",\n225\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n226\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.1\"\n227\t    },\n228\t    {\n229\t      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n230\t      \"description\": \"Grading main panel: the selected submission's text as sanitised Markdown, and its files listed with inline preview for images and PDFs (<img>/<iframe> to /api/files/:id?inline=1, which already exists). Previous attempts (SubmissionHistory) are available in a dropdown.\",\n231\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n232\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.2\"\n233\t    },\n234\t    {\n235\t      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n236\t      \"description\": \"Grading form. With a rubric, each criterion is an exclusive ToggleButtonGroup of levels, and the selected points auto-sum into the raw score (for example 8 + 9 → 17). Without a rubric, the raw score is entered directly. The late penalty is pre-filled as min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty) and can be overridden. The final score is computed live. There is a Markdown feedback editor.\",\n237\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n238\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.3; Acceptance Criteria 1, 6\"\n239\t    },\n240\t    {\n241\t      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n242\t      \"description\": \"finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100), rounded half-up to 2 dp. For example, raw 18 with 20 % → 14.40. It is computed server-side at grading time.\",\n243\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n244\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 (finalScore comment); NFR-1 Correctness; Acceptance Criteria 1\"\n245\t    },\n246\t    {\n247\t      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n248\t      \"description\": \"Grading buttons: 'Save' (graded, not visible to the student), 'Save & return' (returns this submission and sets returnedAt) and the bulk 'Return all graded' (POST /api/assignments/:id/return; submissionIds optional, defaults to all graded and unreturned).\",\n249\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n250\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.4; API table (return row)\"\n251\t    },\n252\t    {\n253\t      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n254\t      \"description\": \"Keyboard shortcuts on the grading screen: J = next student, K = previous student, Ctrl+Enter = save and go to the next student. The shortcuts are not captured while typing in text fields, except Ctrl+Enter.\",\n255\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n256\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.4; Goals 3\"\n257\t    },\n258\t    {\n259\t      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n260\t      \"description\": \"'Grade without submission' for students who did not submit (POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}). It creates the attemptNumber = 0 Submission described in FR-8.\",\n261\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n262\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.5; FR-1 paragraph; API table\"\n263\t    },\n264\t    {\n265\t      \"id\": \"FR-35\",\n266\t      \"description\": \"An 'Exempt' toggle (PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId) writes or deletes a GradeExemption. Exempt students are removed from missing counts and lists, get no due_soon or missing reminders, cannot submit, and are flagged for exclusion from future gradebook calculation (PRD-11).\",\n267\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n268\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.5; FR-4.3 (not exempt); FR-6.1 (Missing not exempt); API table\"\n269\t    },\n270\t    {\n271\t      \"id\": \"FR-36\",\n272\t      \"description\": \"Validate scores server-side: rawScore and the rubric points must be within 0..maxPoints. When allowExtraCredit is true, rawScore may go up to 120 % of maxPoints. penaltyPercent must be 0–100.\",\n273\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n274\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.6; FR-1 (penaltyPercent range)\"\n275\t    },\n276\t    {\n277\t      \"id\": \"FR-37\",\n278\t      \"description\": \"Build the /assignments page for STUDENT. It lists every assignment across the student's ACTIVE enrollments in four tabs: Upcoming (sorted by due date), Missing (past due, not submitted, not exempt), Submitted and Returned. There is a course filter.\",\n279\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n280\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Goals 2\"\n281\t    },\n282\t    {\n283\t      \"id\": \"FR-38\",\n284\t      \"description\": \"The /assignments page for PARENT has a child selector (linked students only) and shows the same content as the student view, read-only.\",\n285\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n286\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.1 (PARENT)\"\n287\t    },\n288\t    {\n289\t      \"id\": \"FR-39\",\n290\t      \"description\": \"The /assignments page for TEACHER is a 'To grade' list of submitted, ungraded submissions across the courses they teach (teacherId or coTeacherIds), oldest first.\",\n291\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n292\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.1 (TEACHER)\"\n293\t    },\n294\t    {\n295\t      \"id\": \"FR-40\",\n296\t      \"description\": \"Add an 'Assignments' nav entry for /assignments to src/config/navigation.ts for STUDENT, PARENT and TEACHER.\",\n297\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n298\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout ('A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry'); FR-6.1\"\n299\t    },\n300\t    {\n301\t      \"id\": \"FR-41\",\n302\t      \"description\": \"Register an 'Assignments' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts. It shows the same per-student data to teachers and admins who view the student (GET /api/students/:id/assignments).\",\n303\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n304\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.2; API table\"\n305\t    },\n306\t    {\n307\t      \"id\": \"FR-42\",\n308\t      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.published to ACTIVE-enrolled students (in-app; email default false). It is sent on publish, or for SCHEDULED assignments on the first student list load after availableFrom. It is sent exactly once, using Assignment.notifiedAt (set atomically).\",\n309\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n310\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.1\"\n311\t    },\n312\t    {\n313\t      \"id\": \"FR-43\",\n314\t      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.due_soon to students with no submission (and not exempt) once dueAt − 24 h has passed and before dueAt. sendDueReminders() runs on every PRD-04 maintenance dispatcher call (src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts). It is idempotent via the AssignmentReminder unique key (kind 'due_soon').\",\n315\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n316\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criteria 8\"\n317\t    },\n318\t    {\n319\t      \"id\": \"FR-44\",\n320\t      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.returned to the student and their parents through the existing notifyStudentAndParents(). The body includes course, title and score, for example 'Mathematics: Fractions worksheet — 18/20'.\",\n321\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n322\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.3\"\n323\t    },\n324\t    {\n325\t      \"id\": \"FR-45\",\n326\t      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.missing to parents only (email default true), once per student, 24 hours after dueAt if the student has still not submitted and is not exempt. It is idempotent via AssignmentReminder (kind 'missing') and runs in the same sendDueReminders() maintenance pass.\",\n327\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n328\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.4; Acceptance Criteria 9\"\n329\t    },\n330\t    {\n331\t      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n332\t      \"description\": \"Add the four notification types to NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts with the category ACADEMIC and the role lists that match their recipients.\",\n333\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n334\t      \"source\": \"FR-7 ('Register and send'); Platform Context (notification type keys registered in types.ts)\"\n335\t    },\n336\t    {\n337\t      \"id\": \"FR-47\",\n338\t      \"description\": \"Register two file access contexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts: 'assignment' (anyone who can view the assignment, with visibility rules applied) and 'submission' (the submitting student, their linked parents, course managers and admins). Any other user is denied.\",\n339\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n340\t      \"source\": \"FR-8.1; Acceptance Criteria 10\"\n341\t    },\n342\t    {\n343\t      \"id\": \"FR-48\",\n344\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/courses/:id/assignments (view course) returns a role-shaped list. Managers get every status with counts. Students and parents get only visible, non-archived assignments, with their own submission state.\",\n345\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n346\t      \"source\": \"API table\"\n347\t    },\n348\t    {\n349\t      \"id\": \"FR-49\",\n350\t      \"description\": \"POST /api/courses/:id/assignments (manage course) creates an assignment with its rubric and attachments.\",\n351\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n352\t      \"source\": \"API table\"\n353\t    },\n354\t    {\n355\t      \"id\": \"FR-50\",\n356\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/assignments/:id (view). For students and parents the response includes their own submission, with grading fields only once returned.\",\n357\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n358\t      \"source\": \"API table; Acceptance Criteria 7\"\n359\t    },\n360\t    {\n361\t      \"id\": \"FR-51\",\n362\t      \"description\": \"PATCH /api/assignments/:id (manage). DELETE /api/assignments/:id (manage) hard-deletes only when there are no submissions. Otherwise it sets archivedAt.\",\n363\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n364\t      \"source\": \"API table (PATCH/DELETE row)\"\n365\t    },\n366\t    {\n367\t      \"id\": \"FR-52\",\n368\t      \"description\": \"Archived assignments are hidden from student and parent lists, /assignments, reminders and new submissions. Managers can still see them.\",\n369\t      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n370\t      \"source\": \"API table ('otherwise archive (add archivedAt)') — the behaviour of an archived assignment is not specified\"\n371\t    },\n372\t    {\n373\t      \"id\": \"FR-53\",\n374\t      \"description\": \"POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions (STUDENT) {text?, fileIds[]} applies the FR-22 to FR-24 rules. The fileIds must be the student's own uploads with context 'submission', and their number must be ≤ maxFileCount.\",\n375\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n376\t      \"source\": \"API table; FR-4.2–4.5\"\n377\t    },\n378\t    {\n379\t      \"id\": \"FR-54\",\n380\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions (manage) lists every enrolled student, including those who have not submitted, with their status, exemption and submission summary.\",\n381\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n382\t      \"source\": \"API table\"\n383\t    },\n384\t    {\n385\t      \"id\": \"FR-55\",\n386\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/submissions/:id is open to the submitting student, their parents and course managers. SubmissionHistory is included only for managers.\",\n387\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n388\t      \"source\": \"API table\"\n389\t    },\n390\t    {\n391\t      \"id\": \"FR-56\",\n392\t      \"description\": \"PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade (manage) {rawScore, penaltyPercent, feedback, rubricScores} sets gradedById/gradedAt and the computed finalScore.\",\n393\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n394\t      \"source\": \"API table; FR-5.3\"\n395\t    },\n396\t    {\n397\t      \"id\": \"FR-57\",\n398\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab= (any role) returns the role-shaped data for /assignments. studentId is accepted for parents (it must be a linked child).\",\n399\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n400\t      \"source\": \"API table; FR-6.1\"\n401\t    },\n402\t    {\n403\t      \"id\": \"FR-58\",\n404\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/students/:id/assignments (view student; uses the existing assertCanViewStudent) returns the per-student assignment list.\",\n405\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n406\t      \"source\": \"API table; FR-6.2\"\n407\t    },\n408\t    {\n409\t      \"id\": \"FR-59\",\n410\t      \"description\": \"Grading, returning, exempting and offline grading change records owned by a student, so each writes an AuditLog row through the existing audit().\",\n411\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n412\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout (mutations on records owned by someone else write AuditLog)\"\n413\t    },\n414\t    {\n415\t      \"id\": \"FR-60\",\n416\t      \"description\": \"Assignments with submissionType NO_SUBMISSION are not counted as Missing and trigger no due_soon or missing reminders. They are graded offline only.\",\n417\t      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n418\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 (NO_SUBMISSION; offline grading paragraph); Seed Data (SCI-7A NO_SUBMISSION graded offline) — the missing/reminder behaviour is not specified\"\n419\t    },\n420\t    {\n421\t      \"id\": \"FR-61\",\n422\t      \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 4 assignments (one returned with all students graded at 55–100 %; one submitted and awaiting grading with 60 % submitted and 2 late; one due in 2 days; one draft). ENG-7A gets 2 (one with a 3-criterion rubric, returned). SCI-7A gets 1 NO_SUBMISSION assignment graded offline. The seed is idempotent and skips when those courses do not exist.\",\n423\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n424\t      \"source\": \"Seed Data\"\n425\t    }\n426\t  ],\n427\t  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n428\t    {\n429\t      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n430\t      \"description\": \"Correctness: all score arithmetic uses Decimal end to end (Prisma.Decimal / decimal.js, which ships with Prisma), never JS floating point. Final scores round half-up to 2 dp.\",\n431\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n432\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n433\t    },\n434\t    {\n435\t      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n436\t      \"description\": \"Integrity: submission, deadline, late-day, visibility and reminder checks use server time only. Client timestamps are never trusted.\",\n437\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n438\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\"\n439\t    },\n440\t    {\n441\t      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n442\t      \"description\": \"Performance: the grading screen switches between students in under 300 ms by prefetching the next and previous submissions.\",\n443\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n444\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; Goals 3\"\n445\t    },\n446\t    {\n447\t      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n448\t      \"description\": \"Privacy: students never see other students' submissions, scores or files, in the API or through the file URLs.\",\n449\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n450\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 4; Acceptance Criteria 10\"\n451\t    },\n452\t    {\n453\t      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n454\t      \"description\": \"Access control is enforced server-side on every handler and server page through requireUser/requireRole and the existing assertCanViewCourse, assertCanManageCourse and assertCanViewStudent. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\",\n455\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n456\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout (requireRole.ts); Roles\"\n457\t    },\n458\t    {\n459\t      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n460\t      \"description\": \"UI component rule: Material UI v9.5.0 and MUI X only, styled through the theme, sx and styled(). No banned libraries, enforced by the ESLint no-restricted-imports rule. Every component (List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataTable/DataGrid, DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar via useToast) is looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\",\n461\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n462\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › UI component rule (1–6)\"\n463\t    },\n464\t    {\n465\t      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n466\t      \"description\": \"API conventions: route handlers are thin (Zod → service → JSON). They use the {data} / list {data,page,pageSize,total} / {error:{code,message,details}} envelopes and the standard error codes. Pagination defaults to 20 (max 100), with ?sort=&order= and ?q=.\",\n467\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n468\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n469\t    },\n470\t    {\n471\t      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n472\t      \"description\": \"Code layout: business logic goes in src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts (the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent). Zod schemas go in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts. Routes go under src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…. Pages go under src/app/(app)/….\",\n473\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n474\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n475\t    },\n476\t    {\n477\t      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n478\t      \"description\": \"Time handling: timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The late-day calculation is correct across a DST change in the school timezone and on the exact 24 h boundary (exactly 24 h late = 1 day).\",\n479\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n480\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout (UTC/school tz); Test Requirements (DST, exact 24 h boundary)\"\n481\t    },\n482\t    {\n483\t      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n484\t      \"description\": \"Markdown (instructions, submission text, feedback) is rendered with react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with every element mapped to an MUI component.\",\n485\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n486\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.2 (sanitised Markdown); UI component rule 4\"\n487\t    },\n488\t    {\n489\t      \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n490\t      \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold, rename existing routes or models, or duplicate existing helpers. Reuse notify(), notifyStudentAndParents(), audit(), registerFileAccess/contexts, the files service and /api/files, the DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, PageHeader and useToast components, formatInSchoolTz, and the courseTabs/studentTabs registries.\",\n491\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n492\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context (reuse paragraph)\"\n493\t    },\n494\t    {\n495\t      \"id\": \"NFR-12\",\n496\t      \"description\": \"Committed code has no console.log. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\",\n497\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n498\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n499\t    },\n500\t    {\n501\t      \"id\": \"NFR-13\",\n502\t      \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint, npm run typecheck and npm run test keep passing.\",\n503\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n504\t      \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints (Constraints)\"\n505\t    },\n506\t    {\n507\t      \"id\": \"NFR-14\",\n508\t      \"description\": \"Unit tests cover: the late-days calculation (exact 24 h boundary, DST change), the penalty cap, final-score rounding and rubric-sum validation. Integration tests cover: resubmission history, the return flow, reminder idempotency and the effect of exemptions on the missing list. A Playwright e2e covers: teacher creates → student submits a file → teacher grades with a rubric and returns → student sees feedback; parent sees the missing list.\",\n509\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n510\t      \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"\n511\t    },\n512\t    {\n513\t      \"id\": \"NFR-15\",\n514\t      \"description\": \"Scope guard: no plagiarism detection, peer review, group assignments, inline document annotation, or gradebook weighting / term grades (PRD-11 consumes these scores). Do not change behaviour owned by later PRDs.\",\n515\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n516\t      \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Assumptions and constraints\"\n517\t    },\n518\t    {\n519\t      \"id\": \"NFR-16\",\n520\t      \"description\": \"Usability goals: a teacher can create and publish an assignment in under 2 minutes, and can grade 30 submissions with the keyboard without leaving the grading screen.\",\n521\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n522\t      \"source\": \"Goals 1, 3\"\n523\t    },\n524\t    {\n525\t      \"id\": \"NFR-17\",\n526\t      \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, support for evergreen browsers (last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari), and basic accessibility (labelled inputs, keyboard-operable controls).\",\n527\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n528\t      \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\"\n529\t    }\n530\t  ],\n531\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n532\t  \"clarificationLog\": [\n533\t    {\n534\t      \"round\": 1,\n535\t      \"questions\": [\n536\t        \"FR-15: Does 'same relative due date' mean the identical due date-time, or the same offset from some per-course anchor such as the next class meeting in the timetable?\",\n537\t        \"FR-13: Should a SCHEDULED assignment's status flip to PUBLISHED when availableFrom passes, or is visibility only computed?\",\n538\t        \"FR-52: What may students, parents and teachers see or do with an archived assignment?\",\n539\t        \"FR-60: Does a NO_SUBMISSION assignment ever count as Missing or trigger due_soon/missing reminders?\",\n540\t        \"FR-10: Should 'next teaching day' skip holidays? (No holiday model exists before PRD-14.)\",\n541\t        \"FR-36: With allowExtraCredit, can rubric level points also exceed criterion maximums, or is extra credit raw-score only?\",\n542\t        \"FR-39/FR-6.1: What should ADMIN see on /assignments? The PRD defines only the STUDENT, PARENT and TEACHER views.\"\n543\t      ],\n544\t      \"unresolved\": [\n545\t        \"FR-15: no interactive user. Default: keep the identical dueAt, and keep the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets from dueAt.\",\n546\t        \"FR-13: default: visibility is computed at read time, and the status stays SCHEDULED.\",\n547\t        \"FR-52: default: archived assignments are hidden from students and parents, closed to new submissions, excluded from reminders, and still visible to managers (marked 'Archived').\",\n548\t        \"FR-60: default: NO_SUBMISSION assignments are excluded from Missing and from reminders.\",\n549\t        \"FR-10: default: use SchoolDay.isTeaching weekdays only.\",\n550\t        \"FR-36: default: extra credit applies to rawScore only. Rubric points stay within each criterion's maximum.\",\n551\t        \"ADMIN /assignments: default: show the TEACHER-style 'To grade' list across all courses.\"\n552\t      ]\n553\t    },\n554\t    {\n555\t      \"round\": 2,\n556\t      \"questions\": [\n557\t        \"Ticket ID: the PRD header says SCH-009, but the pipeline ticket is SH-9. Confirm that SH-9 is canonical for the artifacts.\"\n558\t      ],\n559\t      \"unresolved\": [\n560\t        \"Ticket ID: proceeding with SH-9 (from the task prompt).\"\n561\t      ]\n562\t    }\n563\t  ],\n564\t  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n565\t    \"DEPENDENCY GAP (PRD-08 incomplete): SH-8 QA FAILED. 39 of 60 requirements are not implemented. The file backend exists: FileObject, storage.ts, src/server/files/{access,contexts,files-service,validate,purge}.ts, POST /api/files and GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1. The UI does not exist: there is no FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or Markdown editor. PRD-09 needs these UI components (FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29, FR-30).\",\n566\t    \"The MUI X version mismatch persists: @mui/x-internals is 9.15.0, but @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0 needs an older export. Every page that renders DataTable/DataGrid fails to compile, and FR-17 needs a DataTable.\",\n567\t    \"vitest.config.ts imports 'vitest/config.js', which does not resolve, so `npm test` fails to start (NFR-13). vitest.tmp.config.ts works.\",\n568\t    \"next.config.js has CSP script-src 'self', which blocks hydration in a real browser. Earlier e2e runs used bypassCSP.\",\n569\t    \"studentTabs is not rendered by any page, so the FR-41 tab will not be visible until a tab bar exists. courseTabs IS rendered by src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/CourseTabs.tsx.\",\n570\t    \"Already installed: react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, file-type, and decimal.js (via Prisma). No new dependencies are needed.\",\n571\t    \"Reusable: notifyStudentAndParents() in src/server/notifications/notify.ts; the maintenance hook in src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; registerBuiltInContexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts; the Course fields teacherId and coTeacherIds.\"\n572\t  ],\n573\t  \"status\": \"complete\",\n574\t  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 78 requirements (68 HIGH, 7 MEDIUM, 3 LOW); ≥80% threshold met after round 2\"\n575\t}\n576\t{\n577\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n578\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T09:00:00Z\",\n579\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n580\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n581\t  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n582\t  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n583\t  \"detectionNotes\": \"The run mode declares '--tech-stack react', and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20 on PostgreSQL 16, and Auth.js v5 beta.25. The MUI packages (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/material-nextjs, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts) are all 9.5.0. Everything PRD-09 needs is already installed: react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, and decimal.js (shipped with Prisma; use Prisma.Decimal for score maths). No new dependencies are required. Known environment breaks: (1) @mui/x-internals 9.15.0 is mismatched with @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0, so DataGrid pages fail to compile; (2) vitest.config.ts imports 'vitest/config.js', which does not resolve; (3) the CSP script-src 'self' blocks hydration. Styling goes only through the MUI theme, sx and styled().\",\n584\t  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n585\t}\n586\t{\n587\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n588\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T09:05:00Z\",\n589\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n590\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n591\t  \"status\": \"complete\",\n592\t  \"requirementsCount\": 78,\n593\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n594\t  \"blockers\": [\n595\t    \"DEPENDENCY GAP: PRD-08 (SH-8) failed QA. Its UI layer was never built: there is no FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or Markdown editor component. PRD-09 FR-9/19/20/29/30 depend on them. Architect must decide how to cover this, e.g. build the minimal shared FileUpload and MarkdownView/MarkdownEditor in src/components/ inside this ticket. The backend is reusable as-is: POST /api/files (context field), GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, registerFileAccess and the files service.\",\n596\t    \"ENV BREAK: @mui/x-internals 9.15.0 is mismatched with @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0, so DataTable/DataGrid pages fail to compile. FR-17 (the teacher assignments table) needs it. Either align the MUI X versions in package.json or the lockfile, or render the table without DataGrid. This needs a decision.\",\n597\t    \"ENV BREAK: vitest.config.ts imports 'vitest/config.js', which does not resolve, so `npm test` does not start (NFR-13). Fix the import to 'vitest/config', or keep using vitest.tmp.config.ts.\",\n598\t    \"ENV BREAK: next.config.js has CSP script-src 'self', which blocks hydration in a real browser. The NFR-14 Playwright flow needs bypassCSP (as before) or a CSP fix.\",\n599\t    \"studentTabs has no renderer, so the FR-41 Assignments student tab will be registered but not visible until a tab bar exists on /students/[id]/*.\",\n600\t    \"LOW-confidence defaults to confirm: FR-15 (duplicate keeps the same dueAt), FR-52 (archived behaviour), FR-60 (NO_SUBMISSION excluded from missing and reminders).\",\n601\t    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents(), notify() + NOTIFICATION_TYPES (category ACADEMIC), audit(), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent, registerBuiltInContexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts (add 'assignment' and 'submission'), the maintenance hook in src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts (add sendDueReminders()), the courseTabs/studentTabs registries, formatInSchoolTz, and the ConfirmDialog/EmptyState/PageHeader/useToast/DataTable components.\",\n602\t    \"NFR-6: Dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0 and MUI X 9.5.0) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n603\t  ],\n604\t  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n605\t}\n606\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78","uuid":"1cd140ac-bfec-46e1-9467-0af53f158a23","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:23:50.157Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78/tool-results/bhfyzfk5j.txt","content":"approvals\narchitect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\nqa\nrun-summary.json\ntelemetry\nui-verification\n\nartifacts/approvals:\narchitect-approval.json\ndev-planning-approval.json\nintake-approval.json\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-log.md\ndev-rerun-count.json\nsecurity-scan-report.json\ntask-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/qa:\ncoverage-report.md\nqa-report.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T09:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-09: Assignments & Submissions\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-009 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-9.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the Prisma enums SubmissionType (ONLINE_TEXT, FILE_UPLOAD, TEXT_AND_FILE, NO_SUBMISSION), AssignmentStatus (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and SubmissionStatus (SUBMITTED, RETURNED) in a new prisma migrate migration.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (enum block)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Add an Assignment model with the fields listed in FR-1. Also add allowExtraCredit Boolean @default(false) (from FR-5.6), notifiedAt DateTime? (from FR-7.1) and archivedAt DateTime? (from the API table). Add a Course→Assignment relation (onDelete Cascade), a rubricId @unique relation to Rubric, and @@index([courseId, dueAt]).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 model Assignment; FR-5.6; FR-7.1; API table (DELETE row)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the models AssignmentAttachment (assignment↔FileObject), Rubric and RubricCriterion. RubricCriterion has title, description?, maxPoints Decimal(6,2), order, and levels Json [{label, points, description}].\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 models AssignmentAttachment, Rubric, RubricCriterion\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the models Submission (@@unique([assignmentId, studentId]), with Decimal rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore and Json rubricScores [{criterionId, points, comment}]), SubmissionFile (submission↔FileObject) and SubmissionHistory (attemptNumber, text, fileIds String[], submittedAt).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 models Submission, SubmissionFile, SubmissionHistory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a GradeExemption model with a composite id (assignmentId, studentId), an optional reason and createdAt.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 model GradeExemption\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Add an AssignmentReminder table {assignmentId, studentId, kind} with a unique key on all three columns. It makes the due_soon and missing reminders idempotent.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.2 (AssignmentReminder table)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"Enforce the field limits in Zod schemas in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts, shared by forms and handlers: title ≤150; instructions ≤50,000; maxPoints 0–1000; lateCutoffAt > dueAt; latePenaltyPercentPerDay and maxLatePenaltyPercent 0–100; maxFileCount 1–10; submission text ≤50,000; feedback ≤10,000.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 field comments; Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"A teacher can record a grade for a student who did not submit. The service creates a Submission with text = null, no files, submittedAt = gradedAt and attemptNumber = 0 (the offline/no-submission marker).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 (paragraph after the schema); FR-5.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the create/edit page at /courses/[courseId]/assignments/new. Fields: title, Markdown instructions (the PRD-08 editor), attachments (FileUpload, context 'assignment'), submission type, max points, due date-time (school timezone), optional available-from, late policy (allow-late toggle → cutoff, penalty per day, maximum penalty), maximum file count, allow extra credit, and an optional rubric builder.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2.1; FR-5.6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Default the due date-time to the next teaching day at 23:59 in the school timezone. 'Teaching day' is taken from the existing SchoolDay.isTeaching weekday table, because holidays are not modelled before PRD-14.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2.1 (default next teaching day 23:59); prisma SchoolDay model (PRD-06)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Rubric builder: add, reorder and remove criteria (title, description, levels with label + points + description). The sum of the criterion maximums must equal max points. Otherwise show the inline error 'Rubric totals {sum} points but the assignment is worth {maxPoints}.', and the server rejects the save with VALIDATION_ERROR.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2.2; Acceptance Criteria 5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"Offer 'Save draft' (DRAFT), 'Publish' (PUBLISHED) and 'Schedule' (SCHEDULED). Schedule requires an available-from in the future, and the assignment stays hidden from students and parents until then.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2.3; FR-1 (availableFrom comment)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"A SCHEDULED assignment counts as visible once availableFrom ≤ server now. Visibility is computed at read time. No background job rewrites the status to PUBLISHED.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2.3 ('becomes visible then'); FR-7.1 ('when scheduled becomes visible on first student list load')\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Editing the due date or max points of a published assignment that has submissions shows a warning. Changing max points recalculates nothing: existing scores are kept, and a banner prompts the teacher to review grades.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"A 'Duplicate to other courses' action copies the assignment as DRAFT to selected courses the teacher manages (POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}). The copy keeps the instructions, attachments, settings and rubric. The copy keeps the same due date-time, and availableFrom/lateCutoffAt keep their offsets from dueAt.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-2.5 ('with the same relative due date'); API table (duplicate row)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"description\": \"Register an 'Assignments' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts for all roles that can view the course.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"description\": \"Teacher/admin view of the course Assignments tab: a table with title, due date, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted and a 'Grade' button.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-3.1 (teacher view)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n      \"description\": \"Student view of the course Assignments tab: a list grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned. Parents see the same view, read-only, for their linked child.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-3.1 (student view, parent view)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"description\": \"The assignment page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId] shows the instructions (sanitised Markdown), attachments, due date, late policy summary, rubric (if any) and the submission panel. When under 48 hours remain, it adds a live countdown such as 'Due in 5 h 12 min'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"description\": \"The submission panel shows a Markdown text editor and/or file upload, depending on submissionType (NO_SUBMISSION shows neither). File upload respects maxFileCount. Draft text autosaves to localStorage only, never to the server.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"description\": \"Clicking Submit opens a confirmation Dialog before the POST.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n      \"description\": \"Server submission rules: the assignment is visible; the student is ACTIVE-enrolled in the course; the student is not exempt. If now > dueAt, allowLate must be true and now ≤ lateCutoffAt (when set). Otherwise return VALIDATION_ERROR 'The deadline has passed and late submissions are closed.'\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.3; Acceptance Criteria 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n      \"description\": \"On submit, compute isLate = submittedAt > dueAt and lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h), using server time. For example, due Mon 23:59 and submitted Wed 10:00 gives lateDays = 2.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.4; Acceptance Criteria 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"description\": \"Resubmission is allowed until dueAt (or lateCutoffAt / indefinitely when late is allowed) and only while status = SUBMITTED. It copies the previous attempt into SubmissionHistory, increments attemptNumber, and clears rawScore, penaltyPercent, finalScore, feedback, rubricScores, gradedById and gradedAt. Once the work is RETURNED, resubmission is refused.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.5; Acceptance Criteria 3, 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"description\": \"After submitting, the student sees a receipt such as 'Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)', in the school timezone, plus the files and text submitted.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"description\": \"After return, the student sees the final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and the late penalty applied.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-4.7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"description\": \"Until the work is returned, the student and parent see 'Submitted — awaiting grading'. No score, rubric scores or feedback are sent in the API response.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria 7; FR-5.4 ('Save' = not yet visible to student)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n      \"description\": \"Grading page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade, left panel: an MUI List of all enrolled students with status Chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter, and sorting by name or submission time.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"description\": \"Grading main panel: the selected submission's text as sanitised Markdown, and its files listed with inline preview for images and PDFs (<img>/<iframe> to /api/files/:id?inline=1, which already exists). Previous attempts (SubmissionHistory) are available in a dropdown.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"description\": \"Grading form. With a rubric, each criterion is an exclusive ToggleButtonGroup of levels, and the selected points auto-sum into the raw score (for example 8 + 9 → 17). Without a rubric, the raw score is entered directly. The late penalty is pre-filled as min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty) and can be overridden. The final score is computed live. There is a Markdown feedback editor.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.3; Acceptance Criteria 1, 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"description\": \"finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100), rounded half-up to 2 dp. For example, raw 18 with 20 % → 14.40. It is computed server-side at grading time.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 (finalScore comment); NFR-1 Correctness; Acceptance Criteria 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"description\": \"Grading buttons: 'Save' (graded, not visible to the student), 'Save & return' (returns this submission and sets returnedAt) and the bulk 'Return all graded' (POST /api/assignments/:id/return; submissionIds optional, defaults to all graded and unreturned).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.4; API table (return row)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"description\": \"Keyboard shortcuts on the grading screen: J = next student, K = previous student, Ctrl+Enter = save and go to the next student. The shortcuts are not captured while typing in text fields, except Ctrl+Enter.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.4; Goals 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"description\": \"'Grade without submission' for students who did not submit (POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}). It creates the attemptNumber = 0 Submission described in FR-8.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.5; FR-1 paragraph; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-35\",\n      \"description\": \"An 'Exempt' toggle (PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId) writes or deletes a GradeExemption. Exempt students are removed from missing counts and lists, get no due_soon or missing reminders, cannot submit, and are flagged for exclusion from future gradebook calculation (PRD-11).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.5; FR-4.3 (not exempt); FR-6.1 (Missing not exempt); API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-36\",\n      \"description\": \"Validate scores server-side: rawScore and the rubric points must be within 0..maxPoints. When allowExtraCredit is true, rawScore may go up to 120 % of maxPoints. penaltyPercent must be 0–100.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.6; FR-1 (penaltyPercent range)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-37\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the /assignments page for STUDENT. It lists every assignment across the student's ACTIVE enrollments in four tabs: Upcoming (sorted by due date), Missing (past due, not submitted, not exempt), Submitted and Returned. There is a course filter.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Goals 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-38\",\n      \"description\": \"The /assignments page for PARENT has a child selector (linked students only) and shows the same content as the student view, read-only.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.1 (PARENT)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-39\",\n      \"description\": \"The /assignments page for TEACHER is a 'To grade' list of submitted, ungraded submissions across the courses they teach (teacherId or coTeacherIds), oldest first.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.1 (TEACHER)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-40\",\n      \"description\": \"Add an 'Assignments' nav entry for /assignments to src/config/navigation.ts for STUDENT, PARENT and TEACHER.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout ('A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry'); FR-6.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-41\",\n      \"description\": \"Register an 'Assignments' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts. It shows the same per-student data to teachers and admins who view the student (GET /api/students/:id/assignments).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-6.2; API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-42\",\n      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.published to ACTIVE-enrolled students (in-app; email default false). It is sent on publish, or for SCHEDULED assignments on the first student list load after availableFrom. It is sent exactly once, using Assignment.notifiedAt (set atomically).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-43\",\n      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.due_soon to students with no submission (and not exempt) once dueAt − 24 h has passed and before dueAt. sendDueReminders() runs on every PRD-04 maintenance dispatcher call (src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts). It is idempotent via the AssignmentReminder unique key (kind 'due_soon').\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criteria 8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-44\",\n      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.returned to the student and their parents through the existing notifyStudentAndParents(). The body includes course, title and score, for example 'Mathematics: Fractions worksheet — 18/20'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-45\",\n      \"description\": \"Register and send assignment.missing to parents only (email default true), once per student, 24 hours after dueAt if the student has still not submitted and is not exempt. It is idempotent via AssignmentReminder (kind 'missing') and runs in the same sendDueReminders() maintenance pass.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7.4; Acceptance Criteria 9\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the four notification types to NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts with the category ACADEMIC and the role lists that match their recipients.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-7 ('Register and send'); Platform Context (notification type keys registered in types.ts)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-47\",\n      \"description\": \"Register two file access contexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts: 'assignment' (anyone who can view the assignment, with visibility rules applied) and 'submission' (the submitting student, their linked parents, course managers and admins). Any other user is denied.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-8.1; Acceptance Criteria 10\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-48\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/courses/:id/assignments (view course) returns a role-shaped list. Managers get every status with counts. Students and parents get only visible, non-archived assignments, with their own submission state.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-49\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/courses/:id/assignments (manage course) creates an assignment with its rubric and attachments.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-50\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/assignments/:id (view). For students and parents the response includes their own submission, with grading fields only once returned.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table; Acceptance Criteria 7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-51\",\n      \"description\": \"PATCH /api/assignments/:id (manage). DELETE /api/assignments/:id (manage) hard-deletes only when there are no submissions. Otherwise it sets archivedAt.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table (PATCH/DELETE row)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-52\",\n      \"description\": \"Archived assignments are hidden from student and parent lists, /assignments, reminders and new submissions. Managers can still see them.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"source\": \"API table ('otherwise archive (add archivedAt)') — the behaviour of an archived assignment is not specified\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-53\",\n      \"description\": \"POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions (STUDENT) {text?, fileIds[]} applies the FR-22 to FR-24 rules. The fileIds must be the student's own uploads with context 'submission', and their number must be ≤ maxFileCount.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table; FR-4.2–4.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-54\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions (manage) lists every enrolled student, including those who have not submitted, with their status, exemption and submission summary.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-55\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/submissions/:id is open to the submitting student, their parents and course managers. SubmissionHistory is included only for managers.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-56\",\n      \"description\": \"PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade (manage) {rawScore, penaltyPercent, feedback, rubricScores} sets gradedById/gradedAt and the computed finalScore.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table; FR-5.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-57\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab= (any role) returns the role-shaped data for /assignments. studentId is accepted for parents (it must be a linked child).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table; FR-6.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-58\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/students/:id/assignments (view student; uses the existing assertCanViewStudent) returns the per-student assignment list.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"API table; FR-6.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-59\",\n      \"description\": \"Grading, returning, exempting and offline grading change records owned by a student, so each writes an AuditLog row through the existing audit().\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout (mutations on records owned by someone else write AuditLog)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-60\",\n      \"description\": \"Assignments with submissionType NO_SUBMISSION are not counted as Missing and trigger no due_soon or missing reminders. They are graded offline only.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-1 (NO_SUBMISSION; offline grading paragraph); Seed Data (SCI-7A NO_SUBMISSION graded offline) — the missing/reminder behaviour is not specified\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-61\",\n      \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 4 assignments (one returned with all students graded at 55–100 %; one submitted and awaiting grading with 60 % submitted and 2 late; one due in 2 days; one draft). ENG-7A gets 2 (one with a 3-criterion rubric, returned). SCI-7A gets 1 NO_SUBMISSION assignment graded offline. The seed is idempotent and skips when those courses do not exist.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Seed Data\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Correctness: all score arithmetic uses Decimal end to end (Prisma.Decimal / decimal.js, which ships with Prisma), never JS floating point. Final scores round half-up to 2 dp.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Integrity: submission, deadline, late-day, visibility and reminder checks use server time only. Client timestamps are never trusted.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Performance: the grading screen switches between students in under 300 ms by prefetching the next and previous submissions.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; Goals 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Privacy: students never see other students' submissions, scores or files, in the API or through the file URLs.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 4; Acceptance Criteria 10\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Access control is enforced server-side on every handler and server page through requireUser/requireRole and the existing assertCanViewCourse, assertCanManageCourse and assertCanViewStudent. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout (requireRole.ts); Roles\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"UI component rule: Material UI v9.5.0 and MUI X only, styled through the theme, sx and styled(). No banned libraries, enforced by the ESLint no-restricted-imports rule. Every component (List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataTable/DataGrid, DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar via useToast) is looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › UI component rule (1–6)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"API conventions: route handlers are thin (Zod → service → JSON). They use the {data} / list {data,page,pageSize,total} / {error:{code,message,details}} envelopes and the standard error codes. Pagination defaults to 20 (max 100), with ?sort=&order= and ?q=.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Code layout: business logic goes in src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts (the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent). Zod schemas go in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts. Routes go under src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…. Pages go under src/app/(app)/….\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Time handling: timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The late-day calculation is correct across a DST change in the school timezone and on the exact 24 h boundary (exactly 24 h late = 1 day).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout (UTC/school tz); Test Requirements (DST, exact 24 h boundary)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Markdown (instructions, submission text, feedback) is rendered with react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with every element mapped to an MUI component.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"FR-5.2 (sanitised Markdown); UI component rule 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold, rename existing routes or models, or duplicate existing helpers. Reuse notify(), notifyStudentAndParents(), audit(), registerFileAccess/contexts, the files service and /api/files, the DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, PageHeader and useToast components, formatInSchoolTz, and the courseTabs/studentTabs registries.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context (reuse paragraph)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"Committed code has no console.log. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint, npm run typecheck and npm run test keep passing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints (Constraints)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Unit tests cover: the late-days calculation (exact 24 h boundary, DST change), the penalty cap, final-score rounding and rubric-sum validation. Integration tests cover: resubmission history, the return flow, reminder idempotency and the effect of exemptions on the missing list. A Playwright e2e covers: teacher creates → student submits a file → teacher grades with a rubric and returns → student sees feedback; parent sees the missing list.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Scope guard: no plagiarism detection, peer review, group assignments, inline document annotation, or gradebook weighting / term grades (PRD-11 consumes these scores). Do not change behaviour owned by later PRDs.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Assumptions and constraints\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-16\",\n      \"description\": \"Usability goals: a teacher can create and publish an assignment in under 2 minutes, and can grade 30 submissions with the keyboard without leaving the grading screen.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"Goals 1, 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-17\",\n      \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, support for evergreen browsers (last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari), and basic accessibility (labelled inputs, keyboard-operable controls).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-15: Does 'same relative due date' mean the identical due date-time, or the same offset from some per-course anchor such as the next class meeting in the timetable?\",\n        \"FR-13: Should a SCHEDULED assignment's status flip to PUBLISHED when availableFrom passes, or is visibility only computed?\",\n        \"FR-52: What may students, parents and teachers see or do with an archived assignment?\",\n        \"FR-60: Does a NO_SUBMISSION assignment ever count as Missing or trigger due_soon/missing reminders?\",\n        \"FR-10: Should 'next teaching day' skip holidays? (No holiday model exists before PRD-14.)\",\n        \"FR-36: With allowExtraCredit, can rubric level points also exceed criterion maximums, or is extra credit raw-score only?\",\n        \"FR-39/FR-6.1: What should ADMIN see on /assignments? The PRD defines only the STUDENT, PARENT and TEACHER views.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-15: no interactive user. Default: keep the identical dueAt, and keep the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets from dueAt.\",\n        \"FR-13: default: visibility is computed at read time, and the status stays SCHEDULED.\",\n        \"FR-52: default: archived assignments are hidden from students and parents, closed to new submissions, excluded from reminders, and still visible to managers (marked 'Archived').\",\n        \"FR-60: default: NO_SUBMISSION assignments are excluded from Missing and from reminders.\",\n        \"FR-10: default: use SchoolDay.isTeaching weekdays only.\",\n        \"FR-36: default: extra credit applies to rawScore only. Rubric points stay within each criterion's maximum.\",\n        \"ADMIN /assignments: default: show the TEACHER-style 'To grade' list across all courses.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"round\": 2,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"Ticket ID: the PRD header says SCH-009, but the pipeline ticket is SH-9. Confirm that SH-9 is canonical for the artifacts.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"Ticket ID: proceeding with SH-9 (from the task prompt).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"DEPENDENCY GAP (PRD-08 incomplete): SH-8 QA FAILED. 39 of 60 requirements are not implemented. The file backend exists: FileObject, storage.ts, src/server/files/{access,contexts,files-service,validate,purge}.ts, POST /api/files and GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1. The UI does not exist: there is no FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or Markdown editor. PRD-09 needs these UI components (FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29, FR-30).\",\n    \"The MUI X version mismatch persists: @mui/x-internals is 9.15.0, but @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0 needs an older export. Every page that renders DataTable/DataGrid fails to compile, and FR-17 needs a DataTable.\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts imports 'vitest/config.js', which does not resolve, so `npm test` fails to start (NFR-13). vitest.tmp.config.ts works.\",\n    \"next.config.js has CSP script-src 'self', which blocks hydration in a real browser. Earlier e2e runs used bypassCSP.\",\n    \"studentTabs is not rendered by any page, so the FR-41 tab will not be visible until a tab bar exists. courseTabs IS rendered by src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/CourseTabs.tsx.\",\n    \"Already installed: react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, file-type, and decimal.js (via Prisma). No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"Reusable: notifyStudentAndParents() in src/server/notifications/notify.ts; the maintenance hook in src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; registerBuiltInContexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts; the Course fields teacherId and coTeacherIds.\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 78 requirements (68 HIGH, 7 MEDIUM, 3 LOW); ≥80% threshold met after round 2\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T09:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"The run mode declares '--tech-stack react', and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20 on PostgreSQL 16, and Auth.js v5 beta.25. The MUI packages (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/material-nextjs, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts) are all 9.5.0. Everything PRD-09 needs is already installed: react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, and decimal.js (shipped with Prisma; use Prisma.Decimal for score maths). No new dependencies are required. Known environment breaks: (1) @mui/x-internals 9.15.0 is mismatched with @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0, so DataGrid pages fail to compile; (2) vitest.config.ts imports 'vitest/config.js', which does not resolve; (3) the CSP script-src 'self' blocks hydration. Styling goes only through the MUI theme, sx and styled().\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T09:05:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 78,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"DEPENDENCY GAP: PRD-08 (SH-8) failed QA. Its UI layer was never built: there is no FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or Markdown editor component. PRD-09 FR-9/19/20/29/30 depend on them. Architect must decide how to cover this, e.g. build the minimal shared FileUpload and MarkdownView/MarkdownEditor in src/components/ inside this ticket. The backend is reusable as-is: POST /api/files (context field), GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, registerFileAccess and the files service.\",\n    \"ENV BREAK: @mui/x-internals 9.15.0 is mismatched with @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0, so DataTable/DataGrid pages fail to compile. FR-17 (the teacher assignments table) needs it. Either align the MUI X versions in package.json or the lockfile, or render the table without DataGrid. This needs a decision.\",\n    \"ENV BREAK: vitest.config.ts imports 'vitest/config.js', which does not resolve, so `npm test` does not start (NFR-13). Fix the import to 'vitest/config', or keep using vitest.tmp.config.ts.\",\n    \"ENV BREAK: next.config.js has CSP script-src 'self', which blocks hydration in a real browser. The NFR-14 Playwright flow needs bypassCSP (as before) or a CSP fix.\",\n    \"studentTabs has no renderer, so the FR-41 Assignments student tab will be registered but not visible until a tab bar exists on /students/[id]/*.\",\n    \"LOW-confidence defaults to confirm: FR-15 (duplicate keeps the same dueAt), FR-52 (archived behaviour), FR-60 (NO_SUBMISSION excluded from missing and reminders).\",\n    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents(), notify() + NOTIFICATION_TYPES (category ACADEMIC), audit(), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent, registerBuiltInContexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts (add 'assignment' and 'submission'), the maintenance hook in src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts (add sendDueReminders()), the courseTabs/studentTabs registries, formatInSchoolTz, and the ConfirmDialog/EmptyState/PageHeader/useToast/DataTable components.\",\n    \"NFR-6: Dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0 and MUI X 9.5.0) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n","numLines":606,"startLine":1,"totalLines":606}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LBgSiKikdQeqdFMJomNiuy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
