{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgro9YArK1GBFkLQ1LjDt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0` was ever published. The versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0, so 9.1.0 is the version that was current when `x-data-grid` 9.5.0 shipped. I have enough to write the ADRs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":864,"cache_read_input_tokens":50132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":864},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78","uuid":"b31f3067-5372-4897-a152-11e181d6d925","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:24:15.178Z","request_id":"req_011Cgro9XxhZa73FCpSNEH2C"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgro9YArK1GBFkLQ1LjDt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014wFkAWGekx5rK6fc1sPsJ4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n\nNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n\n**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n\n**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n\n**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n\n**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n\n**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n\n**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n\n**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n\n**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n\n**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n\n**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n\nUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n\n**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n\n**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n\n**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n\n**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n\n---\n\n## Blockers carried forward\n\n1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":864,"cache_read_input_tokens":50132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":864},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78","uuid":"fb0f7e29-ff29-4f34-bcb1-84760f27704f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:25:02.553Z","request_id":"req_011Cgro9XxhZa73FCpSNEH2C","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014wFkAWGekx5rK6fc1sPsJ4":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n\nNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n\n**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n\n**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n\n**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n\n**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n\n**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n\n**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n\n**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n\n**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n\n**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n\n**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n\nUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n\n**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n\n**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n\n**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n\n**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n\n---\n\n## Blockers carried forward\n\n1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n"}}}
{"type":"rate_limit_event","rate_limit_info":{"status":"allowed","resetsAt":1794219000,"rateLimitType":"five_hour","overageStatus":"allowed","overageResetsAt":1796083200,"isUsingOverage":false,"unifiedWindows":{"five_hour":{"utilization":0.19,"resetsAt":1794219000,"status":"allowed"},"seven_day":{"utilization":0.02,"resetsAt":1794718800,"status":"allowed"}}},"uuid":"80e62c1b-a719-49fa-ad95-67a593de6af4","session_id":"a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014wFkAWGekx5rK6fc1sPsJ4","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78","uuid":"1557ed71-c291-47dc-9f30-bd05edba1d37","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:25:02.673Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n\nNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n\n**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n\n**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n\n**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n\n**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n\n**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n\n**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n\n**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n\n**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n\n**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n\n**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n\nUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n\n**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n\n**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n\n**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n\n**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n\n---\n\n## Blockers carried forward\n\n1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":125,"newStart":1,"newLines":113,"lines":["-# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)","+# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions"," ","-Ticket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict (`moduleResolution: bundler`), Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5 beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers with `AdapterDateFns` already in `src/app/providers.tsx`, x-charts), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1, date-fns/date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `package.json` declares `engines.node >=18.18.0`, and local Node is 24.11.1. Nothing in the requirements calls for a different stack. The ADRs below cover how this feature fits into the existing stack and pin the new dependencies.","+**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`."," ","+None of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.","+"," ---"," ","-## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions","+## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies"," ","-**Context.** NFR-9 limits new dependencies to file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable. The latest file-type (22.x) declares `engines.node >=22` and 21.x declares `>=20`. Either would break the repo's `>=18.18.0` engine contract. All five packages are ESM-only.","+**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`)."," ","-**Decision.** Install these exact pins:","-| Package | Version | Why this version |","+**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:","+| Need | Use | Req |"," |---|---|---|","-| `file-type` | `20.5.0` | Newest line with `engines.node >=18`. Use `fileTypeFromBuffer` (FR-5, FR-6). |","-| `react-markdown` | `10.1.0` | Peer is `react >=18` (FR-31). |","-| `remark-gfm` | `4.0.1` | Supports tables and strikethrough for FR-25 and FR-31. |","-| `rehype-sanitize` | `6.0.0` | Provides NFR-2 sanitisation. |","-| `@dnd-kit/sortable` | `10.0.0` | Peer is `@dnd-kit/core ^6.3.0`, which matches the installed 6.3.1 (FR-23). |","+| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |","+| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |","+| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |","+| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |","+| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |","+| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |"," ","-ESM-only packages import cleanly into App Router server and client code under `moduleResolution: bundler`, so `transpilePackages` is not needed. Add it only if `next build` complains.","+**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side."," ","-**Consequences.** No engine bump is needed. Do not upgrade file-type past 20.x without also raising `engines.node`. NFR-11 (single local-disk storage, no S3 SDK) means no cloud dependency is added.","-"," ---"," ","-## ADR-2: Parse multipart uploads with `busboy` (already installed via Next.js), not `request.formData()`","+## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`"," ","-**Context.** NFR-5 requires uploads to stream to disk, with sha256 computed and the size limit enforced during the stream. In Next 14, `Request.formData()` buffers the whole body in memory, which violates NFR-5 for 25 MB files (FR-4). `busboy@1.6.0` is already in `node_modules` as a direct dependency of `next@14.2.18` (`npm ls busboy`). Adding another parser would break NFR-9.","+**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established."," ","-**Decision.** `POST /api/files` (FR-3) runs on the Node runtime (`export const runtime = 'nodejs'`). It pipes `Readable.fromWeb(req.body)` into `busboy({ headers, limits: { files: 1, fileSize: MAX_UPLOAD_MB*1024*1024 } })`. The file stream goes through a `crypto.createHash('sha256')` tap and into `storage.saveFile()` (FR-2), which writes to a temp path under `UPLOAD_DIR` and then `rename`s it to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>` (FR-1). Busboy's `limit` event aborts the upload, deletes the temp file and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'` (FR-4). Type sniffing (ADR-3) runs on the first chunk(s) before the write is committed. The `context` field must come before the file part in the multipart body because the logo rules (FR-40, FR-41) depend on it. FileUpload (FR-13) appends `context` first.","+**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket."," ","-**Consequences.** busboy is a transitive dependency, so `@types/busboy` is not available. Declare a minimal local type or accept `any` at that one call site, with a `ponytail:` comment explaining it. If a Next upgrade drops busboy, add `busboy` explicitly at that point. The intake handoff should note this as the only deviation from the dependency list, and it is a zero-install one. The rate limit check (NFR-3, `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` from `src/server/rate-limit.ts`) runs before any bytes are read.","+**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-3: Validate file types with an extension allowlist plus `file-type` sniffing of the head buffer, using an explicit table","+## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config"," ","-**Context.** FR-5 requires checks on both the extension and the magic number. FR-6 notes that txt/csv have no signature and that docx/xlsx/pptx can sniff as `zip`. FR-41 allows SVG only for `logo`, and SVG is text, so file-type cannot detect it reliably. The Vitest environment is `jsdom`, so file-type's `\"node\"` export condition may not resolve there, while `fileTypeFromBuffer` exists in both the node and core entries.","+**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`)."," ","-**Decision.** In `src/server/files/validate.ts`, keep one `ALLOWED: Record<ext, { mimes: string[]; sniff: 'required' | 'none' | 'zip-or-ooxml' }>` table:","-- Binary types (pdf, doc, xls, ppt, png, jpg/jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4, zip): the sniffed mime must be in `mimes`. doc/xls/ppt sniff as `application/x-cfb`.","-- docx/xlsx/pptx: the sniffed type is `application/zip` or the matching OOXML mime.","-- txt/csv and svg (logo only): sniffing must return `undefined`. If any signature is detected (for example an ELF, PE or zip disguised as .csv), the file is rejected. SVG also requires the head to contain `<svg`, and is limited to 2 MB under context `logo` (FR-40). The logo context also limits extensions to png, jpg, jpeg, webp and svg.","-- The stored `mimeType` comes from the table, not from the client's Content-Type header.","-- Call `fileTypeFromBuffer(head)` on the first 4100 bytes collected from the stream. `head` is a tee of the first chunks, not a re-read.","+**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags."," ","-**Consequences.** The rules are deterministic and testable as a pure function (FR-48). Integration tests that touch busboy or the filesystem add `// @vitest-environment node`. Errors use the FR-5 message `File type .<ext> is not allowed.`","+**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-4: Store files on local disk outside `public/`, serve them only through a Node route handler, and set headers per response","+## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec"," ","-**Context.** NFR-1 says files are never served from a static path. FR-8 sets nosniff, attachment and inline rules. FR-41 sets a CSP for SVG logos. FR-10 requires `logo` to be readable without a session. `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/` path that is not in `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (`src/config/public-routes.ts`). `next.config.js` already sends a site-wide `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a CSP of `default-src 'self'` on `/:path*`.","+**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security."," ","-**Decision.**","-- `src/server/storage.ts` uses `node:fs/promises` and `node:stream/promises` only. `UPLOAD_DIR` is resolved with `path.resolve` and defaults to `./uploads`. Every storage key is checked to stay under `UPLOAD_DIR` after resolution, as a path-traversal guard. This is the only implementation (NFR-11).","-- `GET /api/files/:id` runs on `runtime = 'nodejs'` and returns `new Response(Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream(...)))` with `Content-Type` set to the stored mime, `Content-Length` set to `sizeBytes`, `nosniff`, and `Content-Disposition` set to `attachment` (or `inline` only for image/* or pdf with `?inline=1`) plus an RFC 5987 `filename*`. SVG responses also set `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. If next.config's global CSP is also sent, browsers enforce the stricter intersection, so no config change is needed for this route.","-- Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` so unauthenticated logo fetches reach the handler. The handler then runs the access registry (FR-9) for every request: `auth()` returns `null` for anonymous users, and only the `logo` resolver accepts a null user. Every other context returns 404 without reading bytes (NFR-8).","-- `.gitignore`: create one at the repo root containing `uploads/`, plus `node_modules`, `.next` and `.env` if missing. `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (NFR-12).","+**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff."," ","-**Consequences.** Opening the middleware gate moves the auth decision into the handler, so the access registry must deny by default (FR-9: an unknown context is owner/ADMIN only, and an anonymous user is denied). Integration tests must cover anonymous requests for a lesson file (expect 404) and for a logo (expect 200).","+**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-5: Allow the video-embed origins in the site CSP via `frame-src`","+## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket"," ","-**Context.** FR-30 embeds `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` and `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` iframes. The current CSP has `default-src 'self'` and no `frame-src`, so the browser would block both embeds.","+**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication."," ","-**Decision.** Add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com;` to the CSP string in `next.config.js`. The URL parser lives in `src/lib/video.ts` as a pure function shared by the Zod validator (FR-16) and the viewer (FR-32). It only emits those two origins.","+**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:","+- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).","+- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).","+- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.","+- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29)."," ","-**Consequences.** This is a one-line config change. The `X-Frame-Options: DENY` header only stops other sites from framing SchoolHub, so it does not affect these embeds. Playwright should check that the iframe loads (it is not CSP-blocked) on the seeded YouTube lesson (FR-47).","+Use the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency."," ","----","+**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15)."," ","-## ADR-6: Render Markdown with react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize, map every element to MUI, and restrict images to same origin","-","-**Context.** FR-31 and NFR-2 require sanitised Markdown with `img` allowed from same origin only and MUI element mapping (NFR-7). The current CSP has `img-src 'self' data:`.","-","-**Decision.** `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` is a client-safe component (no hooks, so it also renders on the server) with `remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}` and `rehypePlugins={[[rehypeSanitize, schema]]}`. `schema` extends `defaultSchema` and limits `img` `src` to relative paths: `protocols.src: []` plus a check that the value starts with `/`. The default schema already drops `javascript:` hrefs. A `components` map converts h1–h6, p, a, ul/ol/li, table/thead/tbody/tr/th/td, hr, blockquote, code and pre into MUI Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External `a` elements get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`. The editor Preview tab (FR-25) uses the same component.","-","-**Consequences.** One renderer is used everywhere, so a sanitisation regression shows up in one unit test with `<script>`, `javascript:` and off-origin `img` cases (FR-48). No CSP change is needed for images.","-"," ---"," ","-## ADR-7: Implement reordering with @dnd-kit/sortable, persist the whole order in one transaction, and provide keyboard IconButtons","+## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults"," ","-**Context.** FR-23 covers drag within and across modules, with the full ordering sent to `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder`. NFR-6 requires a keyboard alternative. @dnd-kit/core is already installed.","+**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`."," ","-**Decision.** Each module's lesson List is a `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`, all inside one `DndContext`, and cross-container moves are handled in `onDragOver`. Up/down `IconButton`s modify the same client order array. The server validates that every submitted module and lesson id belongs to the course and that the set equals the existing set. It then writes `position`/`moduleId` for all rows inside one `prisma.$transaction`. A course has at most about 200 lessons (NFR-4), so updating every row is acceptable.","+**Decision.**","+- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.","+- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.","+- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`."," ","-**Consequences.** Reorder is a single idempotent call with no partial states. The update count is O(n) per reorder, which is fine at this scale.","+**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-8: Read content with a bounded number of Prisma queries and compute visibility in TypeScript","+## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only"," ","-**Context.** NFR-4 requires the Content tab to render 20×10 lessons in under 600 ms with no N+1 queries. FR-18 evaluates visibility at read time, with no background job.","+**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4)."," ","-**Decision.** `GET /api/courses/:id/modules` and the Content tab server component call `content-service.listCourseContent(user, courseId)`. That function makes one `module.findMany` with `include: { lessons: { include: { _count: { select: { attachments: true } } } } }` ordered by position, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany` for the student's lessons in that course when the caller is a STUDENT. That is two queries in total. `isVisible(entity, now)` is a pure function in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` and is unit tested (FR-48). Both module and lesson must be visible. Add an `@@index([courseId, position])` on Module and an `@@index([moduleId, position])` on Lesson.","+**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers."," ","-**Consequences.** Visibility is not pushed into SQL. At 200 rows per course, filtering in memory costs nothing, and having the rule in one place means the viewer (FR-32), the Learning tab (FR-35) and FR-44 all agree.","+**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-9: Use existing stack pieces for scheduling, timezones, autosave and notifications","+## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher"," ","-**Context.** FR-28, NFR-10, FR-29, FR-38/39 and FR-12 all match existing infrastructure.","+**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6)."," ","-**Decision.**","-- Schedule picker: use the `DateTimePicker` from `@mui/x-date-pickers` (already wrapped in `src/components/FormField`). Convert school-timezone input to UTC with `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime(SchoolSettings.timezone)`. Zod rejects `publishAt <= now` (FR-28, NFR-10).","-- Autosave (FR-29): a `setInterval` of 10 s plus a dirty flag in the editor, a `beforeunload` listener, and `PATCH /api/lessons/:id`. No new library.","-- Notifications: add `content.lesson_published` to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` and call `notify()` only from the publish-now path (FR-38, FR-39).","-- Orphan purge (FR-12): call `purgeOrphanFiles()` next to `purgeOldNotifications()` inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` daily block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`.","-- Logging (NFR-12): use `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`. Rate limit (NFR-3): use the existing `rateLimit()`, which is per-process. That limitation is already marked with a ponytail comment.","+**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002."," ","-**Consequences.** No scheduler, queue or cron is added. Scheduled lessons appear automatically when read after `publishAt`, and no notification is sent for them, as FR-39 requires.","+**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher."," "," ---"," ","-## Open risks carried forward","-1. **NFR-7:** `mui-mcp` tools (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`) were visible in this session's tool list. Dev must still look up every MUI component against 9.5.0 before using it. If the server is unreachable, that is a hard blocker.","-2. **ADR-2:** depending on Next's transitive busboy is a small fragility (see the Consequences of ADR-2).","-3. **FR-40/42 (LOW confidence):** logo URLs stored as `/api/files/<id>` need an `APP_URL` prefix in email templates. The new `/admin/settings/school` page is a minimal page built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`.","+## Blockers carried forward","+","+1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.","+2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.","+3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.","+4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict (`moduleResolution: bundler`), Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5 beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers with `AdapterDateFns` already in `src/app/providers.tsx`, x-charts), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1, date-fns/date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `package.json` declares `engines.node >=18.18.0`, and local Node is 24.11.1. Nothing in the requirements calls for a different stack. The ADRs below cover how this feature fits into the existing stack and pin the new dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 limits new dependencies to file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable. The latest file-type (22.x) declares `engines.node >=22` and 21.x declares `>=20`. Either would break the repo's `>=18.18.0` engine contract. All five packages are ESM-only.\n\n**Decision.** Install these exact pins:\n| Package | Version | Why this version |\n|---|---|---|\n| `file-type` | `20.5.0` | Newest line with `engines.node >=18`. Use `fileTypeFromBuffer` (FR-5, FR-6). |\n| `react-markdown` | `10.1.0` | Peer is `react >=18` (FR-31). |\n| `remark-gfm` | `4.0.1` | Supports tables and strikethrough for FR-25 and FR-31. |\n| `rehype-sanitize` | `6.0.0` | Provides NFR-2 sanitisation. |\n| `@dnd-kit/sortable` | `10.0.0` | Peer is `@dnd-kit/core ^6.3.0`, which matches the installed 6.3.1 (FR-23). |\n\nESM-only packages import cleanly into App Router server and client code under `moduleResolution: bundler`, so `transpilePackages` is not needed. Add it only if `next build` complains.\n\n**Consequences.** No engine bump is needed. Do not upgrade file-type past 20.x without also raising `engines.node`. NFR-11 (single local-disk storage, no S3 SDK) means no cloud dependency is added.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Parse multipart uploads with `busboy` (already installed via Next.js), not `request.formData()`\n\n**Context.** NFR-5 requires uploads to stream to disk, with sha256 computed and the size limit enforced during the stream. In Next 14, `Request.formData()` buffers the whole body in memory, which violates NFR-5 for 25 MB files (FR-4). `busboy@1.6.0` is already in `node_modules` as a direct dependency of `next@14.2.18` (`npm ls busboy`). Adding another parser would break NFR-9.\n\n**Decision.** `POST /api/files` (FR-3) runs on the Node runtime (`export const runtime = 'nodejs'`). It pipes `Readable.fromWeb(req.body)` into `busboy({ headers, limits: { files: 1, fileSize: MAX_UPLOAD_MB*1024*1024 } })`. The file stream goes through a `crypto.createHash('sha256')` tap and into `storage.saveFile()` (FR-2), which writes to a temp path under `UPLOAD_DIR` and then `rename`s it to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>` (FR-1). Busboy's `limit` event aborts the upload, deletes the temp file and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'` (FR-4). Type sniffing (ADR-3) runs on the first chunk(s) before the write is committed. The `context` field must come before the file part in the multipart body because the logo rules (FR-40, FR-41) depend on it. FileUpload (FR-13) appends `context` first.\n\n**Consequences.** busboy is a transitive dependency, so `@types/busboy` is not available. Declare a minimal local type or accept `any` at that one call site, with a `ponytail:` comment explaining it. If a Next upgrade drops busboy, add `busboy` explicitly at that point. The intake handoff should note this as the only deviation from the dependency list, and it is a zero-install one. The rate limit check (NFR-3, `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` from `src/server/rate-limit.ts`) runs before any bytes are read.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Validate file types with an extension allowlist plus `file-type` sniffing of the head buffer, using an explicit table\n\n**Context.** FR-5 requires checks on both the extension and the magic number. FR-6 notes that txt/csv have no signature and that docx/xlsx/pptx can sniff as `zip`. FR-41 allows SVG only for `logo`, and SVG is text, so file-type cannot detect it reliably. The Vitest environment is `jsdom`, so file-type's `\"node\"` export condition may not resolve there, while `fileTypeFromBuffer` exists in both the node and core entries.\n\n**Decision.** In `src/server/files/validate.ts`, keep one `ALLOWED: Record<ext, { mimes: string[]; sniff: 'required' | 'none' | 'zip-or-ooxml' }>` table:\n- Binary types (pdf, doc, xls, ppt, png, jpg/jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4, zip): the sniffed mime must be in `mimes`. doc/xls/ppt sniff as `application/x-cfb`.\n- docx/xlsx/pptx: the sniffed type is `application/zip` or the matching OOXML mime.\n- txt/csv and svg (logo only): sniffing must return `undefined`. If any signature is detected (for example an ELF, PE or zip disguised as .csv), the file is rejected. SVG also requires the head to contain `<svg`, and is limited to 2 MB under context `logo` (FR-40). The logo context also limits extensions to png, jpg, jpeg, webp and svg.\n- The stored `mimeType` comes from the table, not from the client's Content-Type header.\n- Call `fileTypeFromBuffer(head)` on the first 4100 bytes collected from the stream. `head` is a tee of the first chunks, not a re-read.\n\n**Consequences.** The rules are deterministic and testable as a pure function (FR-48). Integration tests that touch busboy or the filesystem add `// @vitest-environment node`. Errors use the FR-5 message `File type .<ext> is not allowed.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Store files on local disk outside `public/`, serve them only through a Node route handler, and set headers per response\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 says files are never served from a static path. FR-8 sets nosniff, attachment and inline rules. FR-41 sets a CSP for SVG logos. FR-10 requires `logo` to be readable without a session. `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/` path that is not in `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (`src/config/public-routes.ts`). `next.config.js` already sends a site-wide `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a CSP of `default-src 'self'` on `/:path*`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/server/storage.ts` uses `node:fs/promises` and `node:stream/promises` only. `UPLOAD_DIR` is resolved with `path.resolve` and defaults to `./uploads`. Every storage key is checked to stay under `UPLOAD_DIR` after resolution, as a path-traversal guard. This is the only implementation (NFR-11).\n- `GET /api/files/:id` runs on `runtime = 'nodejs'` and returns `new Response(Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream(...)))` with `Content-Type` set to the stored mime, `Content-Length` set to `sizeBytes`, `nosniff`, and `Content-Disposition` set to `attachment` (or `inline` only for image/* or pdf with `?inline=1`) plus an RFC 5987 `filename*`. SVG responses also set `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. If next.config's global CSP is also sent, browsers enforce the stricter intersection, so no config change is needed for this route.\n- Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` so unauthenticated logo fetches reach the handler. The handler then runs the access registry (FR-9) for every request: `auth()` returns `null` for anonymous users, and only the `logo` resolver accepts a null user. Every other context returns 404 without reading bytes (NFR-8).\n- `.gitignore`: create one at the repo root containing `uploads/`, plus `node_modules`, `.next` and `.env` if missing. `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (NFR-12).\n\n**Consequences.** Opening the middleware gate moves the auth decision into the handler, so the access registry must deny by default (FR-9: an unknown context is owner/ADMIN only, and an anonymous user is denied). Integration tests must cover anonymous requests for a lesson file (expect 404) and for a logo (expect 200).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Allow the video-embed origins in the site CSP via `frame-src`\n\n**Context.** FR-30 embeds `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` and `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` iframes. The current CSP has `default-src 'self'` and no `frame-src`, so the browser would block both embeds.\n\n**Decision.** Add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com;` to the CSP string in `next.config.js`. The URL parser lives in `src/lib/video.ts` as a pure function shared by the Zod validator (FR-16) and the viewer (FR-32). It only emits those two origins.\n\n**Consequences.** This is a one-line config change. The `X-Frame-Options: DENY` header only stops other sites from framing SchoolHub, so it does not affect these embeds. Playwright should check that the iframe loads (it is not CSP-blocked) on the seeded YouTube lesson (FR-47).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Render Markdown with react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize, map every element to MUI, and restrict images to same origin\n\n**Context.** FR-31 and NFR-2 require sanitised Markdown with `img` allowed from same origin only and MUI element mapping (NFR-7). The current CSP has `img-src 'self' data:`.\n\n**Decision.** `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` is a client-safe component (no hooks, so it also renders on the server) with `remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}` and `rehypePlugins={[[rehypeSanitize, schema]]}`. `schema` extends `defaultSchema` and limits `img` `src` to relative paths: `protocols.src: []` plus a check that the value starts with `/`. The default schema already drops `javascript:` hrefs. A `components` map converts h1–h6, p, a, ul/ol/li, table/thead/tbody/tr/th/td, hr, blockquote, code and pre into MUI Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External `a` elements get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`. The editor Preview tab (FR-25) uses the same component.\n\n**Consequences.** One renderer is used everywhere, so a sanitisation regression shows up in one unit test with `<script>`, `javascript:` and off-origin `img` cases (FR-48). No CSP change is needed for images.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Implement reordering with @dnd-kit/sortable, persist the whole order in one transaction, and provide keyboard IconButtons\n\n**Context.** FR-23 covers drag within and across modules, with the full ordering sent to `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder`. NFR-6 requires a keyboard alternative. @dnd-kit/core is already installed.\n\n**Decision.** Each module's lesson List is a `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`, all inside one `DndContext`, and cross-container moves are handled in `onDragOver`. Up/down `IconButton`s modify the same client order array. The server validates that every submitted module and lesson id belongs to the course and that the set equals the existing set. It then writes `position`/`moduleId` for all rows inside one `prisma.$transaction`. A course has at most about 200 lessons (NFR-4), so updating every row is acceptable.\n\n**Consequences.** Reorder is a single idempotent call with no partial states. The update count is O(n) per reorder, which is fine at this scale.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Read content with a bounded number of Prisma queries and compute visibility in TypeScript\n\n**Context.** NFR-4 requires the Content tab to render 20×10 lessons in under 600 ms with no N+1 queries. FR-18 evaluates visibility at read time, with no background job.\n\n**Decision.** `GET /api/courses/:id/modules` and the Content tab server component call `content-service.listCourseContent(user, courseId)`. That function makes one `module.findMany` with `include: { lessons: { include: { _count: { select: { attachments: true } } } } }` ordered by position, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany` for the student's lessons in that course when the caller is a STUDENT. That is two queries in total. `isVisible(entity, now)` is a pure function in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` and is unit tested (FR-48). Both module and lesson must be visible. Add an `@@index([courseId, position])` on Module and an `@@index([moduleId, position])` on Lesson.\n\n**Consequences.** Visibility is not pushed into SQL. At 200 rows per course, filtering in memory costs nothing, and having the rule in one place means the viewer (FR-32), the Learning tab (FR-35) and FR-44 all agree.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Use existing stack pieces for scheduling, timezones, autosave and notifications\n\n**Context.** FR-28, NFR-10, FR-29, FR-38/39 and FR-12 all match existing infrastructure.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Schedule picker: use the `DateTimePicker` from `@mui/x-date-pickers` (already wrapped in `src/components/FormField`). Convert school-timezone input to UTC with `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime(SchoolSettings.timezone)`. Zod rejects `publishAt <= now` (FR-28, NFR-10).\n- Autosave (FR-29): a `setInterval` of 10 s plus a dirty flag in the editor, a `beforeunload` listener, and `PATCH /api/lessons/:id`. No new library.\n- Notifications: add `content.lesson_published` to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` and call `notify()` only from the publish-now path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Orphan purge (FR-12): call `purgeOrphanFiles()` next to `purgeOldNotifications()` inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` daily block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`.\n- Logging (NFR-12): use `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`. Rate limit (NFR-3): use the existing `rateLimit()`, which is per-process. That limitation is already marked with a ponytail comment.\n\n**Consequences.** No scheduler, queue or cron is added. Scheduled lessons appear automatically when read after `publishAt`, and no notification is sent for them, as FR-39 requires.\n\n---\n\n## Open risks carried forward\n1. **NFR-7:** `mui-mcp` tools (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`) were visible in this session's tool list. Dev must still look up every MUI component against 9.5.0 before using it. If the server is unreachable, that is a hard blocker.\n2. **ADR-2:** depending on Next's transitive busboy is a small fragility (see the Consequences of ADR-2).\n3. **FR-40/42 (LOW confidence):** logo URLs stored as `/api/files/<id>` need an `APP_URL` prefix in email templates. The new `/admin/settings/school` page is a minimal page built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014wFkAWGekx5rK6fc1sPsJ4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
