{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgroDX7hmxv9TKVPd8gXB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-9 as eight decisions. No new packages are added. Three of the intake blockers rest on fixes I couldn't test here, because this sub-task only writes the decisions file. The developer needs to apply and verify them.\n\nThere was an older `tech-stack-decisions.md` left from SH-8, and I replaced it, since this file belongs to this sub-task. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are also left over from earlier tickets (SH-7 and SH-8). I didn't touch them; the later architect sub-tasks will overwrite them.\n\n**The three environment fixes:**\n- **Data grid tables don't compile** (ADR-2): the data grid package accepts any version of a helper package from 9.1.0 up, and npm installed 9.15.0. No 9.5.0 of that helper exists on npm; it skips from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So the plan is to pin it to `9.1.0` through `overrides` in `package.json`. If it still won't compile, the teacher's assignments table falls back to a plain MUI `Table`.\n- **`npm test` doesn't start** (ADR-3): the test config's only problem is one import line (`vitest/config.js` should be `vitest/config`). The plan is to fix that line and delete the temporary copy of the config.\n- **The security policy blocks the page from loading its scripts in a real browser** (ADR-4): I left the production setting alone, since loosening it would weaken security and the proper fix affects every page. The end-to-end test for this ticket turns the policy off for itself (`bypassCSP`), as earlier test runs did. Until a separate ticket fixes the policy, manual checks in a real browser need the same workaround.\n\n**The other five decisions:**\n- **No new packages** (ADR-1): everything this feature needs is already installed.\n- **Missing upload and Markdown components** (ADR-5): SH-8 never built them, so this ticket builds four small shared ones (Markdown viewer and editor, file upload, file list) on top of SH-8's existing file backend.\n- **Late days** (ADR-6): computed from UTC time differences, so a clock change can't affect them. Exactly 24 hours late counts as 1 day.\n- **Scores** (ADR-7): calculated with exact decimal arithmetic, rounded half-up to 2 places. They travel through the API as text like `\"14.40\"`, not as numbers, which the API contracts step needs to follow.\n- **Reminders and \"published\" notifications** (ADR-8): no scheduler or background job. Database unique keys and conditional updates ensure each one is sent only once.\n\nStill open: the developer must reach mui-mcp before writing any UI, or that's a hard blocker. The Assignments tab on a student's page can't be seen yet, because nothing displays those tabs; that's for the design step. Every requirement ID cited in the file exists in `requirements.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5990,"cache_read_input_tokens":50996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5990},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78","uuid":"649ade33-097f-4b6e-a95b-e3fa4ba64095","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:25:14.671Z","request_id":"req_011CgroDWfv1ET6gaNgDrVuW"}
