{"duration_api_ms":88631,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a92ab962-fa62-4167-a62a-56c6a86ebe78","total_cost_usd":0.6073428000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":47031,"cache_read_input_tokens":260894,"output_tokens":8943,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":820},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":47031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1088,"cache_read_input_tokens":50996,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5990},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":8943,"cacheReadInputTokens":260894,"cacheCreationInputTokens":47031,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6073428000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":820,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":47031,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-9 as eight decisions. No new packages are added. Three of the intake blockers rest on fixes I couldn't test here, because this sub-task only writes the decisions file. The developer needs to apply and verify them.\n\nThere was an older `tech-stack-decisions.md` left from SH-8, and I replaced it, since this file belongs to this sub-task. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are also left over from earlier tickets (SH-7 and SH-8). I didn't touch them; the later architect sub-tasks will overwrite them.\n\n**The three environment fixes:**\n- **Data grid tables don't compile** (ADR-2): the data grid package accepts any version of a helper package from 9.1.0 up, and npm installed 9.15.0. No 9.5.0 of that helper exists on npm; it skips from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So the plan is to pin it to `9.1.0` through `overrides` in `package.json`. If it still won't compile, the teacher's assignments table falls back to a plain MUI `Table`.\n- **`npm test` doesn't start** (ADR-3): the test config's only problem is one import line (`vitest/config.js` should be `vitest/config`). The plan is to fix that line and delete the temporary copy of the config.\n- **The security policy blocks the page from loading its scripts in a real browser** (ADR-4): I left the production setting alone, since loosening it would weaken security and the proper fix affects every page. The end-to-end test for this ticket turns the policy off for itself (`bypassCSP`), as earlier test runs did. Until a separate ticket fixes the policy, manual checks in a real browser need the same workaround.\n\n**The other five decisions:**\n- **No new packages** (ADR-1): everything this feature needs is already installed.\n- **Missing upload and Markdown components** (ADR-5): SH-8 never built them, so this ticket builds four small shared ones (Markdown viewer and editor, file upload, file list) on top of SH-8's existing file backend.\n- **Late days** (ADR-6): computed from UTC time differences, so a clock change can't affect them. Exactly 24 hours late counts as 1 day.\n- **Scores** (ADR-7): calculated with exact decimal arithmetic, rounded half-up to 2 places. They travel through the API as text like `\"14.40\"`, not as numbers, which the API contracts step needs to follow.\n- **Reminders and \"published\" notifications** (ADR-8): no scheduler or background job. Database unique keys and conditional updates ensure each one is sent only once.\n\nStill open: the developer must reach mui-mcp before writing any UI, or that's a hard blocker. The Assignments tab on a student's page can't be seen yet, because nothing displays those tabs; that's for the design step. Every requirement ID cited in the file exists in `requirements.json`.","ttft_ms":3381,"type":"result","duration_ms":92685,"uuid":"57dcd963-ab55-4cfb-90e3-ff432efd196a","ttft_stream_ms":2134,"time_to_request_ms":173,"first_content_frame_ms":2134,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":8943,"cacheReadInputTokens":260894,"cacheCreationInputTokens":47031,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6073428000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":820,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":47031,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
