lableUntil (FR-13, FR-28).\n- `scoring.ts`: `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)` for HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE (FR-22).\n- `shuffle.ts`: a deterministic seeded shuffle with a small inline PRNG (mulberry32) seeded from a hash of the attempt id. No dependency (FR-13).\n- `quiz-service.ts` / `attempt-service.ts` do the Prisma I/O and call the pure functions.\n\n**Consequences.** The NFR-8 unit tests run in Vitest with no database. Regrade (FR-10) is just a loop over these functions. The shuffle stays reproducible for the life of an attempt.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: The server owns the deadline, and the autosave path stays one query\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 sets the autosave budget at under 50 ms for 300 concurrent students. FR-16 makes the server the authority on the deadline (30 s grace, 409 after it). FR-18 auto-submits lazily on load.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` reads only the QuizAttempt row (`studentId`, `status`, `deadlineAt`). It then does one `quizAnswer.upsert` on the composite key. If `now > deadlineAt + 30s`, it auto-submits and throws `AppError('CONFLICT')`; `src/server/http.ts` already maps CONFLICT to 409. It never loads the quiz or the questions on this path.\n- Lazy auto-submit runs in a shared `ensureNotExpired(attempt)` called by GET attempt, the player page and the teacher views. The maintenance run calls `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` (ADR-6).\n- The client timer derives its value from the `deadlineAt` the server returns. It never counts down from local start time.\n- Autosave client: one hook with an 800 ms debounce, a failed-save queue in localStorage keyed by attempt id, and a 5 s retry interval (FR-15). The localStorage pattern already exists in `attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` and `SubmissionPanel.tsx`.\n\n**Consequences.** Clock skew or a tampered client can't extend an attempt. The hot path stays at about 2 queries per save. No WebSockets or SSE are needed.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive\n\n**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components.\n\n**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner\n\n**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch.\n\n**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.\n- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change.\n\nNo BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server.\n\n**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: UI is MUI-only, and the mui-mcp lookup is a hard gate\n\n**Context.** NFR-4 bans non-MUI UI libraries, allows styling only via theme, `sx` and `styled()`, and requires every component to be looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs). An unreachable MCP is a blocker. NFR-3 requires native radio/checkbox inputs and `aria-live` timer announcements.\n\n**Decision.** Player: `RadioGroup`/`Radio`, `FormGroup`/`Checkbox`, `TextField` (multiline for essays, with a 10,000-character counter), `LinearProgress`, a navigator grid of `Button`s, and a sticky header built with `AppBar position=\"sticky\"` or `Box` + `sx`. Timer: a `Typography` with an `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region that announces only at 5 and 1 minutes and turns `error.main` under 2 minutes (FR-14, NFR-3). Status pill: `Chip`. Builder: `Accordion` or `Card` items in a dnd-kit `SortableContext`. Analytics: x-charts `BarChart` and `DataTable`. Dev must look up each component in mui-mcp before using it. If the MCP is unreachable, dev records a blocker and does not guess.\n\n**Consequences.** QA's banned-import and resolvable-MUI-import checks (NFR-4) pass by construction. Dev's first use of x-charts needs the docs lookup, because `src/` has no existing usage to copy.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Testing uses only the existing toolchain\n\n**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests, integration tests and one Playwright e2e, and `npm run lint && typecheck && test` must stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Unit tests in Vitest: grading.ts, deadline.ts, scoring.ts, shuffle.ts determinism, serializers (absence of the `correct` key) and `resultsVisible`.\n- Integration tests in Vitest against the test database, using the existing harness: autosave returns 409 after deadline + grace, auto-submit on load, regrade, and a concurrent start returning one attempt (ADR-2).\n- One e2e in Playwright: teacher builds a 4-question quiz, student takes it with a mid-attempt `page.reload()`, teacher grades the essay, student sees results.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling. The seed data (FR-36) gives the e2e and manual QA a ready-made state.\n\n---\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-10)\n\nNo lockdown browser, proctoring, question banks or LaTeX, so there is no evaluation of KaTeX/MathJax or media-capture libraries.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":113,"newStart":1,"newLines":128,"lines":["-# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions","+# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams"," ","-Ticket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:30:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.","+**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2."," ","-None of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.","+Intake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`). None of the NFRs pushes toward a different stack. NFR-2 (300 concurrent autosaves, <50 ms) is one indexed upsert per request, well within what Postgres handles. FR-15 calls this \"offline\", but it only means a localStorage retry queue, not offline-first sync. Nothing is realtime: the timer is display-only (FR-16). **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7).**"," "," ---"," "," ## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies"," ","-**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).","+**Context.** NFR-7 forbids new dependencies and re-scaffolding. NFR-4 allows only MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X for UI. Every capability PRD-10 needs is already installed or already in the repo."," "," **Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:","+"," | Need | Use | Req |"," |---|---|---|","-| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |","-| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |","-| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |","-| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |","-| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |","-| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |","+| Score maths | `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-3, FR-22, FR-25, NFR-7 |","+| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-2, NFR-6 |","+| Question reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable with MUI list items. Up/Down buttons are the keyboard fallback. | FR-7, NFR-3 |","+| Availability window inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-6 |","+| Score histogram | `@mui/x-charts` `BarChart` (first use in `src/`; look it up via mui-mcp) | FR-26, NFR-4 |","+| Attempts and grading tables | Existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid) | FR-11, FR-24, FR-27 |","+| Markdown prompts and images | Existing `MarkdownEditor`, `MarkdownView`, `FileUpload` | FR-39 |","+| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-27 |","+| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog`, `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-12, FR-17, NFR-7 |","+| Notifications and audit | `notify()` and `audit()` | FR-29, FR-30, FR-38 |","+| Debounce and retry | `setTimeout`/`setInterval` in one small client hook (no lodash) | FR-15 |"," ","-**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.","+**Consequences.** The lockfile doesn't change. Anything dev reaches for outside this table is a scope smell. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banned-library rule still guards NFR-4."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`","+## ADR-2: Data model in one Prisma migration, with a partial unique index in raw SQL"," ","-**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.","+**Context.** FR-1 adds 5 enums and 5 models. FR-19 requires at most one IN_PROGRESS attempt per (quiz, student), and `@@unique` can't express that because it is conditional on status. Intake's key-risks list calls out the race. The repo already has a precedent: `20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql` hand-adds `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... WHERE ...`, and `schema.prisma` notes this in a comment."," ","-**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.","+**Decision.**","+- Create a single migration (`prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then edit it), for example `20261110000000_add_quizzes`. Run it after `20261109000000_add_assignments`.","+- In `schema.prisma`, add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` on QuizAttempt and `@@id([attemptId, questionId])` (or `@@unique`) on QuizAnswer. The QuizAnswer key is what makes the NFR-2 upsert a single statement.","+- In the migration SQL, add `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\" ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';`. Add a schema comment pointing to it, as the attendance comment does.","+- Start-or-resume (FR-19, FR-23, FR-32) runs in a `prisma.$transaction`. On a P2002 unique violation, re-read and return the existing IN_PROGRESS attempt. No advisory locks.","+- Store all points and scores as `Decimal` columns. All timestamps are `timestamptz`/UTC (NFR-6)."," ","-**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.","+**Consequences.** The database enforces race safety, so two tabs both clicking Start get the same attempt. `prisma db push` would drop the partial index, so dev and CI must use `migrate`. That is already the norm."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config","+## ADR-3: Grading and deadline logic as pure functions in `src/server/quiz/`"," ","-**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).","+**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests for every grading rule, the deadline maths with accommodations, and the scoring policies. NFR-7 sets the `src/server/<feature>/` layout (PRD-05/09 precedent)."," ","-**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.","+**Decision.** Use plain TypeScript modules with no Prisma imports in the pure files:","+- `grading.ts`: `gradeAnswer(question, response)` for SINGLE/TRUE_FALSE all-or-nothing, MULTIPLE_CHOICE partial credit `points × max(0,(c−i)/totalCorrect)`, SHORT_ANSWER normalise and match (trim, collapse whitespace, optional case folding), and ESSAY returns `needsReview` (FR-3, FR-4, FR-5).","+- `deadline.ts`: `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)` returns min(start + limit + extra, availableUntil). An untimed quiz returns availableUntil (FR-13, FR-28).","+- `scoring.ts`: `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)` for HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE (FR-22).","+- `shuffle.ts`: a deterministic seeded shuffle with a small inline PRNG (mulberry32) seeded from a hash of the attempt id. No dependency (FR-13).","+- `quiz-service.ts` / `attempt-service.ts` do the Prisma I/O and call the pure functions."," ","-**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.","+**Consequences.** The NFR-8 unit tests run in Vitest with no database. Regrade (FR-10) is just a loop over these functions. The shuffle stays reproducible for the life of an attempt."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec","+## ADR-4: The server owns the deadline, and the autosave path stays one query"," ","-**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.","+**Context.** NFR-2 sets the autosave budget at under 50 ms for 300 concurrent students. FR-16 makes the server the authority on the deadline (30 s grace, 409 after it). FR-18 auto-submits lazily on load."," ","-**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.","+**Decision.**","+- `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` reads only the QuizAttempt row (`studentId`, `status`, `deadlineAt`). It then does one `quizAnswer.upsert` on the composite key. If `now > deadlineAt + 30s`, it auto-submits and throws `AppError('CONFLICT')`; `src/server/http.ts` already maps CONFLICT to 409. It never loads the quiz or the questions on this path.","+- Lazy auto-submit runs in a shared `ensureNotExpired(attempt)` called by GET attempt, the player page and the teacher views. The maintenance run calls `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` (ADR-6).","+- The client timer derives its value from the `deadlineAt` the server returns. It never counts down from local start time.","+- Autosave client: one hook with an 800 ms debounce, a failed-save queue in localStorage keyed by attempt id, and a 5 s retry interval (FR-15). The localStorage pattern already exists in `attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` and `SubmissionPanel.tsx`."," ","-**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.","+**Consequences.** Clock skew or a tampered client can't extend an attempt. The hot path stays at about 2 queries per save. No WebSockets or SSE are needed."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket","+## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive"," ","-**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.","+**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent."," ","-**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:","-- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).","-- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).","-- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.","-- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).","+**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components."," ","-Use the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.","+**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`."," ","-**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).","-"," ---"," ","-## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults","+## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner"," ","-**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.","+**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch."," ","-**Decision.**","-- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.","-- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.","-- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.","+**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:","+- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.","+- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change."," ","-**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.","+No BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server."," ","+**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.","+"," ---"," ","-## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only","+## ADR-7: UI is MUI-only, and the mui-mcp lookup is a hard gate"," ","-**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).","+**Context.** NFR-4 bans non-MUI UI libraries, allows styling only via theme, `sx` and `styled()`, and requires every component to be looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs). An unreachable MCP is a blocker. NFR-3 requires native radio/checkbox inputs and `aria-live` timer announcements."," ","-**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.","+**Decision.** Player: `RadioGroup`/`Radio`, `FormGroup`/`Checkbox`, `TextField` (multiline for essays, with a 10,000-character counter), `LinearProgress`, a navigator grid of `Button`s, and a sticky header built with `AppBar position=\"sticky\"` or `Box` + `sx`. Timer: a `Typography` with an `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region that announces only at 5 and 1 minutes and turns `error.main` under 2 minutes (FR-14, NFR-3). Status pill: `Chip`. Builder: `Accordion` or `Card` items in a dnd-kit `SortableContext`. Analytics: x-charts `BarChart` and `DataTable`. Dev must look up each component in mui-mcp before using it. If the MCP is unreachable, dev records a blocker and does not guess."," ","-**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.","+**Consequences.** QA's banned-import and resolvable-MUI-import checks (NFR-4) pass by construction. Dev's first use of x-charts needs the docs lookup, because `src/` has no existing usage to copy."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher","+## ADR-8: Testing uses only the existing toolchain"," ","-**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).","+**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests, integration tests and one Playwright e2e, and `npm run lint && typecheck && test` must stay green."," ","-**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.","+**Decision.**","+- Unit tests in Vitest: grading.ts, deadline.ts, scoring.ts, shuffle.ts determinism, serializers (absence of the `correct` key) and `resultsVisible`.","+- Integration tests in Vitest against the test database, using the existing harness: autosave returns 409 after deadline + grace, auto-submit on load, regrade, and a concurrent start returning one attempt (ADR-2).","+- One e2e in Playwright: teacher builds a 4-question quiz, student takes it with a mid-attempt `page.reload()`, teacher grades the essay, student sees results."," ","-**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.","+**Consequences.** No new test tooling. The seed data (FR-36) gives the e2e and manual QA a ready-made state."," "," ---"," ","-## Blockers carried forward","+## Out of scope (NFR-10)"," ","-1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.","-2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.","-3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.","-4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.","+No lockdown browser, proctoring, question banks or LaTeX, so there is no evaluation of KaTeX/MathJax or media-capture libraries."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n\nNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n\n**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n\n**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n\n**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n\n**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n\n**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n\n**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n\n**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n\n**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n\n**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n\n**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n\nUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n\n**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n\n**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n\n**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n\n**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n\n---\n\n## Blockers carried forward\n\n1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DFASE6AjXm6PFPfPTjSS84","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
