{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrveDGBZ6fRthfu9sFYs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-10 with status complete. It cites 42 requirement IDs, and a script confirmed every one exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**Overall decision:** keep the current stack and add no new dependencies (NFR-7). Every need maps to something the repo already has, such as the score-maths helpers in `grading-math.ts`, @dnd-kit, the MUI chart and grid components, `csv.ts`, `notify()` and `audit()`. No requirement pushes toward a different stack: the autosave load target (NFR-2) is one database write per save, and the \"offline\" behaviour in FR-15 is just a local retry queue.\n\nThe 8 decisions:\n1. **No new dependencies:** a table maps each need to an existing package or helper.\n2. **Database migration:** one new Prisma migration. A hand-written database index guarantees one in-progress attempt per student per quiz, as in the attendance migration. If two tabs start at once, both get the same attempt.\n3. **Grading code:** grading, deadline, scoring-policy and seeded-shuffle logic go in plain functions under `src/server/quiz/`, so they can be unit-tested without a database.\n4. **Deadline and autosave:** the server owns the deadline. Each autosave is one attempt read plus one write, and returns 409 after the 30-second grace. Expired attempts are auto-submitted when someone loads them.\n5. **Hiding answers from students:** a dedicated student serializer builds responses from an explicit list of allowed fields. One function decides when results become visible.\n6. **Background work:** auto-submit and the \"results released\" notification hook into the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no job runner. The design sub-task (`arch-design-system`) still has to choose how to stop the notification sending twice; a `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz is the smaller option.\n7. **UI:** MUI only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, and timer announcements for screen readers.\n8. **Testing:** Vitest and Playwright only, with no new test tooling.\n\nThe other files in `artifacts/architect/` are left over from SH-9 (Assignments): `system-design.md`, `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, `requirements-analysis-notes.md` and `threat-model-notes.json`. I didn't touch them because they belong to other sub-tasks. The SH-10 runs of `arch-research-reqs`, `arch-design-system` and `arch-api-contracts` will overwrite them. Until then, the existing handoff file wrongly signals that the architect phase is complete. `threat-model-notes.json` isn't owned by any sub-task, so nothing will replace it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":49024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":339,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"552f551a-a5ab-4968-b0db-a75ac04487f5","uuid":"91352904-47cf-474c-a341-cd537276948a","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:02:35.096Z","request_id":"req_011CgrveCazQj1h5EFdnQ6HX"}
