{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsKbfJBaoJAHJ5PkUeA6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JQ1hiHjcnDy5nmvb79AA5c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\nTicket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:\n\n- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.\n- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.\n- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.\n\nNone of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |\n| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |\n| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |\n| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |\n| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |\n| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |\n| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |\n| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |\n| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |\n| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |\n| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |\n\n**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.\n- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.\n- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).\n- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary.\n\n**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod\n\n**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own.\n\n**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop.\n\n**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\".\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper\n\n**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.\n- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).\n- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.\n- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk.\n\n**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\").\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue\n\n**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope.\n\n**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.\n- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).\n- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).\n- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers\n\n**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`.\n\n**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync\n\n**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test.\n\n**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41).\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row\n\n**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.\n- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:\n  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students\n  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses\n  - the scale\n  - one attendance groupBy for the term range\n- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.\n- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`.\n\n**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library\n\n**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.\n\n**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone\n\n**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.\n\n**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":201,"cache_read_input_tokens":47012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":201},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dab3c9a-3324-41d5-b3b7-e3df4e586ca3","uuid":"5320a572-4166-4398-ac84-2f7ec0833a75","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:04:17.254Z","request_id":"req_011CgsKbdp8jZqoSXNdko5mu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JQ1hiHjcnDy5nmvb79AA5c":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\nTicket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:\n\n- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.\n- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.\n- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.\n\nNone of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |\n| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |\n| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |\n| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |\n| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |\n| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |\n| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |\n| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |\n| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |\n| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |\n| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |\n\n**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.\n- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.\n- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).\n- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary.\n\n**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod\n\n**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own.\n\n**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop.\n\n**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\".\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper\n\n**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.\n- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).\n- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.\n- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk.\n\n**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\").\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue\n\n**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope.\n\n**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.\n- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).\n- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).\n- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers\n\n**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`.\n\n**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync\n\n**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test.\n\n**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41).\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row\n\n**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.\n- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:\n  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students\n  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses\n  - the scale\n  - one attendance groupBy for the term range\n- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.\n- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`.\n\n**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library\n\n**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.\n\n**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone\n\n**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.\n\n**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JQ1hiHjcnDy5nmvb79AA5c","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dab3c9a-3324-41d5-b3b7-e3df4e586ca3","uuid":"52fd21cf-58b0-44ab-b919-09c1b071ee7d","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:04:17.351Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\nTicket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:\n\n- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.\n- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.\n- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.\n\nNone of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |\n| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |\n| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |\n| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |\n| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |\n| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |\n| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |\n| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |\n| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |\n| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |\n| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |\n\n**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.\n- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.\n- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).\n- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary.\n\n**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod\n\n**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own.\n\n**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop.\n\n**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\".\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper\n\n**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.\n- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).\n- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.\n- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk.\n\n**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\").\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue\n\n**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope.\n\n**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.\n- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).\n- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).\n- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers\n\n**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`.\n\n**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync\n\n**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test.\n\n**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41).\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row\n\n**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.\n- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:\n  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students\n  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses\n  - the scale\n  - one attendance groupBy for the term range\n- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.\n- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`.\n\n**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library\n\n**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.\n\n**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone\n\n**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.\n\n**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":128,"newStart":1,"newLines":150,"lines":["-# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams","+# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards"," ","-Ticket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:30:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.","+**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2."," ","-Intake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`). None of the NFRs pushes toward a different stack. NFR-2 (300 concurrent autosaves, <50 ms) is one indexed upsert per request, well within what Postgres handles. FR-15 calls this \"offline\", but it only means a localStorage retry queue, not offline-first sync. Nothing is realtime: the timer is display-only (FR-16). **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7).**","+Intake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:"," ","+- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.","+- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.","+- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.","+","+None of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**","+"," ---"," ","-## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies","+## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies"," ","-**Context.** NFR-7 forbids new dependencies and re-scaffolding. NFR-4 allows only MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X for UI. Every capability PRD-10 needs is already installed or already in the repo.","+**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo."," ","-**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:","+**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:"," "," | Need | Use | Req |"," |---|---|---|","-| Score maths | `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-3, FR-22, FR-25, NFR-7 |","-| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-2, NFR-6 |","-| Question reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable with MUI list items. Up/Down buttons are the keyboard fallback. | FR-7, NFR-3 |","-| Availability window inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-6 |","-| Score histogram | `@mui/x-charts` `BarChart` (first use in `src/`; look it up via mui-mcp) | FR-26, NFR-4 |","-| Attempts and grading tables | Existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid) | FR-11, FR-24, FR-27 |","-| Markdown prompts and images | Existing `MarkdownEditor`, `MarkdownView`, `FileUpload` | FR-39 |","-| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-27 |","-| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog`, `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-12, FR-17, NFR-7 |","-| Notifications and audit | `notify()` and `audit()` | FR-29, FR-30, FR-38 |","-| Debounce and retry | `setTimeout`/`setInterval` in one small client hook (no lodash) | FR-15 |","+| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |","+| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |","+| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |","+| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |","+| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |","+| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |","+| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |","+| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |","+| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |","+| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |","+| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |","+| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |","+| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |","+| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |","+| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |"," ","-**Consequences.** The lockfile doesn't change. Anything dev reaches for outside this table is a scope smell. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banned-library rule still guards NFR-4.","+**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7)."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-2: Data model in one Prisma migration, with a partial unique index in raw SQL","+## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions"," ","-**Context.** FR-1 adds 5 enums and 5 models. FR-19 requires at most one IN_PROGRESS attempt per (quiz, student), and `@@unique` can't express that because it is conditional on status. Intake's key-risks list calls out the race. The repo already has a precedent: `20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql` hand-adds `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... WHERE ...`, and `schema.prisma` notes this in a comment.","+**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly."," "," **Decision.**","-- Create a single migration (`prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then edit it), for example `20261110000000_add_quizzes`. Run it after `20261109000000_add_assignments`.","-- In `schema.prisma`, add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` on QuizAttempt and `@@id([attemptId, questionId])` (or `@@unique`) on QuizAnswer. The QuizAnswer key is what makes the NFR-2 upsert a single statement.","-- In the migration SQL, add `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\" ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';`. Add a schema comment pointing to it, as the attendance comment does.","-- Start-or-resume (FR-19, FR-23, FR-32) runs in a `prisma.$transaction`. On a P2002 unique violation, re-read and return the existing IN_PROGRESS attempt. No advisory locks.","-- Store all points and scores as `Decimal` columns. All timestamps are `timestamptz`/UTC (NFR-6).","+- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.","+- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.","+- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).","+- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary."," ","-**Consequences.** The database enforces race safety, so two tabs both clicking Start get the same attempt. `prisma db push` would drop the partial index, so dev and CI must use `migrate`. That is already the norm.","+**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-3: Grading and deadline logic as pure functions in `src/server/quiz/`","+## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod"," ","-**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests for every grading rule, the deadline maths with accommodations, and the scoring policies. NFR-7 sets the `src/server/<feature>/` layout (PRD-05/09 precedent).","+**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own."," ","-**Decision.** Use plain TypeScript modules with no Prisma imports in the pure files:","-- `grading.ts`: `gradeAnswer(question, response)` for SINGLE/TRUE_FALSE all-or-nothing, MULTIPLE_CHOICE partial credit `points × max(0,(c−i)/totalCorrect)`, SHORT_ANSWER normalise and match (trim, collapse whitespace, optional case folding), and ESSAY returns `needsReview` (FR-3, FR-4, FR-5).","-- `deadline.ts`: `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)` returns min(start + limit + extra, availableUntil). An untimed quiz returns availableUntil (FR-13, FR-28).","-- `scoring.ts`: `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)` for HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE (FR-22).","-- `shuffle.ts`: a deterministic seeded shuffle with a small inline PRNG (mulberry32) seeded from a hash of the attempt id. No dependency (FR-13).","-- `quiz-service.ts` / `attempt-service.ts` do the Prisma I/O and call the pure functions.","+**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop."," ","-**Consequences.** The NFR-8 unit tests run in Vitest with no database. Regrade (FR-10) is just a loop over these functions. The shuffle stays reproducible for the life of an attempt.","+**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\"."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-4: The server owns the deadline, and the autosave path stays one query","+## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper"," ","-**Context.** NFR-2 sets the autosave budget at under 50 ms for 300 concurrent students. FR-16 makes the server the authority on the deadline (30 s grace, 409 after it). FR-18 auto-submits lazily on load.","+**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing."," "," **Decision.**","-- `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` reads only the QuizAttempt row (`studentId`, `status`, `deadlineAt`). It then does one `quizAnswer.upsert` on the composite key. If `now > deadlineAt + 30s`, it auto-submits and throws `AppError('CONFLICT')`; `src/server/http.ts` already maps CONFLICT to 409. It never loads the quiz or the questions on this path.","-- Lazy auto-submit runs in a shared `ensureNotExpired(attempt)` called by GET attempt, the player page and the teacher views. The maintenance run calls `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` (ADR-6).","-- The client timer derives its value from the `deadlineAt` the server returns. It never counts down from local start time.","-- Autosave client: one hook with an 800 ms debounce, a failed-save queue in localStorage keyed by attempt id, and a 5 s retry interval (FR-15). The localStorage pattern already exists in `attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` and `SubmissionPanel.tsx`.","+- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.","+- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).","+- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.","+- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk."," ","-**Consequences.** Clock skew or a tampered client can't extend an attempt. The hot path stays at about 2 queries per save. No WebSockets or SSE are needed.","+**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\")."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive","+## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue"," ","-**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent.","+**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope."," ","-**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components.","+**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.","+- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).","+- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).","+- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3)."," ","-**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`.","+**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner","+## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers"," ","-**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch.","+**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`."," ","-**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:","-- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.","-- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change.","+**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`."," ","-No BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server.","+**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event."," ","-**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.","-"," ---"," ","-## ADR-7: UI is MUI-only, and the mui-mcp lookup is a hard gate","+## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync"," ","-**Context.** NFR-4 bans non-MUI UI libraries, allows styling only via theme, `sx` and `styled()`, and requires every component to be looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs). An unreachable MCP is a blocker. NFR-3 requires native radio/checkbox inputs and `aria-live` timer announcements.","+**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test."," ","-**Decision.** Player: `RadioGroup`/`Radio`, `FormGroup`/`Checkbox`, `TextField` (multiline for essays, with a 10,000-character counter), `LinearProgress`, a navigator grid of `Button`s, and a sticky header built with `AppBar position=\"sticky\"` or `Box` + `sx`. Timer: a `Typography` with an `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region that announces only at 5 and 1 minutes and turns `error.main` under 2 minutes (FR-14, NFR-3). Status pill: `Chip`. Builder: `Accordion` or `Card` items in a dnd-kit `SortableContext`. Analytics: x-charts `BarChart` and `DataTable`. Dev must look up each component in mui-mcp before using it. If the MCP is unreachable, dev records a blocker and does not guess.","+**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41)."," ","-**Consequences.** QA's banned-import and resolvable-MUI-import checks (NFR-4) pass by construction. Dev's first use of x-charts needs the docs lookup, because `src/` has no existing usage to copy.","+**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion."," "," ---"," ","-## ADR-8: Testing uses only the existing toolchain","+## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row"," ","-**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests, integration tests and one Playwright e2e, and `npm run lint && typecheck && test` must stay green.","+**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s."," "," **Decision.**","-- Unit tests in Vitest: grading.ts, deadline.ts, scoring.ts, shuffle.ts determinism, serializers (absence of the `correct` key) and `resultsVisible`.","-- Integration tests in Vitest against the test database, using the existing harness: autosave returns 409 after deadline + grace, auto-submit on load, regrade, and a concurrent start returning one attempt (ADR-2).","-- One e2e in Playwright: teacher builds a 4-question quiz, student takes it with a mid-attempt `page.reload()`, teacher grades the essay, student sees results.","+- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.","+- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:","+  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students","+  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses","+  - the scale","+  - one attendance groupBy for the term range","+- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.","+- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`."," ","-**Consequences.** No new test tooling. The seed data (FR-36) gives the e2e and manual QA a ready-made state.","+**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it."," "," ---"," ","-## Out of scope (NFR-10)","+## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library"," ","-No lockdown browser, proctoring, question banks or LaTeX, so there is no evaluation of KaTeX/MathJax or media-capture libraries.","+**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.","+","+**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.","+","+**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.","+","+---","+","+## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone","+","+**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.","+","+**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.","+","+**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added."]}],"originalFile":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams\n\nTicket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`). None of the NFRs pushes toward a different stack. NFR-2 (300 concurrent autosaves, <50 ms) is one indexed upsert per request, well within what Postgres handles. FR-15 calls this \"offline\", but it only means a localStorage retry queue, not offline-first sync. Nothing is realtime: the timer is display-only (FR-16). **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-7 forbids new dependencies and re-scaffolding. NFR-4 allows only MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X for UI. Every capability PRD-10 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-3, FR-22, FR-25, NFR-7 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-2, NFR-6 |\n| Question reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable with MUI list items. Up/Down buttons are the keyboard fallback. | FR-7, NFR-3 |\n| Availability window inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-6 |\n| Score histogram | `@mui/x-charts` `BarChart` (first use in `src/`; look it up via mui-mcp) | FR-26, NFR-4 |\n| Attempts and grading tables | Existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid) | FR-11, FR-24, FR-27 |\n| Markdown prompts and images | Existing `MarkdownEditor`, `MarkdownView`, `FileUpload` | FR-39 |\n| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-27 |\n| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog`, `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-12, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n| Notifications and audit | `notify()` and `audit()` | FR-29, FR-30, FR-38 |\n| Debounce and retry | `setTimeout`/`setInterval` in one small client hook (no lodash) | FR-15 |\n\n**Consequences.** The lockfile doesn't change. Anything dev reaches for outside this table is a scope smell. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banned-library rule still guards NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Data model in one Prisma migration, with a partial unique index in raw SQL\n\n**Context.** FR-1 adds 5 enums and 5 models. FR-19 requires at most one IN_PROGRESS attempt per (quiz, student), and `@@unique` can't express that because it is conditional on status. Intake's key-risks list calls out the race. The repo already has a precedent: `20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql` hand-adds `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... WHERE ...`, and `schema.prisma` notes this in a comment.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Create a single migration (`prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then edit it), for example `20261110000000_add_quizzes`. Run it after `20261109000000_add_assignments`.\n- In `schema.prisma`, add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` on QuizAttempt and `@@id([attemptId, questionId])` (or `@@unique`) on QuizAnswer. The QuizAnswer key is what makes the NFR-2 upsert a single statement.\n- In the migration SQL, add `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\" ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';`. Add a schema comment pointing to it, as the attendance comment does.\n- Start-or-resume (FR-19, FR-23, FR-32) runs in a `prisma.$transaction`. On a P2002 unique violation, re-read and return the existing IN_PROGRESS attempt. No advisory locks.\n- Store all points and scores as `Decimal` columns. All timestamps are `timestamptz`/UTC (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** The database enforces race safety, so two tabs both clicking Start get the same attempt. `prisma db push` would drop the partial index, so dev and CI must use `migrate`. That is already the norm.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Grading and deadline logic as pure functions in `src/server/quiz/`\n\n**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests for every grading rule, the deadline maths with accommodations, and the scoring policies. NFR-7 sets the `src/server/<feature>/` layout (PRD-05/09 precedent).\n\n**Decision.** Use plain TypeScript modules with no Prisma imports in the pure files:\n- `grading.ts`: `gradeAnswer(question, response)` for SINGLE/TRUE_FALSE all-or-nothing, MULTIPLE_CHOICE partial credit `points × max(0,(c−i)/totalCorrect)`, SHORT_ANSWER normalise and match (trim, collapse whitespace, optional case folding), and ESSAY returns `needsReview` (FR-3, FR-4, FR-5).\n- `deadline.ts`: `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)` returns min(start + limit + extra, availableUntil). An untimed quiz returns availableUntil (FR-13, FR-28).\n- `scoring.ts`: `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)` for HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE (FR-22).\n- `shuffle.ts`: a deterministic seeded shuffle with a small inline PRNG (mulberry32) seeded from a hash of the attempt id. No dependency (FR-13).\n- `quiz-service.ts` / `attempt-service.ts` do the Prisma I/O and call the pure functions.\n\n**Consequences.** The NFR-8 unit tests run in Vitest with no database. Regrade (FR-10) is just a loop over these functions. The shuffle stays reproducible for the life of an attempt.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: The server owns the deadline, and the autosave path stays one query\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 sets the autosave budget at under 50 ms for 300 concurrent students. FR-16 makes the server the authority on the deadline (30 s grace, 409 after it). FR-18 auto-submits lazily on load.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` reads only the QuizAttempt row (`studentId`, `status`, `deadlineAt`). It then does one `quizAnswer.upsert` on the composite key. If `now > deadlineAt + 30s`, it auto-submits and throws `AppError('CONFLICT')`; `src/server/http.ts` already maps CONFLICT to 409. It never loads the quiz or the questions on this path.\n- Lazy auto-submit runs in a shared `ensureNotExpired(attempt)` called by GET attempt, the player page and the teacher views. The maintenance run calls `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` (ADR-6).\n- The client timer derives its value from the `deadlineAt` the server returns. It never counts down from local start time.\n- Autosave client: one hook with an 800 ms debounce, a failed-save queue in localStorage keyed by attempt id, and a 5 s retry interval (FR-15). The localStorage pattern already exists in `attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` and `SubmissionPanel.tsx`.\n\n**Consequences.** Clock skew or a tampered client can't extend an attempt. The hot path stays at about 2 queries per save. No WebSockets or SSE are needed.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive\n\n**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components.\n\n**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner\n\n**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch.\n\n**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.\n- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change.\n\nNo BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server.\n\n**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: UI is MUI-only, and the mui-mcp lookup is a hard gate\n\n**Context.** NFR-4 bans non-MUI UI libraries, allows styling only via theme, `sx` and `styled()`, and requires every component to be looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs). An unreachable MCP is a blocker. NFR-3 requires native radio/checkbox inputs and `aria-live` timer announcements.\n\n**Decision.** Player: `RadioGroup`/`Radio`, `FormGroup`/`Checkbox`, `TextField` (multiline for essays, with a 10,000-character counter), `LinearProgress`, a navigator grid of `Button`s, and a sticky header built with `AppBar position=\"sticky\"` or `Box` + `sx`. Timer: a `Typography` with an `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region that announces only at 5 and 1 minutes and turns `error.main` under 2 minutes (FR-14, NFR-3). Status pill: `Chip`. Builder: `Accordion` or `Card` items in a dnd-kit `SortableContext`. Analytics: x-charts `BarChart` and `DataTable`. Dev must look up each component in mui-mcp before using it. If the MCP is unreachable, dev records a blocker and does not guess.\n\n**Consequences.** QA's banned-import and resolvable-MUI-import checks (NFR-4) pass by construction. Dev's first use of x-charts needs the docs lookup, because `src/` has no existing usage to copy.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Testing uses only the existing toolchain\n\n**Context.** NFR-8 requires unit tests, integration tests and one Playwright e2e, and `npm run lint && typecheck && test` must stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Unit tests in Vitest: grading.ts, deadline.ts, scoring.ts, shuffle.ts determinism, serializers (absence of the `correct` key) and `resultsVisible`.\n- Integration tests in Vitest against the test database, using the existing harness: autosave returns 409 after deadline + grace, auto-submit on load, regrade, and a concurrent start returning one attempt (ADR-2).\n- One e2e in Playwright: teacher builds a 4-question quiz, student takes it with a mid-attempt `page.reload()`, teacher grades the essay, student sees results.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling. The seed data (FR-36) gives the e2e and manual QA a ready-made state.\n\n---\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-10)\n\nNo lockdown browser, proctoring, question banks or LaTeX, so there is no evaluation of KaTeX/MathJax or media-capture libraries.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JQ1hiHjcnDy5nmvb79AA5c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
