{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsKfJsyP2eQaUu9RGCmx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-11. The file there before was left over from SH-10 (quizzes), so I replaced it.\n\n**Decision: keep the current stack (Next.js 14, Prisma on PostgreSQL, MUI 9.5.0) and add no new packages.** Nothing in the performance, printing or calculation requirements needs a cache, a job queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. Each need maps to code already in the repo. The only change to `package.json` is one new script line, `gradebook:backfill`.\n\nThe document has 10 decision records:\n1. **No new packages.** Each need is mapped to an existing helper or component.\n2. **Exact decimal grades.** Scores use Prisma's `Decimal` type and a pure calculation file, `grade-calc.ts`, which rounds half-up once at the end.\n3. **Grading-scale bands stored as JSON** and validated as a set. A partial unique index enforces a single default scale.\n4. **Gradebook grid uses MUI's free `DataGrid` directly**, not the existing table wrapper, which can't do column groups or cell editing. Grid props should be checked against the 9.5.0 docs before use.\n5. **Grades sync through direct calls** in the existing assignment, quiz and submission code, inside their transactions. There's no event bus or queue.\n6. **New `getStudentQuizScore` helper** built from the existing quiz scoring functions. The PRD names it but it doesn't exist yet.\n7. **Backfill is a `tsx` script** that reuses the sync functions. It's safe to run twice, and the seed calls it.\n8. **Report cards are frozen as a JSON snapshot.** Regeneration only touches DRAFT cards, and data is loaded in batches to meet the 30-second target.\n9. **Printing uses CSS print rules and `window.print()`**, with no PDF library.\n10. **Dates:** \"past due\" is checked against the exact due time. Term placement uses the school's local date, through the same helper attendance uses.\n\nEvery requirement id I cite exists in `requirements.json`.\n\nTwo things for the later sub-tasks:\n- **Stale files.** The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, `threat-model-notes.json`) still carry `ticketId` SH-10. They belong to the other sub-tasks, so I didn't touch them; they need to be regenerated for SH-11.\n- **Quiz scores can arrive late.** For quizzes whose results appear after close or on manual release, sync has to run again at that point. Dev-planning should hook the release action, or those scores won't show in the gradebook until the next backfill or attempt."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5576,"cache_read_input_tokens":47213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5576},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dab3c9a-3324-41d5-b3b7-e3df4e586ca3","uuid":"91ba5567-cff1-41e7-aa7b-bd1b0b61616f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:04:26.728Z","request_id":"req_011CgsKfJNDRrkzvYR58wLXV"}
