{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsfvXPo3FJqaYK8jFi72","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` for SH-12. It contains 7 ADRs (architecture decision records), each with Context, Decision and Consequences, and every one cites FR/NFR ids that exist in `requirements.json`. Nothing was run or tested; this step only writes the decisions file.\n\n- **ADR-1:** Keep the current stack (Next.js 14, Prisma, MUI 9.5) and add no dependencies. Every need maps to code or packages already in the repo.\n- **ADR-2:** Audience membership is checked with database joins rather than by loading every recipient. One shared rules module in `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` feeds the recipient list, the single-user check and the feed filter, so they can't disagree. It isn't tied to announcements, so calendar events (PRD-14) can reuse it. The ADR also lists the indexes needed to meet the 200 ms feed target.\n- **ADR-3:** A scheduled announcement becomes visible when its publish time passes, with no cron needed. `publishDueAnnouncements()` runs inside the existing maintenance route at `/api/internal/email/dispatch`. It marks `notifiedAt` atomically, so each announcement notifies exactly once even if two runs overlap.\n- **ADR-4:** I settled the open reminder question. A new nullable `Announcement.lastRemindedAt` column stores the last send, and a second reminder within 24 hours returns 429 RATE_LIMITED rather than 409 CONFLICT. This column is the only change to the data model intake specified.\n- **ADR-5:** A small regex helper turns Markdown into plain text for the 200-character feed excerpt and the 300-character email text. It can leave stray characters on unusual Markdown, which only affects how excerpts look. If that becomes a problem, swap in the `remark` and `strip-markdown` packages.\n- **ADR-6:** The sidebar unread badge comes from a new optional `badgeEndpoint` field on `NavItem`, polled the same way `NotificationBell` already does.\n- **ADR-7:** All teacher targeting rules sit in one function, `assertCanTarget`, called from both create and edit. Users outside the audience get 404 rather than 403, so they can't tell the announcement exists; `requirements.json` allows either, so `arch-design-system` can change this. Anonymous file access is allowed only for public announcements that are currently visible.\n\nThe `artifacts/architect/` folder still holds the other SH-11 files: `system-design.md`, `api-contracts.json`, the handoff file, `requirements-analysis-notes.md` and `threat-model-notes.json`. I left them alone because the later sub-tasks own them and will overwrite them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":360,"cache_read_input_tokens":49137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":360,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdd2c86a-7f10-4a3f-8735-81ad1382f632","uuid":"480c24c3-d4a4-42f5-8436-7782ee855e1a","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:30:10.051Z","request_id":"req_011CgsfvX99s9czpdNSVYCyz"}
